{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6","id":1266310,"title":"RWBY Volume 6","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-10T18:38:29-08:00","id":1266310,"title":"RWBY Volume 6","content":"Discussions and theories about this volume","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12378-fma245","name":"FMA245","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T18:46:26-08:00","id":1266313,"title":"","content":"It's okay so far, Volume 5 was actively <b>bad</b> and it seems like they listened to some of the criticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T20:43:47-08:00","id":1266336,"title":"","content":"I'm sick of hearing complaints to be honest. RWBY never got as bad as the internet complaints said it did<br /> <br /> As for 6, fast start, ep 2 (I'm not paying, so am a week behind) slowed down a bit, but am intrigued by what comes next<br /> <br /> and why did they bring her back? was that necessary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T22:47:11-08:00","id":1266348,"title":"","content":"Holy shit, this Volume is like... actively good! It's like we're back in the grand old days of Volume 3 again! The fight in the first episode is EASILY top five in the series, maybe top three; it doesn't have a ton of dramatic weight behind it, which is literally the only thing holding it back. The best choreographed thing they've done since moving to Maya, and demonstrating that that engine has real power behind it if they actually know how to use it.<br /> <br /> Pacing is working well; Volume 5 managed the near trick of simultaneously being the longest volume and the one where the least happened. So far six hasn't had a single wasted moment, but doesn't feel rushed. (So far.)<br /> <br /> I stand by my prior claim that the Gods of Remnant are a pair of evil motherfuckers. I mean... just grotesquely bad beings.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T02:10:21-08:00","id":1266366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266336#post1266336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sick of hearing complaints to be honest. RWBY never got as bad as the internet complaints said it did</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree strongly. I don't want to rehash old arguments though, so I am looking forward to watching and discussing season 6.<br /> <br /> Edit 1: Episode one was amazing. Great animation, great cinematography, FANTASTIC fight scenes, which were of uniform animation quality, design, action, and showed off each character's unique abilities. Just by the language of motion we could see the Ruby/Weiss bond, the Blake/Yang new relationship, and that Qrow taught Ruby how to use a scythe. Absolutely top notch stuff. And I loved the Manticore Grimm. I have zero complaints.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Episode 2 was also great. Everyone had enough of Oz's cryptic bullshit and finally called him out on it, and his reluctance to be open and forthrite with the people <i>tasked with saving the world</i> has come back to bite him in the ass. This is exactly the payoff I was hoping for, drama and consequences arising from character actions. I'm very excited to see where this goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 11-11-2018, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T06:38:36-08:00","id":1266394,"title":"","content":"HAHAHA... Oh, <i>Salem</i>. Spoilers for Episode 3!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So she was Perfect Soul this whole dang time? <b>Hilarious</b>! *threads fingers* I'm no fan of the Jiaran Bruce Almighty, but I can get behind her as a villain easily enough<br /> <br /> Honestly though, I'm a liiitle conflicted here. I'm not too big a fan of some of the tropes in Salem's backstory, love the basic <i>principle </i>of her challenging the gods, but 'it was all for love' is... uuugh. And having her Crossing The Line moment in the new world be related to Oz and the kids doesn't help. *taps* I'm interested to see her take on things, her philosophy, what she's trying to accomplish and the like. I feel this is a reasonable background, with the potential to make her an excellent villain, just feel we need a little more on where she's at right now.<br /> <br /> Also, am I the only one wondering why Oz has kept all this so damn secret? I mean... he doesn't trust people, and sharing the God of Creation's mission with Salem was what led to them parting ways, but.... IDK, I feel like we're still in the dark on something with him too. Ruby asking 'what is he hiding' rather than 'why is Oz keeping secrets' may come back to bite the party.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T09:40:19-08:00","id":1266432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266394#post1266394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HAHAHA... Oh, <i>Salem</i>. Spoilers for Episode 3!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So she was Perfect Soul this whole dang time? <b>Hilarious</b>! *threads fingers* I'm no fan of the Jiaran Bruce Almighty, but I can get behind her as a villain easily enough<br /> <br /> Honestly though, I'm a liiitle conflicted here. I'm not too big a fan of some of the tropes in Salem's backstory, love the basic <i>principle </i>of her challenging the gods, but 'it was all for love' is... uuugh. And having her Crossing The Line moment in the new world be related to Oz and the kids doesn't help. *taps* I'm interested to see her take on things, her philosophy, what she's trying to accomplish and the like. I feel this is a reasonable background, with the potential to make her an excellent villain, just feel we need a little more on where she's at right now.<br /> <br /> Also, am I the only one wondering why Oz has kept all this so damn secret? I mean... he doesn't trust people, and sharing the God of Creation's mission with Salem was what led to them parting ways, but.... IDK, I feel like we're still in the dark on something with him too. Ruby asking 'what is he hiding' rather than 'why is Oz keeping secrets' may come back to bite the party.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Discussing episode 3 spoilers<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I don't really feel like Salem's original challenge was for love. That struck me as far more of trying to destroy them because she felt they were assholes and had no right to the power they had. Remember her objection to the light brother saying he wouldn't bring back the dead because it goes against the natural order and rules was to call him out on not being fair. Probably not helped by the time she had to ponder afterwords that Ozma had freaked out when he was brought back from the dead the first time, followed by doing it all again in under five minutes ostensibly because darkness was miffed at his brother for destroying a gift to ,what he thought was, his worshipper and then annoyed at her for lying about going to him second. That they were clearly fallible meant she probably felt she was more deserving of the title of god than they were.<br /> <br /> Not that I don't think getting her love back was part of the objective, just that it was probably more of a fringe benefit by the time she makes the challenge.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T10:55:28-08:00","id":1266451,"title":"","content":"They made a mistake in Volume 5 with the three character shorts leaving them without time and resources for more important fights. So this time, they kept it down to one short.<br /> <br /> I liked Volume 5, but Volume 6 seems to be Rooster Teeth hitting a whole new stride.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T12:06:20-08:00","id":1266468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266394#post1266394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HAHAHA... Oh, <i>Salem</i>. Spoilers for Episode 3!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So she was Perfect Soul this whole dang time? <b>Hilarious</b>! *threads fingers* I'm no fan of the Jiaran Bruce Almighty, but I can get behind her as a villain easily enough<br /> <br /> Honestly though, I'm a liiitle conflicted here. I'm not too big a fan of some of the tropes in Salem's backstory, love the basic <i>principle </i>of her challenging the gods, but 'it was all for love' is... uuugh. And having her Crossing The Line moment in the new world be related to Oz and the kids doesn't help. *taps* I'm interested to see her take on things, her philosophy, what she's trying to accomplish and the like. I feel this is a reasonable background, with the potential to make her an excellent villain, just feel we need a little more on where she's at right now.<br /> <br /> Also, am I the only one wondering why Oz has kept all this so damn secret? I mean... he doesn't trust people, and sharing the God of Creation's mission with Salem was what led to them parting ways, but.... IDK, I feel like we're still in the dark on something with him too. Ruby asking 'what is he hiding' rather than 'why is Oz keeping secrets' may come back to bite the party.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'm pretty sure the bit at the very end where Oz asks Djinn how to beat Salem and she says its impossible is why he hid this. The two people we know betrayed him did so because they believed Salem was unbeatable and apparently they were at least partially right.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1904-heraklitas","name":"Heraklitas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T13:51:07-08:00","id":1266490,"title":"","content":"Salem never once cared about &quot;Other People&quot;.<br /> <br /> She definitely loved Ozma, but she was otherwise extremely self-centered.<br /> <br /> The Light God tries to explain why all humanity needs to accept death; Salem doesn't care about what other people have to suffer. She wants to be the exception.<br /> <br /> The Light God tries to explain that Ozma is resting. She doesn't care.<br /> <br /> (When the Light God later offered Ozma the chance to walk the world again, Ozma preferred to stay in the afterlife and find Salem, before he was told she wasn't among the new arrivals and never would be. So the afterlife is not oblivion or unpleasant or lonely, and bringing him back just rips him away from all of that. This explains why, given that Ozma died peacefully the first time, he reacting so badly to being resurrected the first time. Also, the Light God made sure that Ozma wouldn't go back to his rest only to be repeatedly ripped away from it, but ensured that he would always go straight to the next person whom would help him and give him company on his long, long quest.)<br /> <br /> The Light God breaking his rules might provoke his brother to break their agreement entirely, when that agreement is the only reason the Dark God hasn't destroyed everything? She doesn't care.<br /> <br /> Lying to the Dark God, risking a cosmic battle between him and his brother, and giving him a whole new reason to hate created beings such that he might break his agreement? She doesn't care.<br /> <br /> Tricking three whole nations of people into attempting to kill their gods, regardless of the actual possible consequences, and without caring how many of them would die or whether it was even possible for them to get what she promised them? Possibly finally provoking the Dark God to break the agreement and destroy everything? She doesn't care.<br /> <br /> She just watched them all die with a Thanos finger-snap? She doesn't care, she'll just go get more and throw away as many armies as it takes until the gods give her what she wants.<br /> <br /> The next three things we can only partially blame on her dip in the Pool of Annihilation and the desire for destruction that it gave her.<br /> <br /> Ozma wants to unite the world? Okay, so she resorts to invasion and killing to conquer the entire planet.<br /> <br /> Their kids have divine magic? Okay, time to replace the new humanity with their children.<br /> <br /> Ozma tries to take the kids away? Okay, time to murder their kids and then him.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for her actions BEFORE her dip in the black pool, some people have blamed her father's horrible parenting for her inability to think beyond herself. While that's definitely a consideration, ultimately Salem has to be held responsible for her own choices, and she was manipulating, dividing, and leading people to their deaths long before her black bath.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":".  removed spoiler tags now that episode is out 11-17-2018, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T15:01:30-08:00","id":1266500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266451#post1266451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They made a mistake in Volume 5 with the three character shorts leaving them without time and resources for more important fights .</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't sound right, Sunder. Of those three character shorts, Blake's was clearly itself under-resourced (that wasn't a &quot;fight&quot; and the shit they did with the wagon was frankly embarrassing) and Yang's was BARELY a fight. Weiss's was pretty great, but that was what, five minutes long?<br /> <br /> If those character shorts didn't exist V5 wouldn't have had that much better fights, because the resources put into said shorts didn't amount to much. At BEST, it could have either salvaged the fight in Blake's house, or one-quarter of the &quot;fight&quot; at Haven.<br /> <br /> Whereas this year, we had the Adam short, which was quality action end-to-end, which they then followed up with MORE quality action.<br /> <br /> V5 was definitely under-resourced, but the character shorts can't be blamed for it, I don't think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T16:40:44-08:00","id":1266532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266500#post1266500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the resources put into said shorts didn't amount to much.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ursa, both environments, and the new model for Winter were all totally new assets not used again in Volume 5.<br /> <br /> The effort taken to make those assets could instead have been put into doing more with the assets made for the Haven fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T16:42:28-08:00","id":1266533,"title":"","content":"Maybe its just me, I'd say volume 5's issue was that it didn't feel like its own thing. Like volume 5 felt rather generic to me, and that was a bit of a problem in volume 4 as well just not as extreme, where I feel that 6 seems to be going well so far is that it feels like things to its own world. I'll need time and more to see where it goes, but volume 6 feels more like a story that is tied to its own setting than volume 5 felt to me. I mean at the risk of a minor spoiler we might actually get a proper explanation on why magic was met with skepticism as a thing that existed when we have Semblences in this setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T17:00:17-08:00","id":1266538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heraklitas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266468#post1266468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'm pretty sure the bit at the very end where Oz asks Djinn how to beat Salem and she says its impossible is why he hid this. The two people we know betrayed him did so because they believed Salem was unbeatable and apparently they were at least partially right.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yep, gotta be careful in how you phrase a question or a request to a Genie.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThe very existence of flame-throwers proves that some time, somewhere, someone said to themselves, You know, I want to set those people over there on fire, but I'm just not close enough to get the job done.\u201d George Carlin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/123-trax","name":"Trax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar123_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T21:14:15-08:00","id":1266606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heraklitas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266468#post1266468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the bit at the very end where Oz asks Djinn how to beat Salem and she says its impossible is why he hid this. The two people we know betrayed him did so because they believed Salem was unbeatable and apparently they were at least partially right.</div> </div> </div> </div>He asked for a way to destroy her, not beat her. Even if she's impossible to kill, it might be possible to imprison her.<br /> <br /> For example, within one of the Vaults.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266538#post1266538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, gotta be careful in how you phrase a question or a request to a Genie.</div> </div> </div> </div>In case you didn't notice, Jinn goes far behind answering the bare minimum of a question. She takes you on a full-blown VISION QUEST to show you EXACTLY what happened in the past, with your own eyes, and she even narrates to tell you what your eyes can't see.<br /> <br /> She isn't designed to be a literal genie or a jackass genie. Her entire purpose is to give people knowledge, and she seems to go all-out in order to do so. She takes pride in it.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, a perfectly acceptable answer to &quot;How do I destroy Salem?&quot; would be &quot;Convince this person to do it for you&quot;, if any such person existed.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that Salem and her minions have dealt with Silver-Eyed Warriors before, and Salem actually wanted Ruby brought back to her ALIVE, without stipulating her eyes be gouged out. So Salem isn't afraid that Ruby's Eye Blasts can hurt her.<br /> <br /> The gods themselves cursed Salem to be immortal, and if even the Relic of Destruction and the Pools of Annihilation weren't the answer to Ozma's question, then NOTHING short of the gods themselves COULD BE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":".  removed spoiler tags now that episode is out 11-17-2018, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T21:46:14-08:00","id":1266608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266606#post1266606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">He asked for a way to destroy her, not beat her. Even if she's impossible to kill, it might be possible to imprison her.<br /> <br /> For example, within one of the Vaults.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In case you didn't notice, Jinn goes far behind answering the bare minimum of a question. She takes you on a full-blown VISION QUEST to show you EXACTLY what happened in the past, with your own eyes, and she even narrates to tell you what your eyes can't see.<br /> <br /> She isn't designed to be a literal genie or a jackass genie. Her entire purpose is to give people knowledge, and she seems to go all-out in order to do so. She takes pride in it.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, a perfectly acceptable answer to &quot;How do I destroy Salem?&quot; would be &quot;Convince this person to do it for you&quot;, if any such person existed.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that Salem and her minions have dealt with Silver-Eyed Warriors before, and Salem actually wanted Ruby brought back to her ALIVE, without stipulating her eyes be gouged out. So Salem isn't afraid that Ruby's Eye Blasts can hurt her.<br /> <br /> The gods themselves cursed Salem to be immortal, and if even the Relic of Destruction and the Pools of Annihilation weren't the answer to Ozma's question, then NOTHING short of the gods themselves COULD BE.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Just piggy backing the comment here for continuity of discussion.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> On the Jinn topic, I doubt Jinn will try to screw a person over since that feels kind of counter to the point of the relics. (Presuming the relics are meant to be both tool of aid and trial for people to actually get the frack along.) Especially considering the limitation of only 3 questions every hundred years deal. While I doubt she would be as benevolent as walking a person through coming up with the proper question to ask to get the results they want (I believe she was stated to be all knowing provided the desired information was not regarding future events.) it would be fair to assume that she's not designed to give bare minimum answers in an attempt to screw the user over. <br /> <br /> That said the limitations and the question are important to consider since those will influence the information given. I mean I doubt that if they had asked why Ozpin was still hiding a lot of information about the relics, Salem, and who knows what; we probably would not have gotten the in depth explanation on everything and hell the information given might have just been, &quot;Oh he knew Salem has about as perfect a form of immortality as you're going to get, and that when he asked me ages back how to destroy her I told him he couldn't. And he figures that'll just crush your moral into paste if not cause you to defect to Salem's side altogether.&quot; Which would have been problematic and lost useful information. Like that bringing the relics together causes judgment day. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T01:26:23-08:00","id":1266638,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else want to slum it with me and discuss episode 1 or 2? I'm sure Ep 3 has <i>TONS</i> of bombshells but i'm not a paid up member so i'm a week behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T08:12:34-08:00","id":1266700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266638#post1266638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else want to slum it with me and discuss episode 1 or 2? I'm sure Ep 3 has <i>TONS</i> of bombshells but i'm not a paid up member so i'm a week behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit, what about Jaune's Semblance, y'all. Boosting other people's Semblances. Right now, any application has to be stationary, but the options are still staggering.<br /> <br /> Imagine him boosting Weiss so that she can conjure an even BIGGER summoned creature, or multiple summons and copies of summons. Or super-charge her Dust-casting.<br /> <br /> Imagine him boosting GLYNDA.<br /> <br /> Weep that we will never see him boost Pyrrha.<br /> <br /> Pray that he never boosts Qrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T10:03:10-08:00","id":1266725,"title":"","content":"I have to wonder what boosting some semblances would even do.<br /> <br /> Like Raven's. Bigger portals, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T10:09:22-08:00","id":1266728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266700#post1266700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit, what about Jaune's Semblance, y'all. Boosting other people's Semblances. Right now, any application has to be stationary, but the options are still staggering.<br /> <br /> Imagine him boosting Weiss so that she can conjure an even BIGGER summoned creature, or multiple summons and copies of summons. Or super-charge her Dust-casting.<br /> <br /> Imagine him boosting GLYNDA.<br /> <br /> Weep that we will never see him boost Pyrrha.<br /> <br /> Pray that he never boosts Qrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh shucks, is that officially his semblance now? I thought they went out of their way last season to explain it wasn\u2019t and he was just straight up sharing energy like how Phyrra did to him in the early episodes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T10:31:16-08:00","id":1266733,"title":"","content":"He can share energy. That means he can heal people, boost semblances and probably supercharge a maiden if he got his hands on one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T10:44:52-08:00","id":1266736,"title":"","content":"So the relics passively draw Grimm, at least according to Ozpin, so does anyone else think that means that had the relics not been put into vaults you'd have massive Grimm nests or hives centered on them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T11:26:24-08:00","id":1266743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266728#post1266728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh shucks, is that officially his semblance now? I thought they went out of their way last season to explain it wasn\u2019t and he was just straight up sharing energy like how Phyrra did to him in the early episodes.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266733#post1266733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He can share energy. That means he can heal people, boost semblances and probably supercharge a maiden if he got his hands on one.</div> </div> </div> </div>He outright states he wasn't giving Weiss his energy.<br /> <br /> Let me repost my Tumblr article:<br /> <br /> <b><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><a href=\"https://sunder-the-gold.tumblr.com/post/171321357603/jaune-arc-amplifier\" target=\"_blank\">Jaune Arc \u2013 Amplifier</a></span></b></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Jaune\u2019s Semblance is the power to magnify the basic abilities of Aura, whether his own or that of others.<br /> <br /> By amplifying his own Aura, he can rapidly accelerate the speed and comprehensiveness of his healing, heighten its protection to the point that striking him injures his <i>attacker</i>\u2026 and it might even be responsible for his various feats of brute strength.<br /> <br /> Essentially, Jaune has the option to spend more Aura than his peers in order to enjoy proportionate returns. Fortunately, he apparently has a larger supply of soul-energy than those peers, which keeps him from running into endurance issues.<br /> <br /> But perhaps more impressive is Jaune\u2019s ability to bestow this amplification unto others.<br /> <br /> Weiss Schnee once received a cut across her face which, even with Aura left for protection at the time, did not heal well enough to avoid a scar which endures years later. Yet under the effects of Jaune\u2019s Semblance, Weiss\u2019 Aura seems to have completely reversed all of the damage inflicted by a flaming spear through her liver after her Aura had broken. Her skin is unmarred, and she returned to the fight with enough power to summon a Lancer Queen.<br /> <br /> For now, Jaune requires \u201cI\u2019m not touching you\u201d levels of close proximity and several uninterrupted minutes to perform such miracles. In the future, he might be able to empower battle-ready allies while he fights alongside them, amplifying their powers in combat.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i><i><i><i><i><a href=\"http://sunder-the-gold.tumblr.com/post/157992976064/jaune-arc-character-sub-index\" target=\"_blank\">back to my sub-index for Jaune Arc</a></i></i></i></i></i> </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i><a href=\"http://sunder-the-gold.tumblr.com/post/150568126304/semblance-index\" target=\"_blank\">back to my Semblance index</a></i> </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T11:37:08-08:00","id":1266746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266736#post1266736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the relics passively draw Grimm, at least according to Ozpin, so does anyone else think that means that had the relics not been put into vaults you'd have massive Grimm nests or hives centered on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider that Oscar was wearing the Relic on his hip and has TWO human souls to draw Grimm attention, but there was never more than one Grimm attacking him at a time, and never was it the Sphinx.<br /> <br /> Consider that we know for a fact that Grimm attack trains all of the time. The WOR on the CCT Towers illustrates this as the greatest reason why relying on trains for communication is problematic, and the first train we ever saw was loaded with robot Knights and the giant Spider-Tank with its Fuck Off Laser. A laser that would have been a reasonable answer to something like the Sphinx.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind also that the conspirators were talking about how Grimm were getting worse even before Beacon fell, and after Beacon fell, hunters all over the world died against the sudden global surge of Grimm attacks, leaving fewer hunters to deal with increasingly bad Grimm activity. A vicious cycle.<br /> <br /> Given that all wilderness is effectively Grimm territory, the fact that Dee and Duddely (Tweedle Dee and Dum) thought it noteworthy to say the train would be passing through &quot;Grimm territory&quot; implies to me that Mistral had detected unusually high numbers of Grimm in that area.<br /> <br /> So when Ozpin says the Relic's attractive is &quot;faint&quot;, I'm fully inclined to believe its not any more attractive than a single human being, so taking it aboard a train is no worse than adding another passenger.<br /> <br /> The only thing worse would be letting people imagine that the Relic is more attractive than it is, which leads to more anxiety, which leads to more Grimm encounters, which leads to confirmation bias and worse imaginations and worse anxiety, which leads to more Grimm attacks, in a vicious cycle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T15:23:29-08:00","id":1266799,"title":"","content":"Thoughts about the divine curse:<br /> <br /> Who cursed Salem to live forever? The God of Light; the sympathetic, non-dickish brother.<br /> <br /> Why? Why did he think Salem was that important? Why doesn't he remove the curse? What is unique about Salem?<br /> <br /> Realization: She was the first person to go to the God of Darkness and ask for something, or at least something that people would normally go to his brother to get. Or maybe she was just the first to lie to him.<br /> <br /> One way or another, Salem is uniquely important to the Dark God. She seems to have gained his attention in the way that no other human did before. He actually did something for her to be nice, even if it was motivated by his own vanity.<br /> <br /> In short, Salem represents a turning point for the Dark God.<br /> <br /> Which god moved first to attack her when she was about to attack them at the pools of annihilation? The God of Light. He stopped her from provoking his brother, who would have killed her or worse. He saved her life from his brother, and then he went even further to protect her life from his brother and his destructive creations and anything else.<br /> <br /> WHY?<br /> <br /> Remember what the ENTIRE POINT of this story is. This entire story is the God of Light trying to change his brother's perspective. To change his mind and get him to like created things so that he'll stop destroying everything.<br /> <br /> Salem became an opportunity that the Light God COULD NOT ALLOW to vanish.<br /> <br /> If Salem can learn the lessons that the God of Light has been trying to impart to his brother, his brother who is watching her might finally change his own mind too. He might also accept the value of mortal life and the weight of mortal death. He might also stop thinking only of himself, as Salem does, and consider how his actions hurt other people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":".  removed spoiler tags now that episode is out 11-17-2018, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T18:51:58-08:00","id":1266833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266700#post1266700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit, what about Jaune's Semblance, y'all. Boosting other people's Semblances. Right now, any application has to be stationary, but the options are still staggering.<br /> <br /> Imagine him boosting Weiss so that she can conjure an even BIGGER summoned creature, or multiple summons and copies of summons. Or super-charge her Dust-casting.<br /> <br /> Imagine him boosting GLYNDA.<br /> <br /> Weep that we will never see him boost Pyrrha.<br /> <br /> Pray that he never boosts Qrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that it could work this way in all cases.<br /> <br /> Jaune can both amplify people and top them off. (We don't yet know if he can apply that power to himself; your tumblr article is presumptuous on that score.) But that might not provide all people with a highly <i>usable</i> boost.<br /> <br /> Take Raven. Raven can create portals to people she is bonded to. Jaune's boost might allow her to make bigger or multiple portals... but if her Semblance is explicitly limited in scope to &quot;one at a time, of this size&quot; then his turbocharge might not help her much beyond letting her keep them open longer or giving her a bigger shield. Which, to be fair, isn't to be trifled with.<br /> <br /> In the same vein, he could presumably make Ruby go faster (an explicit part of her Semblance) but probably not give her the ability to straight-up teleport (a power she does not have and thus cannot be amplified.)<br /> <br /> Weiss is interesting because... we know the Schnee Semblance can &quot;downshift.&quot; You can get smaller, less awesome summons, presumably at-will. (Or Winter has killed a bunch of really really tiny Nevermores.) If it can upshift under Amplification, that's super super cheaty, because usually the way their Semblance works is if you want to summon something especially titanic or deadly, you first must defeat that thing, which of course is quite hard. But if Jaune can upshift Weiss, she might be able to call forth a summons that could give the Wyvern a run for its money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T20:21:01-08:00","id":1266851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266833#post1266833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jaune can... top them off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I can't stop you from not believing what Jaune himself said. But it would be nice if you would at least admit you're doing that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We don't yet know if he can apply that power to himself; your tumblr article is presumptuous on that score. </div> </div> </div>Then you don't remember Volume 1, where immediately after Pyrrha does that awakening ritual, Jaune instantly heals the cut on his check,<br /> <br /> Cardin tries to punch Jaune in the face, and there's a blinding flash. After which, Jaune's bruise is healed and Cardin's punching fist is injured.<br /> <br /> Less clear are Jaune's feats of brute strength. Parrying the claw of the giant Deathstalker without getting knocked flat on his ass, despite lacking the training which allowed Pyrrha do the same (possibly with assistance from her Polarity Semblance behind her shield). Beheading in one stroke the Ursa Major that Cardin couldn't defeat. Checking the charge of the Nuckelavee -- a feat that Nora, whose Semblance is electrical super-strength -- called impressive.<br /> <br /> All of those strength feats could be Jaune using his amplification Semblance to double-boost his strength without realizing it, just like he healed himself and super-soaked Cardin's punch without meaning to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the same vein, he could presumably make Ruby go faster </div> </div> </div>Only for an initial burst, unless she carries him with her the way she's done for Penny, Nora, and Weiss.<br /> <br /> I don't know why you bother digressing into &quot;giving people abilities they don't have&quot; though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it can upshift under Amplification, that's super super cheaty </div> </div> </div>As cheaty as allowing Ren to mask an entire train full of people instead of just two. Someone did a count -- at least 71 people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T21:05:36-08:00","id":1266856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266851#post1266851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I can't stop you from not believing what Jaune himself said. But it would be nice if you would at least admit you're doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way am I doing this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then you don't remember Volume 1, where immediately after Pyrrha does that awakening ritual, Jaune instantly heals the cut on his check, </div> </div> </div>And Pyrrha doesn't think that's at all remarkable (she finds his AMOUNT of Aura remarkable, not the same thing) implying that this is within the standard range of Aura-related healing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cardin tries to punch Jaune in the face, and there's a blinding flash. After which, Jaune's bruise is healed and Cardin's punching fist is injured. </div> </div> </div>Which, again, nobody finds remarkable, which implies it is within the standard range of Aura-related goings on.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Less clear are Jaune's feats of brute strength. Parrying the claw of the giant Deathstalker without getting knocked flat on his ass, despite lacking the training which allowed Pyrrha do the same (possibly with assistance from her Polarity Semblance behind her shield). Beheading in one stroke the Ursa Major that Cardin couldn't defeat. Checking the charge of the Nuckelavee -- a feat that Nora, whose Semblance is electrical super-strength -- called impressive. </div> </div> </div><i>Everybody</i> in this show demonstrates super-strength when the fight calls for it, though.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of those strength feats could be Jaune using his amplification Semblance to double-boost his strength without realizing it, just like he healed himself and super-soaked Cardin's punch without meaning to. </div> </div> </div>They COULD be, yes. You present it as a fact, rather than as a possibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know why you bother digressing into &quot;giving people abilities they don't have&quot; though. </div> </div> </div>Well, in the context of a discussion of what Jaune's Semblance can and cannot do, that would seem to be relevant. What constitutes &quot;Amplification?&quot; What are the hypothetical limits here?<br /> <br /> Ren's Semblance, for example, can explicitly be extended to others in its standard form. So it makes sense that Jaune amping him can allow him to extend it to MANY MANY others. But what if his Semblance could only affect himself in its standard form? Would Amplification simply make him better at that, or would it let him extend it further? Where's the border between &quot;boosted version of what you have&quot; and &quot;entirely new power?&quot; CAN Jaune's Semblance give people what is effectively an entirely new power?<br /> <br /> One hopes the team has been experimenting with this. Nora comes to mind. Nora is theoretically capable of GENERATING electricity, not just absorbing it, although we rarely see this. (I'm not sure we've EVER seen her generate, actually.) Could Jaune enable her to go the full Electro, just start hurling bolts of lightning left and right? Or would that be pushing it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As cheaty as allowing Ren to mask an entire train full of people instead of just two. Someone did a count -- at least 71 people. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was pretty crazy. I mean... hell, if the Relic hadn't been there, Ren might have been able to just do his thing with Jaune, and the Grimm would probably have milled around aimlessly and then left. Jaune + Ren represent an extraordinarily powerful combo from the perspective of keeping large numbers of people alive. It's SUPER cheaty, especially from the perspective of the Grimm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":4742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","user":"Murcushio","date":". 11-13-2018, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T21:15:46-08:00","id":1266857,"title":"","content":"Anyone else think young Salem should have had silver eyes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T00:30:13-08:00","id":1266893,"title":"","content":"Re: Jaune; I see what I did. When he said \u201cno, I\u2019m not healing her\u201d I stupidly thought he was saying, no that\u2019s not my semblance I\u2019m just doing this thing - rather than, oh yeah that is my semblance but no I\u2019m not healing her I\u2019m doing something different. Apologies. <br /> <br /> Re show in general; I\u2019m super glad they decided to do a big ball of exposition to start of this volume, I was a hair\u2019s breadth <br /> from canceling my subscription. <br /> <br /> Re ep3;<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I\u2019m wondering if Djinn didn\u2019t mention the conditional nature of Salem\u2019s immortality to Oz because; 1) <i>he</i> is still incapable of fulfilling the condition that would take it away (but possibley someone else well known for plucky speeches about hope could manage it) or, 2) Salem in her new form is now incapable of the introspection require to fulfil that condition. <br /> <br /> Admittedly I\u2019d be a little disappointed if it was just that it was left out because \u201cyou can\u2019t\u201d sounds cooler, though I understand that part of the story was in brief.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T10:54:51-08:00","id":1267007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1266856#post1266856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what way am I doing this?</div> </div> </div> </div>How can Jaune &quot;top them off&quot; if he's not giving them his energy? As I've already said in this thread, he tells us himself that he's not giving anyone his Aura.<br /> <br /> We've seen what happens when you try to put foreign Aura into someone else. Pyrrha screamed in agony.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Pyrrha doesn't think that's at all remarkable </div> </div> </div>She smirks when she sees the cut heal.<br /> <br /> Speaking of cuts, you remember the one Weiss received in the White Trailer? The one that became a scar.<br /> <br /> Jaune has no scar, and thanks to him, neither does Weiss' stomach. You can look right through the hole in her dress and see unblemished skin. Weiss is healed up so well that RUBY is the one who collapses after the battle is over; Weiss isn't even wincing or holding her side.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They COULD be, yes. You present it as a fact, rather than as a possibility. </div> </div> </div>I do NOT, in fact. I NEVER present the strength feats as factual applications of his Semblance. Always as possible ones.<br /> <br /> As facts, I present the proven healing, and the defensive flash of which we've never seen the like again. The animators made Cardin's injured hand very obvious.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nora is theoretically capable of GENERATING electricity, not just absorbing it, although we rarely see this. (I'm not sure we've EVER seen her generate, actually.) </div> </div> </div>The only time seems to be when she's charging up for the final blow that breaks the Petra Gigas' body. They call it an upgrade like she's put some container of Lightning Dust in her hammer's head, but she's never used it since. It seems more like a technique where she used her Semblance to electrify her weapon to inflict greater damage, and she hasn't used it since because it didn't prove effective.<br /> <br /> Nora might be juicing her muscles a tiny bit for an extra edge of speed and strength, but it seems that using external sources of electricity is more cost-effective than making her own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T11:18:41-08:00","id":1267022,"title":"","content":"So yeah, Episode 3 had a veritable gold mine of huge reveals. But in my opinion none are more shocking than:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Okay one... Salem's plumbing still works countless years later, after being cursed, and after a dip in the Tar Pits of the Dark Brother.<br /> <br /> Two: Ozpin fucked that. At LEAST four times.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T11:26:56-08:00","id":1267026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1267022#post1267022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah, Episode 3 had a veritable gold mine of huge reveals. But in my opinion none are more shocking than:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Okay one... Salem's plumbing still works countless years later, after being cursed, and after a dip in the Tar Pits of the Dark Brother.<br /> <br /> Two: Ozpin fucked that. At LEAST four times.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Salem still being biologically human and fully functional does have interesting possible implications. Though humanity was partly the Dark Brother's work too, so I'm not super surprised the plumbing still works. <br /> <br /> Oz enthusiastically banging Salem in that state... Well, really, her appearance back then is basically 'sexy vampire' so I can totally understand. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T12:49:21-08:00","id":1267058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1267007#post1267007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can Jaune &quot;top them off&quot; if he's not giving them his energy?</div> </div> </div> </div>A big part of Jaune's Semblance seems to be that he can apply it to people who are completely depleted, or presumably not completely depleted but running low, and they'll both heal up and shoot back to being brimming with Aura very, very quickly.<br /> <br /> What's that if not &quot;topping them off?&quot; Presumably, Nora could shout out during a fight &quot;Jaune! I'm low!&quot; and he could run over to her and apply his Semblance to... top her off.<br /> <br /> Indeed, this could quite possibly be a strong strategy; Nora is the bruiser of Team JN_R, who both doesn't fight from a distance/use quick strikes (Ren) or have a defensive option (Jaune.) She goes in with a huge two-hander that requires her to commit to her strikes and often takes a bruising in return. She's taken real bad hits a lot and is probably the member of the team who could benefit most from simply a pure Aura boost when it comes to staying power, before you even get into it helping her Semblance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She smirks when she sees the cut heal. </div> </div> </div>Which means little in this context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do NOT, in fact. I NEVER present the strength feats as factual applications of his Semblance. Always as possible ones. </div> </div> </div>I was referring to this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Jaune\u2019s Semblance is the power to magnify the basic abilities of Aura, <b>whether his own</b> or that of others.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>We don't have NEARLY enough information for that to be presented confidently as a fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nora might be juicing her muscles a tiny bit for an extra edge of speed and strength, but it seems that using external sources of electricity is more cost-effective than making her own. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, precisely. It makes me wonder just what she could do with Jaune behind her, because Nora Valkyrie is already terrifyingly potent. If she could be amped in a way that lets her shoot lightning or level buildings with a single hammer blow... hoo boy.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"