,"user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T19:59:09-08:00","id":1267489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1267323#post1267323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird hypothesis with basically no evidence that occurred to me regarding a thing in episode 3.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Anyone else wondering if dust is a side-effect brought on by the whole vaporization of the entire human race that one time?</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ellie Main (I think that's hername, am I right) had the same idea on the after show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T19:18:59-08:00","id":1268128,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> So if mankind was wiped out completely, why and how did it come back? And how dare the gods presume to judge a mankind they didn't even create? (Their humans they killed and then they buggered off. If there was anything about them returning to recreate mankind, I missed it? </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T22:28:02-08:00","id":1268172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1268128#post1268128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> So if mankind was wiped out completely, why and how did it come back? And how dare the gods presume to judge a mankind they didn't even create? (Their humans they killed and then they buggered off. If there was anything about them returning to recreate mankind, I missed it? </div></div> </div> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> They didn't mention recreating it, but the light brother did mention that humanity was going to start coming back eventually regardless. This could be an indicator that not all of humanity had been wiped out. Which could be from a number of reasons ranging from the destruction being targeted to those with magic and not hitting the few without, the light sibling purposely sparing some, or setting things in motion to have them come back, or just that humanity was the only thing that got wiped out and the light brother figured humanity 2.0 would eventually evolve from one of the remaining species. <br /> <br /> As for daring, well I mean a few local nations were conned into attacking them with power that, from what we can tell, probably couldn't have even been used to hurt the brothers if they chose to take the shots and the dark brother decided to retalliate by explicitly extincting the species. Face it the least d*bag theory I've seen on the brothers is Sunder's positing that the light brother is really hoping Salem will turn over a new leaf since he thinks that might get his brother to stop being such a pain. So we're not really standing on the grounds of these things being exceptionally benevolent. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T06:01:37-08:00","id":1268240,"title":"","content":"I am going to go back and remove ALL my Spoiler tags after Chapter 3 is available to the public, like I do on other forums, to make these conversations more accessible.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Like so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1268172#post1268172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They didn't mention recreating it, but the light brother did mention that humanity was going to start coming back eventually regardless. This could be an indicator that not all of humanity had been wiped out. Which could be from a number of reasons ranging from the destruction being targeted to those with magic and not hitting the few without, the light sibling purposely sparing some, or setting things in motion to have them come back, or just that humanity was the only thing that got wiped out and the light brother figured humanity 2.0 would eventually evolve from one of the remaining species.</div> </div> </div> </div>The brothers created the planet. Or at least, the Light Brother did, since the Dark Brother didn't care for making things like rocks, water, and grass. They could have designed it to produce a new crop of humanity if the first one was wiped out.<br /> <br /> Essentially, they seemed to have agreed to &quot;best two out of three&quot; in their contest of whether creatures made by both of them would choose to validate the Light God's philosophy of creation and coexistence or the Dark God's philosophy of destruction and egocentricism.<br /> <br /> This experiment between the two of them is a WAGER and a WAR. This isn't one of those Chem Lab lessons in high school, these two are scientists competing with each other to prove The Truth. Whoever is wrong has to stop doing what they want and abide by the other's way of life.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for daring, well I mean a few local nations were conned into attacking them with power that, from what we can tell, probably couldn't have even been used to hurt the brothers if they chose to take the shots and the dark brother decided to retalliate by explicitly extincting the species </div> </div> </div>But ask yourself this: If only three nations attacked the gods, why didn't the REST of the world DEFEND the gods?<br /> <br /> Either no one else in the world cared enough about the gods to defend them, which would be offensive in itself, or the three nations had to fight and kill other human beings before they marched on the gods themselves, in which case humanity had very much proven it wasn't interested in coexistence with itself, let alone the brothers.<br /> <br /> Also, the brothers were remarkably chill gods, when you get down to it. Anyone could just walk into their sanctums at any time, and the god would instantly appear to hear whatever they had to say. Even the God of Darkness. There was also no word that either of them demanded worship or sacrifices.<br /> <br /> The Light God expressed sympathy for Salem, and gently tried to explain why he couldn't do what she asked, and when she made it clear that she wouldn't listen, he gently sent her away. He's the one that wanted to make humanity in the first place, and the one giving humanity a second chance, and the one sending Ozma back to help them succeed at the second chance after Salem corrupted herself in the Pool of Annihilation.<br /> <br /> His brother never wanted to make mankind and, as we can see, is perfectly happy to wipe them all out forever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Face it the least d*bag theory I've seen on the brothers is Sunder's positing that the light brother is really hoping Salem will turn over a new leaf since he thinks that might get his brother to stop being such a pain. </div> </div> </div>I'm so happy that someone here has read my articles!<br /> <br /> The ones relevant to this conversation will be properly indexed and removed of Spoiler tags as soon as the episode goes public.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, I posted that theory on this thread. Nevermind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So we're not really standing on the grounds of these things being exceptionally benevolent. </div> </div> </div>Certainly not the Dark God, but the Light God has to concede a lot to his brother in order to maintain the agreement between them, or else his brother will just return to destroying everything without giving it a chance. Salem deserved some sort of punishment for nearly starting the war all over again and dooming her entire planet and species the first time, and becoming a living lesson for his brother that might save humanity for eternity is a punishment that fits her crime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-17-2018, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T13:36:04-08:00","id":1268393,"title":"","content":"I finally watched the episode. I noticed something:<br /> <br /> I've seen everyone talking about Salem killing her family, but...I don't see her doing anything to the girls. She fought Ozma, but we're not shown the daughters dying or their bodies. Just the ruined castle and her killing him.<br /> <br /> So are they out there somewhere? Seems almost a chekhov's gun to show the one using magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T13:57:26-08:00","id":1268399,"title":"","content":"Btw, am I the only one who wants to Ghost Eating Technique those two brothers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T15:33:11-08:00","id":1268416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1268128#post1268128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> So if mankind was wiped out completely, why and how did it come back? And how dare the gods presume to judge a mankind they didn't even create? (Their humans they killed and then they buggered off. If there was anything about them returning to recreate mankind, I missed it? </div></div> </div> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Out there guess, but probably something to do with the relics (which contain the foundation of humanity in them). Kinda like how the Faunus are still a big mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T17:26:55-08:00","id":1268436,"title":"","content":"New ep thing<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Huh, yeah you know it hadn't occurred to me that part of the reason Ozpin hadn't mentioned the story is because people would invariably want to know the plan for dealing with an entity that ,so far as anyone knows, has perfect immortality and access to literal magic. Which does not go over well when you don't have a plan to tell them. So maybe part of the cryptic thing might have been a bit of a defense on Ozpin's part that he just got really in over his head on. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T17:52:11-08:00","id":1268440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1268399#post1268399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, am I the only one who wants to Ghost Eating Technique those two brothers?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're far from alone in that sentiment, but not everyone agrees.<br /> <br /> I, for one, would like to point out that the God of Light has been trying to put an end to his brother's bullshit since the beginning of time, and only isn't socking him in the face right now because starting their old brawl all over again would (1) destroy the whole world anyway, and (2) break their agreement so that the Dark God would just go back to destroying everything he makes forever.<br /> <br /> So he has to play nice with his brother and concede some things in order to get his brother to concede other things.<br /> <br /> And I've already explained why I think the God of Light has a good reason to leave Salem immortal even as she's working against him in his contest against his brother. As a punishment, serving as a potential lesson for his brother fits her crime of nearly igniting their war all over again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T18:07:20-08:00","id":1268443,"title":"","content":"A few more thoughts:<br /> <br /> So was Ozpin the name of the last bearer? Or has Ozma started calling himself that now? And which is the one talking?<br /> <br /> Where is his old staff?<br /> <br /> Salem seems to have set up headquarters in the Dark D-bag's realm. So, that means the Light Jackass's realm must also still be there. Maybe they should try to find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T23:52:05-08:00","id":1268487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1268240#post1268240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am going to go back and remove ALL my Spoiler tags after Chapter 3 is available to the public, like I do on other forums, to make these conversations more accessible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh thank god.<br /> <br /> Sunder, whatever arguments we might or might not have over RWBY, you doing just this one thing makes you a King Among Forum Dwellers, as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter d</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, am I the only one who wants to Ghost Eating Technique those two brothers?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are not. The two brothers are both exceptionally evil.<br /> <br /> The God of Light is better than his brother, but he still thought it would be a great idea to grotesquely transgress the bodily autonomy of hundreds if not thousands of people yet unborn by cramming Ozma inside of them and granting him significant power to violate the sanctity and agency of their own bodies and minds without their knowledge or consent. This is a great crime.<br /> <br /> If it were me, I would be trying to figure out a way to destroy at least one of the four relics. (Probably the destruction one, because that's the least productive one, unless that one is absolutely and completely required to destroy one of the other three.) Without their nasty little apocalypse trigger, the Gods don't come back, and good riddance.<br /> <br /> I'm at this point speculating that Salem's goal is to assemble all four Relics and push the big red button, if for no other reason than &quot;assemble the Relics and then have no plans at all to push the button&quot; on her part would be very bad writing; you don't put this kind of Chekov's gun on the wall and have no plans to follow through. If the villain is planning to assemble the four things that summon the beings that end the world, they are presumably planning to use them to summon said beings. There's room for twists in there; for example, Salem may think she's amassed enough power to go for God Slaying 2: This Time It's Personal, and make it STICK. And she needs the Relics to call them home to make that happen.<br /> <br /> But I think it's a safe assumption that she wants all four in order to use them for their intended purpose.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T00:20:17-08:00","id":1268489,"title":"","content":"I think Salem wants to summon the two arrogant god brothers in the hopes that this time, they'll finish the job and kill her along with humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T01:47:41-08:00","id":1268496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1268443#post1268443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A few more thoughts:<br /> <br /> So was Ozpin the name of the last bearer? Or has Ozma started calling himself that now? And which is the one talking?</div> </div> </div> </div>My assumption is he'll modify his name based on the current host, since as he's noted they eventually become a singular conciousness anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1268443#post1268443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is his old staff?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the timeline of different hosts I figured he just modified it as time went on and used parts of it for other things, plus wear and tear. I mean we did see the gem getting smaller throughout the timeline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1268443#post1268443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Salem seems to have set up headquarters in the Dark D-bag's realm. So, that means the Light Jackass's realm must also still be there. Maybe they should try to find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on if there was anything special about the area. We know the dark brother set up the original pool that created the Grimm, and presumably that was the thing in his temple he crawled out of*, we don't know that the light brother had done anything with his temple outside of make it a pretty area. In short we don't know if the light brother's base was there because it was special, or if it was special because the light brother was there.<br /> <br /> *On a seperate note I have to admit that bit was animated well it did come off as kind of unsettling to watch the dark brother's entrance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T03:42:15-08:00","id":1268508,"title":"","content":"btw, I think CottageSalem may well be the most beautiful character we've seen on this show so far (and remember, she's up against Yang and Blake for that title).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T09:00:44-08:00","id":1268557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1268487#post1268487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh thank god.<br /> <br /> Sunder, whatever arguments we might or might not have over RWBY, you doing just this one thing makes you a King Among Forum Dwellers, as far as I'm concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't my idea, but it was one I was happy to execute.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The God of Light is better than his brother, but he still thought it would be a great idea to grotesquely transgress the bodily autonomy of hundreds if not thousands of people yet unborn by cramming Ozma inside of them and granting him significant power to violate the sanctity and agency of their own bodies and minds without their knowledge or consent. This is a great crime. </div> </div> </div>Whatever harm the God of Light may do to some people, he's arguably justified in that his brother will simply destroy everyone, forever, for all time, possibly including their afterlife, if the God of Light cannot get humanity to convince his brother to stop being an asshole.<br /> <br /> The God of Light doesn't want to hurt anyone, but what else can he do?<br /> <br /> And just like Ozpin would later do himself, it seems that the God of Light kept secrets from Ozma when offering him the deal. Before and after Ozma accepted the deal, the god didn't explain that Salem was immortal and cursed to desire destruction. Sure, he warned Ozpin that she wasn't the same woman he'd known and that she would only bring him pain, but arguably the CRUCIAL detail was that Salem would single-handedly doom Ozma's efforts to succeed at his task to virtual impossibility.<br /> <br /> (or maybe his brother demanded that the God of Light NOT reveal that information, in return for letting him send Ozma back at all)<br /> <br /> The god also didn't explain the exact details of Ozma's method of reincarnation. This is the crime that Ozpin sought very hard to avoid committing himself with Pyrrha. Even after she said she would do it, he warned her what might happen if she took someone's Aura into herself, and he gave her time to think it over. Even after she voluntarily got into the pod, he told her that he needed to hear her explicitly give her permission.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it were me, I would be trying to figure out a way to destroy at least one of the four relics. (Probably the destruction one, because that's the least productive one, unless that one is absolutely and completely required to destroy one of the other three.) </div> </div> </div>Leaving aside the wisdom of this general idea, I think you want to keep Destruction (because who doesn't need an WMD from time to time?) and destroy Choice.<br /> <br /> Hear me out.<br /> <br /> If the God of Light made the Relics of Creation and Knowledge, then logically his brother made the Relics of Destruction and... Choice.<br /> <br /> The God of Darkness is an asshole. He didn't care if people had knowledge, so he's fine with them being ignorant. He wants them to destroy each other, and to destroy them himself.<br /> <br /> I think to the extent that he wants them to have Choice, it is to prove that they aren't worthy of existence, or rather that Choice rightfully belongs to those with the power to impose their choices on others. (Hypocritical, given his rage at his brother trying to control him.) Furthermore, the Relic of Choice is a crown; a symbol of authority, even tyranny.<br /> <br /> I believe the Relic of Choice is a mind-control device that gives one person the power to deny free will to others.<br /> <br /> It is the Relic that the Last King of Vale buried under his own personal school and made the most challenging to access. I think he feared and hated it the most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-18-2018, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T11:58:43-08:00","id":1268601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1268557#post1268557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whatever harm the God of Light may do to some people, he's arguably justified in that his brother will simply destroy everyone, forever, for all time, possibly including their afterlife, if the God of Light cannot get humanity to convince his brother to stop being an asshole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then he shouldn't have agreed to go-around number two.<br /> <br /> People aren't toys. People aren't <i>experiments</i>, which is how the God of Light implicitly refers to them as. They do not exist to validate his philosophical positions or his sense of order and correctness. He should not have agreed to a second bite at the apple if all it was going to be is &quot;let's introduce a bunch of people into a terrible world, with a terrible creature stalking it who I helped create and cannot be bothered to destroy, and then judge the shit out of them if they aren't up to not only MY standards, but the standards of the guy who is even more evil than I am who thinks genocide is a great idea. Oh, and we're not going to tell people that they're part of a giant experiment with a giant bet on it, either.&quot;<br /> <br /> The response of an ethical being in that situation should be &quot;no deal, brother. Your terms aren't good enough. If we're to create thinking beings, they deserve better than to be subjected to such horror.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The God of Light doesn't want to hurt anyone, but what else can he do? </div> </div> </div>Again; not put people in this situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And just like Ozpin would later do himself, it seems that the God of Light kept secrets from Ozma when offering him the deal. Before and after Ozma accepted the deal, the god didn't explain that Salem was immortal and cursed to desire destruction. Sure, he warned Ozpin that she wasn't the same woman he'd known and that she would only bring him pain, but arguably the CRUCIAL detail was that Salem would single-handedly doom Ozma's efforts to succeed at his task to virtual impossibility. </div> </div> </div>This is also a dick move, yeah.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (or maybe his brother demanded that the God of Light NOT reveal that information, in return for letting him send Ozma back at all) </div> </div> </div>Possible! That seems like their style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The god also didn't explain the exact details of Ozma's method of reincarnation. This is the crime that Ozpin sought very hard to avoid committing himself with Pyrrha. </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? No it isn't. Ozpin deliberately withholds all sorts of vital information from Pyrrha (and, as we now know, the rest of the Ozluminati) from Pyrrha that is absolutely necessary for him to be an ethical, moral actor in that affair. Off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> 1) Does not tell Pyrrha that her new job will make her a top-priority target of the Grimm's immortal queen.<br /> 2) Does not tell Pyrrha that her new job will make her the key to an object of world-bending power and that anyone who wants that key, including but not limited to the Grimm's aforementioned immortal queen, will regard her as an object to be used.<br /> 3) That the Grimm's immortal queen has specifically strong immortality (&quot;literally can't die&quot;) rather than weak immortality (&quot;will not age, but can be killed&quot;) and so Pyrrha literally cannot fight her way out of this.<br /> <br /> And that's just off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> If that's him &quot;trying very hard&quot; then he is bad at his self-appointed job, and he should feel bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe the Relic of Choice is a mind-control device that gives one person the power to deny free will to others. </div> </div> </div>In this hypothetical, yeah, Choice would be what you want to pop rather Destruction. If the Relic of Choice were indeed some kind of vicious mind-control device, it would be at the top of the list.<br /> <br /> We don't know what the other three do (which is something Team RWBY should really kick out of Ozpin at the first opportunity) but if one were to enact my &quot;destroy one so the Gods can never return to murder us all&quot; plan, which one you picked would be contingent. If the Relic of Destruction is, say, a sword that can destroy almost anything (presumably the Destruction Relic cannot destroy Salem), some kind of ultimate cutting implement against which no Aura, armor, shield, hide, or anything can stop it... that's fairly anodyne and maybe you can keep it around.<br /> <br /> If it's some kind of city-wrecker though, something whose lowest setting is &quot;lays waste to kingdoms&quot; and then scales up from there... at that point there's little productive use for it and the other three might be REALLY sweet.<br /> <br /> There's opportunity for more reveals here. The Knowledge Relic is fairly anodyne and straightforward, but I really hope that the other three have some cool twists and turns with them. The Choice Relic is the most pregnant with possibility; that can potentially do all KINDS of neat things within a wide possibility space.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T12:32:18-08:00","id":1268609,"title":"","content":"Nah, Ozpin told Pyrrha <a href=\"https://sunder-the-gold.tumblr.com/post/178966222816/ozpin-told-pyrrha-all-she-needed-to-know\" target=\"_blank\">everything she needed to know</a>. If he told her any more, she couldn't have walked away with the ability to trust the adults to take care of things without her. She couldn't have let herself push that burden onto anyone else.<br /> <br /> They told her just enough so that she didn't feel pressured to save the entire world. Which Ozpin wouldn't have asked her to do, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T12:45:07-08:00","id":1268613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1268609#post1268609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, Ozpin told Pyrrha <a href=\"https://sunder-the-gold.tumblr.com/post/178966222816/ozpin-told-pyrrha-all-she-needed-to-know\" target=\"_blank\">everything she needed to know</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. He didn't. Not even close. Among other things, he's drafting her into a forever war from which her only escape is death. With what he told her, Pyrrha has a reasonable hope of one day winning out; you find whoever is killing Maidens, or really whoever is specifically after Amber, and you stop them.<br /> <br /> But you can't win out against Salem like that.<br /> <br /> And even without Salem, &quot;you are the unique key to an object of literally world-ending power&quot; is incredibly relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If he told her any more, she couldn't have walked away with the ability to trust the adults to take care of things without her. She couldn't have let herself push that burden onto anyone else. </div> </div> </div>Ozpin <i>doesn't get to make that decision for her. </i>That is wildly and grossly unethical. When you paint a target for a creature like Salem on someones back, anything less than full disclosure is not anywhere near enough.<br /> <br /> The other members of the Ozluminati are also complicit in this. I don't expect better from Jimmy Ironwood, and Glynda is something of a question mark, but I <i>do</i> expect better from Qrow.<br /> <br /> I expect this kind of bullshit on Oz's part to be a major point of contention between Oscar and Oz. Oscar, as shown in his speech to Hazel, places immense value on people being able to exercise informed agency; for him, the key element in Hazel's conflict with Ozpin was whether or not Hazel's sister was able to make an informed and free choice as to follow Ozpin.<br /> <br /> Oz... does not seem to be real big on informed agency. Oz appears to be big on telling people precisely enough to get them to do what he wants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They told her just enough so that she didn't feel pressured to save the entire world. Which Ozpin wouldn't have asked her to do, anyway. </div> </div> </div>Ozpin was absolutely asking her to save the entire world. The people who are the keys to the apocalypse buttons are <i>constantly</i> engaged in the task of saving the entire world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T00:01:47-08:00","id":1268746,"title":"","content":"Oh brainstorm: i had an idea for what 4 daughters' names should be (I dont remember them being named). They are:<br /> <br /> Valerie<br /> Misty<br /> Vicky<br /> Mandy<br /> <br /> <br /> Think about those and you may get where I'm going with this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T00:39:53-08:00","id":1269144,"title":"","content":"I feel like the only one who doesn't hate the Gods from Ep. 3<br /> <br /> They <i>made the world</i>. All of it, every tree and bird and person. Every tiger that feeds on every deer is part of their enormous creation, and they have made at least two worlds that we know of. <br /> <br /> <b>Can we have any idea how alien in mind and scope they must be?</b> Some people are decrying them killing humans, but so what? Humans to them are nothing. Humans are grass on a lawn. They can make or unmake humans at any time, by will alone. <i>And the humans tried to usurp the power of the gods</i>. Not a single one of us would wring are hands and cry about rights and losses if we had to kill an wild animal that threatened us in our homes. Not one of us spares a thought for an inconvenient mosquito or the menacing sting of the hornet. And the humans took the power that <i>the gods themselves gave</i>. That's like dogs starting a conspiracy to kill us for our beds. Yes, I am a human and I feel human dignity and all that, but once the gods are physically, tangibly real, we have to accept that we go from &quot;undisputed top of the Right To Live By Virtue Of Meaning Totem Pole to <i>several notches down</i>. And then the gods went ahead and made more humanity just to see if the experiment could fix itself. That's <b><i>the most merciful deal in the history of time</i></b>. <br /> <br /> Kill them? No. Worship them? No. They can't be treated with our morality just as I can not be held to the standards of ants and other bugs. How many hives have I carelessly destroyed? how many pesticides have a used to make life a little more convenient for myself? I don't even pass the bar we are holding them to, and they are beings of PHENOMENAL COSMIC POWER. <br /> <br /> Some people want to <i>Kill Destruction</i>. Can you even fathom that? All of us, here, forever, with no more births, no more deaths, no seasons, no foods, no growth, all because nothing could ever be born or we'd run out of room in a heartbeat. Static, stagnant. Or worse- we'd become tumorous, our numbers would expand until we filled all of the planet and space. Because we are small, fearful, and petty. Because we are like Salem, little more than angry children. <br /> <br /> I like the Gods of this show. I like them for being wiser and grander than mere mortals. Their eyes see a horizon much farther than ours. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> aaand the Love makes you evil stuff was kinda dumb but I liked the rest of it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T02:43:26-08:00","id":1269160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1269144#post1269144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the only one who doesn't hate the Gods from Ep. 3</div> </div> </div> </div> Hate, nah. I think the prevailing opinion is they're d-bags.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1269144#post1269144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They <i>made the world</i>. All of it, every tree and bird and person. Every tiger that feeds on every deer is part of their enormous creation, and they have made at least two worlds that we know of.<br /> <br /> <b>Can we have any idea how alien in mind and scope they must be?</b> Some people are decrying them killing humans, but so what? Humans to them are nothing. Humans are grass on a lawn. They can make or unmake humans at any time, by will alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't really get around an argument on whether or not mass slaughter of sentient life is moral or not just because its easy to make, destroy, and replace. Just means you get to be completely serious if you tell someone, &quot;I brought you into this world and I can take you out. It won't make no difference [sic] either cause I'll make another that looks just like you.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1269144#post1269144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>And the humans tried to usurp the power of the gods</i>. Not a single one of us would wring are hands and cry about rights and losses if we had to kill an wild animal that threatened us in our homes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually I've met a fair amount of people that would or did when. Plus your comparison isn't really working since the veracity of the idea that the humans threatened the brothers depends heavily on which version of threatened we use. Made promises, or took actions to imply harm and violence, sure. Actually possessed the capability to follow through on those though, that doesn't seem as strong an argument. The former without the capacity for the latter well I mean I guess you might annoy them or hurt their feelings, but that really isn't a great cause for wiping out a species. I mean Salem's entire case was based off of them not being all knowing and infallible, that doesn't actually mean that humanity possessed any means of causing harm to either sibling beyond getting one to take a shot at the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1269144#post1269144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not one of us spares a thought for an inconvenient mosquito or the menacing sting of the hornet.</div> </div> </div> </div> And I hold nothing against them for thinking I'm an ass if I kill them when they feed on me or cause me harm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1269144#post1269144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And the humans took the power that <i>the gods themselves gave</i>. That's like dogs starting a conspiracy to kill us for our beds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna have to argue against that considering how often my cat has tried to sever the tendons in my ankles to bring me down. (She's adorable, but really she's been at it for close to a decade now so not much progress.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1269144#post1269144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I am a human and I feel human dignity and all that, but once the gods are physically, tangibly real, we have to accept that we go from &quot;undisputed top of the Right To Live By Virtue Of Meaning Totem Pole to <i>several notches down</i>. And then the gods went ahead and made more humanity just to see if the experiment could fix itself. That's <b><i>the most merciful deal in the history of time</i></b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think a species being more powerful than humanity makes humanity as whole less entitled to continuing to exist. Heck going back to your animal thing earlier, people go vegetarian and vegan because they believe those animals have just as much of a right to live as humans do. Hell considering the aformentioned potential that humanity lacks a means to harm them and that they don't need humanity for anything like food or companionship; one could make an argument that they are actually less justified in killing humans than humans killing animals. Since humans at least need to eat to continue living and those animals contain important compounds for continued healthy existence.<br /> <br /> Now as for the relic judgment system that's an unknown we already brought up. All we got was the Light brother telling Ozma that humanity would come back, now this could easily imply that they set the wheels in motion to restart humanity again. Except, well it also doesn't confirm that they did. It is just as possibly that all they did was choose not to wipe prevent humanity from coming back into existence again. Note, that we also don't see any faunis until we're in the second trial at humanity, at which point we are explicitly shown them. Considering this is the one meant to verify whether or not humanity should exist at all, it seems like it would be a really bad idea to throw in a new type of being in with the first type if you're not even sure if the concept is viable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1269144#post1269144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kill them? No. Worship them? No. They can't be treated with our morality just as I can not be held to the standards of ants and other bugs. How many hives have I carelessly destroyed? how many pesticides have a used to make life a little more convenient for myself? I don't even pass the bar we are holding them to, and they are beings of PHENOMENAL COSMIC POWER.</div> </div> </div> </div> Really? What species did you knowingly wipe out because it was inconvenient? Just saying you're making a very problematic statement that power = morality; which you know considering which game's forum we're on should be a point that such is not how it works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1269144#post1269144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some people want to <i>Kill Destruction</i>. Can you even fathom that? All of us, here, forever, with no more births, no more deaths, no seasons, no foods, no growth, all because nothing could ever be born or we'd run out of room in a heartbeat. Static, stagnant. Or worse- we'd become tumorous, our numbers would expand until we filled all of the planet and space. Because we are small, fearful, and petty. Because we are like Salem, little more than angry children.</div> </div> </div> </div> So far we haven't seen that they are needed for the system to continue, in fact evidence suggests that even if they created the system ,and obviously we've seen them ignore and violate it when it suits them, it would seem that this is much like the Primordials where they created the system to operate even if they were no longer at the wheel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1269144#post1269144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Gods of this show. I like them for being wiser and grander than mere mortals. Their eyes see a horizon much farther than ours.</div> </div> </div> </div> Light maybe, at the very least I can see him trying to play a longer game. Darkness seems content to just be powerful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1269144#post1269144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">aaand the Love makes you evil stuff was kinda dumb but I liked the rest of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, I'm still seeing that as more Salem having entitlement issues than love making her evil. Though I think we can all agree that the fight at the end where she killed Ozma the first time probably did not help her psyche, especially if the kids died in that fight like some people are speculating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 11-20-2018, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T03:35:18-08:00","id":1269170,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://i.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/newsfeed/001/433/127/c66.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T23:19:46-08:00","id":1269452,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3400_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3400\" data-vbnamecard=\"3400\">nalak42</a> , those are all good points, I just wanted to offer a defense of the Gods since no one else had. Although given Light and Dark's ability to call souls back from the afterlife with the apparent difficulty of flicking a lightswitch, I doubt they place the same value on human life as we do. Light, at least, seemed to think the Balance was the only thing protecting humanity at all. I don't fault Dark for exterminating the humans when they literally just showed up at the house of the two gods to kill them and steal their powers (with Salem promising that she'd keep doing that forever). There was probably a nongenocidal answer, but that's gods for you. <br /> <br /> I haven't seen Ep 4 so I don't know what other bombshells come out, but I have this question- what does Salem hope she's going to <b>actually</b> accomplish? best case scenario, she gets the relics together, the gods come back, and they... destroy everything again and leave Salem where she was before. She's 0 for 2 in getting killed, what makes her think the third time is the charm?<br /> <br /> What happened to the Pool of Light? the Pool of Dark exists without Darkness maintaining it. Salem knows where it is and never tried to jump in to see what would happen? She <i>can't die</i>. I swear if that comes up as the Macguffin to undo her I am gonna link this post <i>so hard</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T01:17:46-08:00","id":1270048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1268393#post1268393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen everyone talking about Salem killing her family, but...I don't see her doing anything to the girls. She fought Ozma, but we're not shown the daughters dying or their bodies. Just the ruined castle and her killing him.<br /> <br /> So are they out there somewhere? Seems almost a chekhov's gun to show the one using magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbt<br /> <br /> Okay there was a very clear establishing shot of one of the daughters' toys in the wreckage, in the aftermath of a fight that involved the castle being blasted, Ozma being fatally wounded, and Salem was fucking vaporized (we see her reform when the rubble settles)<br /> <br /> Like, Salem didn't deliberately kill her kids but make no mistake... Those kids were EXCEPTIONALLY dead.<br /> <br /> I mean, at least three of them were, I could maybe buy ONE of them managing to escape. But nah, those kids are dead and it's because Salem took exception to her husband taking the kids away from the crazy bitch that was advocating a purge of the Invalids and replacing them with a Pure Master Race.<br /> <br /> And considering her reaction to him trying to leave was to start flinging fireballs <i>dude was right to do so</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T07:05:18-08:00","id":1270104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1269144#post1269144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the only one who doesn't hate the Gods from Ep. 3</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't.<br /> <br /> Well, I think the Dark God is a spoiled child and an abusive parent/creator, but that's really the point. There wouldn't be a story if he wasn't, because basically the whole story of <i>RWBY </i>is the Older Brother trying to teach his Younger Brother a lesson in kindness and humility so that everyone can coexist.<br /> <br /> Not that the Older Brother is perfect. I think he struggles against a tendency to be controlling. His brother certainly accused him of such, and it was only after the Dark God made that accusation that the Light God slowed down enough to explain himself, whereas previously he had just stormed into his brother's bedroom and killed a mortal that his younger brother had resurrected.<br /> <br /> They might have been provoked by Salem, but the Old Brother very nearly did <i>personally </i>reignite the very feud he was trying to stop, through his own mistakes. Salem wasn't mistaken when she learned that they were fallible.<br /> <br /> Further, it is interesting that the Dark God is the one who made the Relic of Choice, though we'll have to wait to see if the Crown is a rather dark take on Choice by giving one the power to take it away. Presumably, it can't mind-control people, or else a Wizard might have tried using it against Salem, who shouldn't have a defense against that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> aaand the Love makes you evil stuff was kinda dumb but I liked the rest of it. </div> </div> </div>It wasn't love, but selfishness.<br /> <br /> Remember how much Ozma was thrashing about in panic, perhaps even pain, when he was first resurrected? The Light God called his current state &quot;rest&quot;. She had him torn away from his rest and it caused him severe distress, but Salem doesn't care because she got what she wanted. From the start, Salem was a self-centered person who didn't consider the feelings or needs of others. The sort of person who would demand the gods treat her as an exception among her species and to the rules of life and death, and then try to manipulate, attack, or blackmail them when they refused to treat her any differently than any other woman.<br /> <br /> <br /> To further reinforce the idea of <i>RWBY </i>death as rest, consider this question: <i>why </i>did the God of Light send Ozma back to Remnant, instead of literally anyone else? He had to know just how badly he was going to risk pissing Salem off.<br /> <br /> Remember that originally, Ozma didn't care about going back to Remnant, because he thought everyone he knew and cared about was dead. He didn't care about the new humanity he'd never met, or at least not badly enough to give up his rest, especially when he could find Salem waiting for him in the afterlife.<br /> <br /> He <i>only</i> agreed to return upon learning that Salem was still on Remnant.<br /> <br /> Ozma might have literally been the last person the Light God dared to ask to take up the mission, because everyone else the Light God could trust with the mission declined it on the grounds that they had no one to go back to. Especially after her actions got everyone killed, there was no one left among the entire Human 1.0 species that cared about Salem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-01-2018, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T18:06:18-08:00","id":1270474,"title":"","content":"New episode things<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> So we have an excellent show on how one can narrate fights using Rainwalker and weapons like it now. Also am I alone in thinking Neo looks adorable with Torchwig's hat? I also am looking forward to next week, because I am so swiping whatever happened to the farm for my campaign.(Might have to modify it, but hey that's just fun.)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T21:31:27-08:00","id":1270519,"title":"","content":"Episode 4:<br /> <br /> Of course he has no plan. He was focused on destroying her. When he found out he couldn't he couldn't think of another way and is just now trying to stay ahead of her. His fault is he couldn't shift gears and think of another way after that. Well, victory isn't in destruction every time.<br /> <br /> Salem is terrifying when calm....and got scarier as she went.<br /> <br /> they're focusing a lot on Emerald. I do theink they're setting up a plot point for her. A defection maybe, she is too afraid of Salem to stay, though I hope it's not a death arc.<br /> <br /> I notice something. Salem lists why everyone is there: Justice, Love, Reverence. Now, we only know about two of her lieutentants so far, but it seems to line up to them, though in twisted ways. They see it that way but that's not what it is. Justice would be Hazel, as in he seeks it for his sister though what he really wants is Revenge. Reverence is Tyrion, though it's sick obsessive worship. So, if Watts is there for some twisted reason he could justify as love that would fit.<br /> <br /> They also fit Salem's motivations. She loved Oz/ma/pin. She wants justice for what happened to him and her (or revenge again). And she reveres herself. So, how does this lead to an endgame for her?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 11-25-2018, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T21:41:53-08:00","id":1270521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1270474#post1270474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New episode things<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> So we have an excellent show on how one can narrate fights using Rainwalker and weapons like it now. Also am I alone in thinking Neo looks adorable with Torchwig's hat? I also am looking forward to next week, because I am so swiping whatever happened to the farm for my campaign.(Might have to modify it, but hey that's just fun.)</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It is only for a second, but look at her expression as she lifts to face Cinder, wearing the hat. That's sorrow right there. Also notice how her clothes are all torn apart...but only after she lets the hat appear. Hiding her ragged state the whole fight. Now I feel sorry for her <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Cool fight scene tho. Glad to see her style translated well to the Maia setup and crew.<br /> Also I bet Qrow dies in this fucking house. Too much grimm!day5.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T21:54:04-08:00","id":1270524,"title":"","content":"A thought: Maria can't be some random old lady who just happened to be in the rear cars. She has too much personality and independant force of will to be an extra. She has to be someone. And I see 3 possiblilities:<br /> <br /> -A Silver-eyed Warrior (good, we need someone to teach Ruby to actually use that power)<br /> <br /> -A lost Maiden<br /> <br /> -Decended from one of Oz/Salem's daughters.<br /> <br /> Ok, attack this idea....NOW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T22:38:45-08:00","id":1270529,"title":"","content":"Sooo... aren't the daughters of Ozma and Salem obviously the original Maidens? Four sisters all wearing season-colored dresses?<br /> <br /> Oz's next incarnation is even shown as an old man. Now did he simply live to be old or.... did he reincarnate into an old man, then became a hermit because he was depressed? If the latter, he's then the hermit that the maidens come to in order to cheer up. Then he's so happy that his daughters came to him and were so incredibly nice that he... uh... does something to make the Maiden magic pass down?<br /> <br /> Okay, it's not obvious or certain, but it does seem at least quite plausible to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T00:05:11-08:00","id":1270536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1270524#post1270524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thought: Maria can't be some random old lady who just happened to be in the rear cars. She has too much personality and independant force of will to be an extra. She has to be someone. And I see 3 possiblilities:<br /> <br /> -A Silver-eyed Warrior (good, we need someone to teach Ruby to actually use that power)<br /> <br /> -A lost Maiden<br /> <br /> -Decended from one of Oz/Salem's daughters.<br /> <br /> Ok, attack this idea....NOW</div> </div> </div> </div>The FNDM as a whole has largely come to the conclusion that she's gotta be a Silver-Eyed Warrior. The lengths they went to to shield her eyes, plus the framing in the credits, have that theory running massively ahead of everything else.<br /> <br /> As for being descended from Salem... the thing is, that happened so long ago that either EVERYONE is descended from Salem, or no-one is. If the kids lived to reproduce at all, after many centuries everyone on the planet can most likely be tied back to that line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T01:10:54-08:00","id":1270547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1270529#post1270529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo... aren't the daughters of Ozma and Salem obviously the original Maidens? Four sisters all wearing season-colored dresses?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been thinking something similar. When Ozma created the Maidens, he was replacing his daughters. Four young girls bearing magic. Of course, he wouldn't have known if all the girls died or not.<br /> <br /> As for his old incarnation, he's shown walking by many gravestones. I think that shows he was not the next, and he was around a while.<br /> <br /> As for the girls' decendants... look up the hidden elf village trope. could work.<br /> <br /> Or am I too hopeful for a happy ending?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T05:02:37-08:00","id":1270569,"title":"","content":"Random thought on the function of Maiden-hood and how they relate to Oz. <br /> <br /> Oz\u2019s \u2018aura/soul\u2019 skips around every time a host dies but the way it\u2019s been discussed and framed sounds like his essence acts a little bit like an exaltation, while he picks up bits from each host it is only the essential Oz that moves on to the next, Oscar and his predecessors seem free of this. <br /> <br /> Now, since the Maidens are empowered by the \u2018wizard\u2019 which I\u2019m assuming is Oz by dividing up his magic amongst them, it sounds like he has fragmented himself and those large portions of his power are \u2018afflicted\u2019 with the same host-seeking properties. <br /> <br /> Additional thought; if this is how it works, what does this mean for Qrow and Raven\u2019s powers? They were gifted in the same way (he mentions splitting his magic between them) but Oz had a lot less magic to give them. Or maybe he just ensorcelled them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T06:12:43-08:00","id":1270578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1270547#post1270547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have been thinking something similar. When Ozma created the Maidens, he was replacing his daughters. Four young girls bearing magic. Of course, he wouldn't have known if all the girls died or not.<br /> <br /> As for his old incarnation, he's shown walking by many gravestones. I think that shows he was not the next, and he was around a while.<br /> <br /> As for the girls' decendants... look up the hidden elf village trope. could work.<br /> <br /> Or am I too hopeful for a happy ending?</div> </div> </div> </div>The maidens might be literally his and salem's kids because as far as we saw they were magical and magic is thus somehow inheritable.<br /> It's not enough to have someone with magic, or a lot of people would have magic. From there to &quot;they kinda reincarnate not unlike Oz does because they inherited it from him&quot; is not a big jump.<br /> <br /> So there are 4 souls capable of magic in this world, all of which latch on to women and don't seem to retain any personality, just the power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T07:22:55-08:00","id":1270591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1270578#post1270578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The maidens might be literally his and salem's kids because as far as we saw they were magical and magic is thus somehow inheritable.<br /> It's not enough to have someone with magic, or a lot of people would have magic. From there to &quot;they kinda reincarnate not unlike Oz does because they inherited it from him&quot; is not a big jump.<br /> <br /> So there are 4 souls capable of magic in this world, all of which latch on to women and don't seem to retain any personality, just the power.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fairy tale of the Four Seasons/Maidens explains why Ozpin doesn't have the elemental blasty powers of Ozma.<br /> <br /> If he didn't give those powers away to four young women, then where did that power of his go?<br /> <br /> If they already had those powers, then wouldn't each Maiden be stronger than Ozma was if they each also got roughly 1/5 of Ozma power on top of their own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T07:33:29-08:00","id":1270592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1270519#post1270519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Episode 4:<br /> <br /> Of course he has no plan. He was focused on destroying her. When he found out he couldn't he couldn't think of another way and is just now trying to stay ahead of her. His fault is he couldn't shift gears and think of another way after that. Well, victory isn't in destruction every time.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Achieve harmony, summon the Gods, and get them to deal with Salem&quot; isn't a bad plan when it's the only real plan available to him. Even if the gods don't kill Salem or remove her immortality, then all of humanity getting magic back at least makes Salem and the Grimm less of a threat.<br /> <br /> The Wizard was even winning for the past 80 years.<br /> <br /> It took at least 10 years to bring his new global system down; 10 years of Raven hiding the Spring Maiden from everyone in one way or another, and leaving him unable to access the Relic of Knowledge. For all we know, Salem turned Leo 10 years ago, and it was while he was looking for a way to let Salem capture the Spring Maiden that the girl felt so scared and pressured that she would run away and decide to join a gang of bandits.<br /> <br /> Leo's betrayal was an equally terrible blow in its own regard, considering how it let Salem's agents directly into Beacon, and perhaps gave Watts the opportunity to design the Queen Virus (if he needed to study Haven Tower to learn how to infect Beacon Tower.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> they're focusing a lot on Emerald. I do theink they're setting up a plot point for her. A defection maybe, she is too afraid of Salem to stay, though I hope it's not a death arc. </div> </div> </div>Emerald is definitely questioning her choices. Every time we see her at Evernight, she more and more obviously Doesn't Want To Be There.<br /> <br /> But which scares her more? Staying with Salem, away from Cinder? Or inviting Salem's wrath by leaving her terrifying presence to go join forces with Salem?<br /> <br /> Salem may be dividing her allies as much as her enemies. She might be deliberately keeping Emerald and Cinder apart, so that they don't get any ideas of trying to escape her and form their own independent group, like Raven did to Ozpin.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They also fit Salem's motivations. She loved Oz/ma/pin. She wants justice for what happened to him and her (or revenge again). And she reveres herself. So, how does this lead to an endgame for her? </div> </div> </div>If Cinder manages to redeem herself this Volume by retrieving the Relic of Knowledge, Salem is liable to let us know what she wants when she asks Jinn her question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T08:23:28-08:00","id":1270606,"title":"","content":"I noticed that ScrewAttack put up a DBX video for Ruby vs Ragna Bloodedge, which RWBY fans might enjoy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OlqfZfaKfNU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OlqfZfaKfNU\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OlqfZfaKfNU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OlqfZfaKfNU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1551-barefoot-monkey","name":"Barefoot Monkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1551_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T12:03:05-08:00","id":1270656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barefoot Monkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1270606#post1270606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed that ScrewAttack put up a DBX video for Ruby vs Ragna Bloodedge, which RWBY fans might enjoy.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OlqfZfaKfNU\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OlqfZfaKfNU</a></div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s neat to see Ragna use his sword\u2019s scythe form for more than a finishing attack, but where\u2019s all of his Black Beast summons?<br /> <br /> And I don\u2019t know why people say Ruby used her Silver Eyes; they glowed but she didn\u2019t blast him with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T22:13:26-08:00","id":1270769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1270656#post1270656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And I don\u2019t know why people say Ruby used her Silver Eyes; they glowed but she didn\u2019t blast him with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forget, have we established what the heck the Silver Eyes even do? I know they can screw up Grimm, and Grimm hybrids like Cinder, but has it ever been established if they work on other things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T03:14:09-08:00","id":1270795,"title":"","content":"IIRC it was Cinder's Maiden powers that made her vulnerable.<br /> <br /> So it seems they affect things possessing the Old Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T03:17:31-08:00","id":1270796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1270795#post1270795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC it was Cinder's Maiden powers that made her vulnerable.<br /> <br /> So it seems they affect things possessing the Old Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anti-magic, huh. Hmm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T06:13:52-08:00","id":1270811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1270795#post1270795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC it was Cinder's Maiden powers that made her vulnerable.<br /> <br /> So it seems they affect things possessing the Old Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maiden powers come from Ozpin. Bird powers come from Ozpin. Raven has both, Qrow has one, and Oscar has whatever magic Ozpin has left.<br /> <br /> None of them reacted to Ruby\u2019s blast. Only Cinder, who is the only person in the room hosting a Grimm parasite.<br /> <br /> Which she was hosting when Ruby blasted her on top of Beacon tower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T06:33:43-08:00","id":1270815,"title":"","content":"So Salem was just BSing when she literally told Cinder the maiden powers made her weak to the silver eyes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T10:11:38-08:00","id":1270866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1270815#post1270815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Salem was just BSing when she literally told Cinder the maiden powers made her weak to the silver eyes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider that the method through which Cinder got those Maiden powers was a Grimm. The same Grimm that gives her the ability to steal more Maiden powers, when presumably that shouldn\u2019t be possible.<br /> <br /> The power to become a quadruple Maiden is definitely a power worth being called a power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T04:08:01-08:00","id":1271412,"title":"","content":"something I've been wondering...<br /> <br /> Jinn can answer 3 questions a century. She had two left when Ruby summoned her. <br /> <br /> <br /> What did Ozpin already ask her this century?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T08:10:31-08:00","id":1271454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1271412#post1271412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">something I've been wondering...<br /> <br /> Jinn can answer 3 questions a century. She had two left when Ruby summoned her. <br /> <br /> <br /> What did Ozpin already ask her this century?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve also been wondering.<br /> <br /> The Wizards have asked at least four questions, and we only know about three of them. We know they are so important that Ozpin had two left that he didn\u2019t use before the Spring Maiden fled.<br /> <br /> Raven ran away roughly 17 years ago. So while Ozpin had two questions left, he preferred the idea of permanently sacrificing more of his own dwindling magical powers to give Qrow and Raven the power to gather information for him as birds.<br /> <br /> Since the Wizards have probably controlled the Relic of Knowledge for more than 200 years (and I can provide my logic if you wish), they\u2019ve likely asked more than four questions.<br /> <br /> At least one of those questions has to be \u201cWhat does Salem WANT?\u201d But Jinn didn\u2019t reveal that. Maybe she didn\u2019t judge it important, maybe it isn\u2019t something Ozpin considers a secret, maybe Jinn has run into a limit on how much information she could reveal with a single answer, or maybe Rooster Teeth needed to end the chapter where they did regardless of in-universe considerations.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhere is Salem?\u201d is a low-priority question, since attacking her is futile. Still, it could be useful if you want to spy on her, or watch the coming and going of her minions... it\u2019s only after learning the answer that spying seems impractical, since she is surrounded by Grimm emerging from their apparent place of birth.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think he needed to ask how to make the vaults, since Jinn already gave him instructions for how to use the Relic of Creation that is likely responsible for them. <br /> <br /> He probably asked Jinn at least once what Salem was planning, which gave him a baseline understanding of her methods, minions, and resources, letting him begin his own counterplans. Or maybe he got such information for free when asking what Salem wanted?<br /> <br /> Or maybe asking what Salem is planning would have been the optimal choice, as it would cover her end-goal as well as her short- and long-term goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T20:03:38-08:00","id":1271672,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I liked the gods, both of them. They are stark characters with incredible agency, coming across as alien in their morality as they should for beings of creator-level power. <br /> <br /> I also appreciate that both of their non-Dragon forms look Faunus to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T20:26:35-08:00","id":1271677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1271672#post1271672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, I liked the gods, both of them. They are stark characters with incredible agency, coming across as alien in their morality as they should for beings of creator-level power.<br /> <br /> I also appreciate that both of their non-Dragon forms look Faunus to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like how they both come across as brothers who had their sibling quarrels in the past but have since matured into individuals who can talk through their disputes without needing to come to blows again. It gives them a dimension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T23:05:35-08:00","id":1271705,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This really does feel like the &quot;we listened to the fans&quot; volume, what with Neo's return and what appears to be a Grimm threat on a par with the Nuckelavee. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T23:26:04-08:00","id":1271711,"title":"","content":"and this is only the midpoint","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T07:38:15-08:00","id":1271770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1271705#post1271705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This really does feel like the &amp;quot;we listened to the fans&amp;quot; volume, what with Neo's return and what appears to be a Grimm threat on a par with the Nuckelavee. </div></div> </div> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>People say \u201clistened to fans\u201d, but I think Rooster Teeth is usually keenly aware of how far their execution fell short of their vision, given how hard they work and how much stuff always ends up in the cutting room floor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T11:29:45-08:00","id":1271805,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I remember in the AMAs and Streams post Volume 5, the crew were talking about how they're trying and they're really getting the hang of showing more and just telling less. I guess that's why, in spite of the shortcomings, I give RWBY a lot of slack and focus on when it works because one, I still enjoy it, and two... They're <i>trying</i>, and they <i>want</i> to get better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T12:00:39-08:00","id":1271818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1271770#post1271770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People say \u201clistened to fans\u201d, but I think Rooster Teeth is usually keenly aware of how far their execution fell short of their vision, given how hard they work and how much stuff always ends up in the cutting room floor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note, I'm drawing a distinction between finally getting backstory for the main antagonist and the return of a popular character who'd previously had a total screen time measured in minutes.<br /> <br /> One of those was necessary, the other wasn't but it is a fan pleasing move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T12:51:32-08:00","id":1271831,"title":"","content":"Actually, I think the returning character may be intended to serve a narrative purpose of giving another major antagonist someone to talk to, thus revealing her background as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T14:08:34-08:00","id":1271844,"title":"","content":"There are a handful of winks to criticisms in the first episode. I think there\u2019s been a marked improvement \u2014and that fan pleasing choices have been worked into the story for more then fan pleasing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T14:24:32-08:00","id":1271847,"title":"","content":"I was really disappointed with Nuckelavee in Volume 4.<br /> <br /> <br /> First of all, we'd seen a thunderstorm rolling in on the previous episode, the whole village is overcast, and Nora climbs a building, but she never once absorbs a lightning strike. Ruby also never shoots her with a Lightning Dust round. Our heroes factually didn't have to give that fight their all to win it, even before complaints that Ruby is never <i>shown </i>using her Semblance. Therefore, it makes the Petra Gigas look like a more dangerous opponent, since both Ruby and Nora DID use their Semblances.<br /> <br /> Though in Nora's case, it seemed like she used her Semblance's oft-forgotten ability to generate electricity to electrify her weapon, even if they make it sound like they added a generator to it to give her a jolt. (Not that a generator would make sense, since she could just use Lightning Dust directly instead of spending Fire Dust to fuel an electric generator.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Second of all, the Nuckelavee was more creepy than menacing. By Word of God, it's a combination of two separate models of Grimm that something mixed together... but it looks like even after 10 years the two Grimm have no idea how to work together except for one to completely stop moving when the other one wants to do anything. That surely made choreography easier, but far from impressive.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the horse didn't charge or thrash about nearly enough. WAY TOO much slow, creepy walking. Remember how swiftly King Taijitu, Giant Nevermore, and Giant Deathstalkers move when they're fighting? They move like living, furious beasts instead of shambling, distracted zombies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-29-2018, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T17:37:10-08:00","id":1271882,"title":"","content":"well, there in we have the biggest problem with V4 and 5. The action was not as exciting or well executed as previous seasons. Which is understandable, since it seems Monty was the action guy for the show. People said there wasn't enough action, but there was just as much as before, it just sucked. And it seems RT did figure that out too because this season they hired a guy just to choreograph the fight scenes. And it shows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T18:46:17-08:00","id":1271900,"title":"","content":"Yes, things seem to have greatly improved. The fight against the Sphinx was much better than the fight against the Petra Gigas, let alone the Nuckelavee.<br /> <br /> So far I can't think of a single area in which Volume 6 isn't better than Volumes 4-5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T21:17:02-08:00","id":1271917,"title":"","content":"I think the lack of Ilia isn't an improvement, but otherwise...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T01:11:35-08:00","id":1271932,"title":"","content":"The choreography on the Nuckelavee fight wasn't the greatest, but as an enemy it managed to overcome how utterly unthreatening the Grimm have been to me since the end of Volume 2 and the technical limitations didn't create storytelling problems like the Battle of Mistral did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T08:11:14-08:00","id":1271978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1271932#post1271932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The choreography on the Nuckelavee fight wasn't the greatest, but as an enemy it managed to overcome how utterly unthreatening the Grimm have been to me since the end of Volume 2 and the technical limitations didn't create storytelling problems like the Battle of Mistral did.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the Petra Gigas?<br /> <br /> There were definitely problems with that fight, but the threat the Grimm posed seemed real enough, and comparable. The principle difference is that Ren went berserk against the Nuckelavee and threw off their teamwork, and Jaune having a weapon this time was not enough to offset that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T17:31:17-08:00","id":1272082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1271882#post1271882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, there in we have the biggest problem with V4 and 5. The action was not as exciting or well executed as previous seasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not at all the biggest problem with V4 and V5. I mean, it was absolutely <i>a</i> problem, but not <i>the</i> biggest problem. The biggest problem was the writing. Four was awkward as hell, and I'll be blunt about five: Miles and Kerry should be ashamed of it. Its problems are deeply baked into the structure. It would still have been the worst volume even if the fights had been orgasm-inducingly good. The Raven plotline alone is so jaw-droppingly dumb I can't even.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T19:16:30-08:00","id":1272103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1271978#post1271978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the Petra Gigas?</div> </div> </div> </div>The tone still felt more like something from one of the earlier volumes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T21:59:55-08:00","id":1272123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1272103#post1272103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tone still felt more like something from one of the earlier volumes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably owing to the fact that it was slower and clumsier than Grimm which are naturally that size.<br /> <br /> The Petra Gigas' strength was in endurance. It was capable of ignoring or negating any damage they inflicted on its golem-body, such that it could eventually wear its prey down. Elder Grimm instead have the speed to be a bigger immediate threat.<br /> <br /> Since Team RNJR had the ability to completely break its body and leave it defenseless, and then kill it before it escaped, its strengths didn't avail it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T01:33:05-08:00","id":1272141,"title":"","content":"A major thing that the Nuckelavee has going for it as an enemy is that it's probably pretty infamous. It's played a role in the destruction of three settlements and hasn't left the general area in at least a decade. There's no way it's not crossed paths with fully trained Huntsmen (besides the one that Team RNJR found dying) it apparently came off best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T10:56:37-08:00","id":1272208,"title":"","content":"Today's chapter was another whopper.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">We finally get to see Mile's favorite Grimm. The ones that are weak, but terrifying in packs.<br /> <br /> No speed, no strength, but they're tough, and they constantly generate a frequency that induces apathy and lethargy in any human or faunus who hears them. When they strain themselves, they can blast the wavelength out to weaken their prey.<br /> <br /> Blake seemed especially affected, though she was also the one closest to them for that last blast.<br /> <br /> Even the most experienced huntsman is easy prey when he's too tired to care about keeping his Aura protection active. The Apathy Grimm don't need strength to kill you with their claws then. In fact, they don't even need to touch you; you'll slowly waste away on the ground in their presence.<br /> <br /> Someone pointed out that this proves Grimm don't FEED on negative emotions. These Grimm prevent you from feeling ANYTHING; that's why Bartleby thought to use just two of them to take the edge off of his family and workers, to make everyone less attractive to other Grimm.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T13:24:23-08:00","id":1272225,"title":"","content":"not a First member so a week behind. <br /> <br /> Loved the Neo-Cinder fight. Interesting Cinder held back. Wonder if she felt bad...nah. Probably thought Neo could be talked down and usefull.<br /> <br /> Oh, and that song is awesome. MAy have a new second favorite RWBY soundrack song.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T15:45:40-08:00","id":1272246,"title":"","content":"Do you figure Exalted can support an entire Cane-Fu martial arts Style?<br /> <br /> Do you think there\u2019s room for an umbrella Charm that lets you negate grappling throws and other knockback effects?<br /> <br /> <br /> What about the chapter 1 fight with the Sphinx and Manticores? Would you model all of the Manticores as a battle group that everyone but Qrow was fighting while he was busy with the Sphinx? Or would you have each player fight their own Manticore?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T18:09:44-08:00","id":1272275,"title":"","content":"I think the umbrella c