atar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T21:17:47-08:00","id":1272299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1272297#post1272297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note: is there a name for a Cinder/Neo ship?</div> </div> </div> </div>Currently? I'd go with &quot;Sleep With One Eye Open&quot;.<br /> <br /> Though there's always &quot;Cosplay Competitors&quot;, after their dress-up arms-race in previous Volumes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T23:19:40-08:00","id":1272315,"title":"","content":"There seems to be a small calling for something like melted icecream on that pairing as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T23:59:55-08:00","id":1272322,"title":"","content":"Looked that up, it has been in use for at least 10 months. Not surprising, I think every possible pairing on that show has a ship.<br /> <br /> I am shipping these two now though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T00:44:13-08:00","id":1272333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1272322#post1272322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looked that up, it has been in use for at least 10 months. Not surprising, I think every possible pairing on that show has a ship.<br /> <br /> I am shipping these two now though.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also one that views the pairing as called Fire and Ice cream. Though I'll need to see more interaction between Neo and Cinder before I start putting stock in that pairing, since I personally prefer Chaos Emerald (Cinder/Emerald) for the time being. *<br /> <br /> <br /> *Though I am totally willing to support an Emerald/Neo ship solely based on it apparently being called Mint Chocolate chip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T01:28:32-08:00","id":1272338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1272275#post1272275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the umbrella ccharmyou describe should be an evocation of the weapon</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We have that artifact umbrella in Arms as a basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T19:03:47-08:00","id":1272508,"title":"","content":"I'm still not sure how anybody gets that the gods are &quot;alien&quot; or &quot;wise&quot; or &quot;beyond human comprehension&quot;. They both seem quite human to me. From moment one, the allegedly less dickish of the pair was more concerned about being respected by his creations than being decent to them.<br /> <br /> They played tug-o-war with a good man's soul while squabbling like children, destroying and recreating Oz a good half-dozen times, and then..<br /> <br /> Act 1:<br /> <br /> ShinyGod: Hey Salem, remember how I talked a big game about life and death being a delicate balance which cannot be screwed with? I lied; you're immortal now, explicitly so you can't join your true love until you learn the lesson I want you to. Behold my compassion.<br /> <br /> Salem: So you CAN and WILL make people immortal?<br /> <br /> ShinyGod: Oh yeah, I just resent being told to do it on command. See ya!<br /> <br /> Act 2:<br /> <br /> GloomyGod: Lookit that, the problem we created came back to bite us in the ass - but not like, meaningfully, it's just kind've annoying. Time to destroy everyone in the world *but* Salem for Salem's temerity.<br /> <br /> ShinyGod: I can and will repeatedly bring people back to life, but nah, that seems about right.<br /> <br /> Act 3:<br /> <br /> ShinyGod: Hey Oz, remember how I talked a big game about life and death being a delicate balance which cannot be screwed with?<br /> <br /> Oz: No?<br /> <br /> ShinyGod: Well I did, and I lied. You have to go back.<br /> <br /> Oz: Nah, I'd rather stay here and wait for Salem.<br /> <br /> ShinyGod: She's not coming, for um, some reason. Anyway, I'm gonna make you immortal, but in a way that fucks with the minds of random strangers. Behold my compassion. <br /> <br /> <br /> Oz: Sounds legit, sure.<br /> <br /> ShinyGod: Oh, also, here are four neat toys - don't bring them together until you achieve world peace or we'll destroy the entire world.<br /> <br /> Both of these fucksticks are abusive parents that make Old Testament Yahweh look chill and composed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T21:10:08-08:00","id":1272531,"title":"","content":"Yup, wanna take my Dire Lance and smack them both in the ethereal crotch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T01:03:59-08:00","id":1272559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1272508#post1272508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both of these fucksticks are abusive parents that make Old Testament Yahweh look chill and composed.</div> </div> </div> </div>...They're acting pretty standard fare for this type of comparison, actually.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T03:37:12-08:00","id":1272566,"title":"","content":"all gods are dicks. Which is why I think the Klingons had the right idea killing theirs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T06:00:06-08:00","id":1272590,"title":"","content":"One important thing about the gods and Remnant: Whatever endgame involving humanity and the gods they get, Grimm will be a part of it. Grimm are not some kind of punishment to humans or anything of the sort. They're the dark god's response to the shit the light god keeps making.<br /> I doubt whatever end the series has won't involve them somehow, but I totally see potential in the &quot;fuck these two assholes let's throw the relics on the sun and keep going with our lives&quot; scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T06:00:35-08:00","id":1272591,"title":"","content":"Never got an answer.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to run the Sphinx and Manticore battle on the train in Exalted, would you model the Manticores as individuals for each non-Qrow player character, or as a single battle group that fights and is fought by everyone but Qrow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T06:03:31-08:00","id":1272593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1272591#post1272591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never got an answer.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to run the Sphinx and Manticore battle on the train in Exalted, would you model the Manticores as individuals for each non-Qrow player character, or as a single battle group that fights and is fought by everyone but Qrow?</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't see the question before :x<br /> <br /> That model seems appropriate. I wouldn't exempt qrow from being attacked if I judged the battle group covered his position, but it doesn't change anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T06:12:57-08:00","id":1272598,"title":"","content":"We never saw a Manticore engage Qrow after the Sphinx joined the fight, though he killed at least one before it did.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, we did see Yang grapple a Manticore by the horns, and I think Blake tangled at least one in her ribbon. Grappling individuals of a battle group isn\u2019t mechanically allowed.<br /> <br /> Battlegroups are good for modeling when multiple characters are each being attacked by multiple opponents, but none of the students ever seemed to fight more than one Manticore at a time, so I can see a case where each Manticore is rolled into battle separately. Which allows for characters with grappling attacks to still employ those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T08:04:20-08:00","id":1272622,"title":"","content":"Grappling individuals of a battle group is narratively allowed, though. Yang can stunt her brawl attacks however she likes.<br /> <br /> More to the point, like hell am I keeping track of a dozen mooks that go down in one hit, plus an actual worthy opponent - this is exactly what Battle Groups are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T08:04:28-08:00","id":1272623,"title":"","content":"That's all easily translated as artistic license, unless you intend for every manticore to be a troublesome opponent. They seemed to have little trouble fighting them, the issue was doing that without exploding the passengers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T08:51:02-08:00","id":1272632,"title":"","content":"Also, &quot;not shown&quot; isn't always the same thing as &quot;never happened&quot;. I think we can safely assume that Qrow was being engaged by manticores off-camera (there's no compelling reason why he wouldn't be) but that nothing really came of it because his Parry and Evasion are both ridiculous, and he's capable of slaying these things as morning exercise.<br /> <br /> Remember, earlier he was flanked by two of them and smoked 'em both before they could even really attack him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","user":"Amayad","date":". 12-03-2018, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T03:51:08-08:00","id":1272955,"title":"","content":"This questions isn't just about rwby, but this season and the discussion here is an example:<br /> <br /> If a god/spirit/otherworldly being is supposed to be unknowably alien or incomprehensibly vast beyond our understanding of morality, how are humans meant to learn any lessons on morality from such beings?<br /> <br /> If their views are incomprehensible to us, doesn't that mean we will never be able to meaningfully learn from them?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T10:51:42-08:00","id":1272990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1272955#post1272955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This questions isn't just about rwby, but this season and the discussion here is an example:<br /> <br /> If a god/spirit/otherworldly being is supposed to be unknowably alien or incomprehensibly vast beyond our understanding of morality, how are humans meant to learn any lessons on morality from such beings?<br /> <br /> If their views are incomprehensible to us, doesn't that mean we will never be able to meaningfully learn from them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It depends on the circumstances, but yeah if an entity is so alien that you can't ascribe human morality to it then short of being made like said entity one wouldn't be able to learn its view of morality. Some series get away with the scenario by playing it more towards alien circumstances to things humans can understand. For example &quot;Speaker for the Dead&quot; had a race where part of their growing up involved being ritualistically gutted. This led to a few conflicts owing that one was a result of doing this to a human without knowing that humans work that way and another was a human refusing to gut the alien because the human wasn't aware that this was not a suicide request.<br /> <br /> In other cases its a bit less effective. For example killing people doesn't seem to take much effort for either brother in RWBY, whereas the most effort we see in bringing anyone back was the light brother putting Ozma in the reincarnation cycle , and that's only because he wanted Ozma's permission on the front, to entities like that killing people could be viewed as significantly less immoral than it would be for a human since they could literally undo the fatality. Meaning for them they could view killing and raising a human with the same impact as flicking someone's nose. Granted that doesn't seem to be how it's played in show I'm merely making a point. The thing is entities like that trying to teach the importance of life is a bit tricky considering the entities teaching it are immortal with apparently easy and complete control over life and death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T14:15:40-08:00","id":1273014,"title":"","content":"We can all agree that Salem didn\u2019t value the lives of others as much as she should, and that her own kind would want her to appreciate them more, right?<br /> <br /> That is, none of the original humanity should be happy that she lied to them all to get them to agree to fight gods that had proven they could kill people with a wave of their hands, and provoked the God of Destruction to kill them all?<br /> <br /> We can agree that, after watching the God of Destruction effortlessly No Sell the attack against him and then just as easily wipe out her army, Salem\u2019s response should not have been to threaten to sacrifice another army to them for her own sake? Like, maybe she should have tried pleading with the brothers to bring back the people she had led to their deaths? Or taken any responsibility for it at all?<br /> <br /> Jinn ever said that afterwards, Salem never once blamed herself for what she provoked the gods into doing. Even a righteous person should examine themselves and question if they made a mistake, or they\u2019re only self-righteous by definition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T20:46:02-08:00","id":1273044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1272508#post1272508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both of these fucksticks are abusive parents that make Old Testament Yahweh look chill and composed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Amayad, I like both your jib AND the manner in which you have cut it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We can all agree that Salem didn\u2019t value the lives of others as much as she should, and that her own kind would want her to appreciate them more, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, absolutely. And the hell of it is, that's like... past Salem, who was almost certainly a much more cuddly person who valued human life more than the modern incarnation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We can agree that, after watching the God of Destruction effortlessly No Sell the attack against him and then just as easily wipe out her army, Salem\u2019s response should not have been to threaten to sacrifice another army to them for her own sake? Like, maybe she should have tried pleading with the brothers to bring back the people she had led to their deaths? </div> </div> </div>I can agree with this, yeah, although it's a bit sort of... the kind of person who is going to respond that way is probably the sort of person who doesn't assemble a murder army in the first place, yeah? If Salem actually cared about the army, she would, paradoxically, have probably not assembled it in the first place.<br /> <br /> Like, you can argue that on a purely practical level, regardless of her ACTUAL feelings Salem should have immediately knuckled under to the Gods and told them whatever lies they wanted to hear and attempted to alter her behavior in whatever way they found most congenial in order to get to an out. But that's a practical argument, not a moral one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or taken any responsibility for it at all? </div> </div> </div>This part is tricky, because Salem isn't the only one with agency here. The Gods have it as well, as do the other people involved. Nobody <i>had</i> to sign onto Salem's agenda of &quot;Murder the Gods. Topple their thrones. Steal their power, and make it yours.&quot; She was lying to them, but the lie itself isn't one that really makes you look good for responding to it with &quot;Divine murders to make myself immortal? Oh fuck the hell <i>yes</i>. Sign me up!&quot;<br /> <br /> Similarly, the God of Darkness doesn't really look good for deciding &quot;this pathetic attack, which did not, in fact, pose any kind of threat to me at all, warrants genocide and global disaster as a response.&quot; Whatever else Salem might have done, that's not on her.<br /> <br /> That said, Salem had every reason to expect that even if they won, there would be massive casualties. She knowingly marched people into what was gonna be a slaughter for her own selfish reasons, using lies as a goad, and THAT'S something she absolutely should take responsibility for.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T07:51:47-08:00","id":1273098,"title":"","content":"My point is, the gods aren\u2019t hypocrites for wanting Salem to respect life more than she does, because even her own kind expect that from her, and the gods aren\u2019t asking her to respect life as much as they do. (And neither of them agree on how important life is, to begin with.)<br /> <br /> And how much they respect mortal life is clearly influenced by how easily they can just bring everyone back and make them immortal whenever they feel like it, with any time spent being dead apparently feeling like no time at all to people.<br /> <br /> Ozma had no idea how much time had passed since his last death and the day he was first reincarnated in another person; indeed, he found \u201cdeath\u201d more pleasant than life, given that the first time he was brought back he panicked, and he declined the offer to return to life until he learned the woman he loved was left behind on Remnant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T17:44:34-08:00","id":1273180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1273098#post1273098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is, the gods aren\u2019t hypocrites for wanting Salem to respect life more than she does, because even her own kind expect that from her, and the gods aren\u2019t asking her to respect life as much as they do. (And neither of them agree on how important life is, to begin with.)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but they sure are hypocrites for refusing to bring a man back to life because it would screw with the balance of life and death, then bringing that same man back to life to fix the problem they created.<br /> <br /> Hey, ShinyGod, if you just did that in the first place....<br /> <br /> Beings that actually give a shit about mortal lives do not commit global genocide in a fit of pique, generally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","user":"Amayad","date":". 12-06-2018, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T18:22:07-08:00","id":1273185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1273180#post1273180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but they sure are hypocrites for refusing to bring a man back to life because it would screw with the balance of life and death, then bringing that same man back to life to fix the problem they created.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Light God didn't bring Ozma back to life. He sent his ghost back to cohabit with someone. Apparently, that's different enough to appease his brother.<br /> <br /> If the Light God had done what Salem wanted, then it would have been his brother storming his sanctum to demand he play by the rules.<br /> <br /> And if that didn't happen immediately, then humanity would be storming his pool on their own, demanding that he resurrect all of THEIR loved ones too. Because contrary to what Salem thinks, she's not anyone special who deserved special treatment.<br /> <br /> The Light God had to say No to her the same way he had to say No to everyone else who asked him for the same thing.<br /> <br /> The God of Death might have been willing to act against his own philosophy to gift the first mortal to ever come to him for help, but if Salem had never come to him because his brother had started handing out resurrections, the God of Death would likely take it pretty badly. He already seemed to see the rules he'd agreed to as stacked against him, so his brother breaking the rules to appeal even more to the mortals would surely drive him over the edge.<br /> <br /> Then everyone would die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T18:24:18-08:00","id":1273187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1273180#post1273180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but they sure are hypocrites for refusing to bring a man back to life because it would screw with the balance of life and death, then bringing that same man back to life to fix the problem they created.<br /> <br /> Hey, ShinyGod, if you just did that in the first place....<br /> <br /> Beings that actually give a shit about mortal lives do not commit global genocide in a fit of pique, generally.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair that was the dark brother and he didn't seem to give too much of a crap about it considering his reason for bringing Ozma back boiled down to, &quot;Finally someone comes to me to ask a favor instead of my brother. I've never had worshippers before, what would you like so I may prove that I am way better than my brother. Which, you clearly know since you came here first, but we're proving this to everyone else too.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T18:27:55-08:00","id":1273190,"title":"","content":"Basically, the God of Darkness doesn't much care for rules, so the only way to make him care about the rules is to never break them yourself, lest he has cause to say that the rules mean nothing.<br /> <br /> But because he doesn't care about the rules, he'll glad break them himself on a whim, though his brother can hold him sternly enough to his word that he gives up and toes the line again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1273044#post1273044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This part is tricky, because Salem isn't the only one with agency here. The Gods have it as well, as do the other people involved. Nobody <i>had</i> to sign onto Salem's agenda of &quot;Murder the Gods. Topple their thrones. Steal their power, and make it yours.&quot; She was lying to them, but the lie itself isn't one that really makes you look good for responding to it with &quot;Divine murders to make myself immortal? Oh fuck the hell <i>yes</i>. Sign me up!&quot;<br /> <br /> Similarly, the God of Darkness doesn't really look good for deciding &quot;this pathetic attack, which did not, in fact, pose any kind of threat to me at all, warrants genocide and global disaster as a response.&quot; Whatever else Salem might have done, that's not on her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, agreed. Didn't mean to suggest otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T18:41:50-08:00","id":1273192,"title":"","content":"Though I think Salem did make one heck of a leap from the observed bit that they aren't all knowing to the assumption that it means they aren't omnipotent or close enough that its academic from a mortal perspective.<br /> <br /> Though my current hypothesis is Salem is looking to go for apotheosis by swiping the power of the gods. Makes the most sense if we're operating under the idea that she wants the relics to summon those things as opposed to wanting the relics in places where no one else will ever get them lest the world somehow get a passing grade on judgement day and the gods decide to wipe her out rather than dealing with her being a nuisance in the new world. Plus we had that bug that stole maiden powers in season 3 which so screams lower scale model to me when you've got the brothers in the bleachers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T21:33:14-08:00","id":1273200,"title":"","content":"nah, I think whatever she's trying to do, it has more to do with spiting Oz*** than anything to do with the gods. listen to her monologues. And the lyrics to Divide. It's all directed at Oz*** himself, not just his as an obstacle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T01:22:40-08:00","id":1273240,"title":"","content":"oh seems this episode had an alternate ending :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://i.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/001/436/437/2e7.png\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/001/436/437/2e7.png\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/001/436/437/2e7.png\" target=\"_blank\"> https://i.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/001/436/437/2e7.png </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T02:20:52-08:00","id":1273241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1273185#post1273185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because contrary to what Salem thinks, she's not anyone special who deserved special treatment.</div> </div> </div> </div>But she is held as special and given special treatment by the gods: They casually kill everyone to try to teach her a lesson. No one's life is as important as whether she understands.<br /> If that's not special treatment, what is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T04:06:23-08:00","id":1273245,"title":"","content":"She wasn't anyone special at first. Then she made a bit of an impression on the dark god. <br /> <br /> And recall, <i>he's</i> the one who killed everyone, so he's the one who chose to spare her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T05:48:24-08:00","id":1273249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1273245#post1273245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She wasn't anyone special at first. Then she made a bit of an impression on the dark god. <br /> <br /> And recall, <i>he's</i> the one who killed everyone, so he's the one who chose to spare her.</div> </div> </div> </div>He spared her even earlier than that, when he blasted her and Ozma with dark fire but she was left untouched even as the ground under her was scorched.<br /> <br /> Which is part of what makes me think the God of Light decided that she had become someone special, in a way. <br /> <br /> It is after that that the God of Life stopped her from provoking his brother further and then cursed her with immorality that could only be broken if she accepted the lesson the Older Brother has been trying to teach his Younger Brother this whole time.<br /> <br /> Because maybe it will be more persuasive to the Dark Brother if the lesson comes from the first mortal to approach him, the only mortal to try manipulating him, the mortal who has been as cavalier about others\u2019 lives as he has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T16:31:12-08:00","id":1273347,"title":"","content":"That doesn't really scan for me, Sunder the Gold. From the moment Salem approaches them with her army, the gods more or less act as one. Neither tries to stop the other from killing all of humanity, or leaving, and we are left with the impression that the whole relic-judgment thing is both of them acting together. Both gods will return and judge humanity, not one or the other, both of them.<br /> <br /> But judge humanity on what? Things they don't agree on themselves? Things they are evidently incapable of effectively teaching?<br /> <br /> That's my issue with the unknowable alien thing: They act as though they are examples to humans, but they can't be if they act so inhumanly. And if they're not, the whole judgment aspect falls flat on its face as a story element.<br /> <br /> I think (or hope?) that these conflicts in the story will be discovered by the main characters once they have some time to think things through, and that this will open the path to the Third Option (talk the gods down from their high horse).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T09:36:43-08:00","id":1273591,"title":"","content":"Well, the eponymous character of Episode 7 has just about the coolest new weapon we've seen since season 3 or so. It's very Exalted-like as well! If someone hasn't come up with something similar already, it wouldn't surprise me if it gets homebrew'd soon.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking... White Jade? Magnetism is an aspect of Earth, after all. Although looking at the character as whole, it's very much a Chosen of Endings shtick, which naturally points towards Starmetal, with the two pieces &quot;destined&quot; to meet and part.<br /> <br /> What do you all think?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12013-artex","name":"artex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12013_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T10:34:17-08:00","id":1273594,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure starmetals destiny stuff is usually so literal, but yeah, white jade could fit. I think she was supposed to be using gravity dust in-universe, so earth fits well there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T11:06:39-08:00","id":1273605,"title":"","content":"White jade with moonsilver elements. White jade for gravity and magnetism; moonsilver for changing forms, pair-bonding, and duality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T18:53:59-08:00","id":1273645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1273591#post1273591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the eponymous character of Episode 7 has just about the coolest new weapon we've seen since season 3 or so. It's very Exalted-like as well! If someone hasn't come up with something similar already, it wouldn't surprise me if it gets homebrew'd soon.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking... White Jade? Magnetism is an aspect of Earth, after all. Although looking at the character as whole, it's very much a Chosen of Endings shtick, which naturally points towards Starmetal, with the two pieces &quot;destined&quot; to meet and part.<br /> <br /> What do you all think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's magnetism. There's a purple glow; that's gravity dust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T19:32:11-08:00","id":1273650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1273645#post1273645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's magnetism. There's a purple glow; that's gravity dust.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gravity Dust is surely involved (magnetism wouldn't explain how she could be dragging the Giant Nevermore down towards her inferior mass while she's flying upwards at it), but the sickles clearly show an attraction towards each other that doesn't seem like Gravity alone.<br /> <br /> Gravity alone would be dragging EVERYTHING around a sickle towards it, rather than attracting only the sickle's twin.<br /> <br /> Maria might be using a special combination of Gravity and Magnetism Dust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T23:45:38-08:00","id":1273674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/m_2-TrTBujs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/m_2-TrTBujs\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/m_2-TrTBujs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/m_2-TrTBujs </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T00:37:43-08:00","id":1273681,"title":"","content":"The sickles attract each other alone through gravity because dust can do shit like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T07:31:49-08:00","id":1273714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1273347#post1273347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't really scan for me, Sunder the Gold. From the moment Salem approaches them with her army, the gods more or less act as one.</div> </div> </div> </div>People with different opinions and priorities, when they have come to an agreement, can present a united front to a third party.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Neither tries to stop the other from killing all of humanity </div> </div> </div>That's an odd statement to make, as it supposes the God of Creation would ever consider destroying them. Either in person or in Qrow's story, the elder brother has never once destroyed anything, only fought his brother to make him stop destroying things.<br /> <br /> It ignores how the Light God hung his head in sorrow before his brother killed them all. And how he talked about it to Ozma, &quot;A tragedy has befallen your people, at the hands of my brother.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's also really old for people to keep ignoring every time I've pointed out the fact that the older brother has never been able to protect his creations from his brother. Remember Qrow's story? The brothers are too evenly matched for the older brother to fight his sibling AND protection his creations. When he created things, his brother destroyed them. It was only when the creator god neglected to create anything new that he attacked his brother. Possibly for two reasons.<br /> <br /> First, the brothers seemed to need to rest after a round of creation or destruction. So after the dark god destroyed his things for the last time, the older brother attacked when he was tired.<br /> <br /> Second, a clash between the god of destruction and his equally powerful brother would probably destroy anything in existence as collateral damage, so after the younger brother finished destroying everything, the older brother had nothing left to protect to hold him back.<br /> <br /> The entire reason humanity exists is because the older brother used his position of dominance as grounds to sue for peace and compromise. The whole reason humanity was allowed to continue existing, and why the planet still exists, and why humanity is given a second chance, is because the older brother honors his compromise with his brother enough that his brother remains willing to compromise in return.<br /> <br /> If the light god had tried to stop his brother from killing their rebellious creations, his brother wouldn't stop without a fight. A fight that would destroy the planet AND the agreement to ever allow there to be a planet again.<br /> <br /> <br /> Can you at least try to understand the two gods in terms of Cold War USA and Russia? How they agreed to peace on the table, but under it they were competing through proxies to see whose ideals stood up to the test? Did the USA and Russia need to agree on anything, or have the same character and values and priorities, or were they able to be completely different and still agree that they didn't want Nuclear War?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or leaving </div> </div> </div>Assuming that either one of them wanted to remain, neither one would allow the other to be the only remaining god on Remnant. That wouldn't be fair in their agreement.<br /> <br /> The older brother wouldn't want his brother to stay and keep breaking the place, and the younger brother wouldn't want his brother to stay and fix the place.<br /> <br /> Because they're DIFFERENT from each other.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and we are left with the impression that the whole relic-judgment thing is both of them acting together. </div> </div> </div>So why wasn't the younger brother present to talk to Ozma?<br /> <br /> Don't include me in &quot;we&quot;. MY impression is that the dark god who just wiped out humanity is perfectly happy to be done with the whole business of creation, which he saw as disgusting from the beginning and needed to be convinced to try.<br /> <br /> MY impression is that the judgment is the Light God's attempt to give humanity a second chance, and while his younger brother is compromising enough to give him that chance, he's not happy about it. He's sulking, somewhere out of sight where no one can see him pout.<br /> <br /> I also get the impression that he feels humanity will fail the second chance just like they failed the first, so that he can come back and destroy them as his brother had agreed to allow him to do in their mutual compromise. Or the Dark God thinks that Ozma won't be enough to save humanity from Salem and his Grimm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But judge humanity on what? Things they don't agree on themselves? </div> </div> </div>That's the entire point, isn't it?<br /> <br /> If humanity chooses the Light God's way, then the Light God wins and they get to live. They proved him right, and he wins the bet he made with his brother.<br /> <br /> If humanity chooses the Dark God's way, then the Dark God wins and he gets to destroy them. They proved him right, and he wins the bet he made with his brother.<br /> <br /> Because the Light God and Dark God want different things, and they only have peace because they compromised.<br /> <br /> Why don't you understand compromise between people who want different things? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Things they are evidently incapable of effectively teaching? </div> </div> </div>One failure out of one attempt is insufficient evidence.<br /> <br /> Salem had choices, and even the best teachers can't MAKE anyone learn anything.<br /> <br /> Haven't you heard about how you can lead a horse to water, but can't make her drink?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They act as though they are examples to humans </div> </div> </div>I don't see HOW, except that each brother wants to be a different example.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T07:39:57-08:00","id":1273715,"title":"","content":"LG: &quot;Honestly, I was expecting the whole &quot;Immortal til you learn a lesson&quot; thing to take a century or two, tops.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T10:23:29-08:00","id":1273749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1273715#post1273715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">LG: &amp;quot;Honestly, I was expecting the whole &amp;quot;Immortal til you learn a lesson&amp;quot; thing to take a century or two, tops.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Learning her lesson certainly would have taken less effort than repeatedly trying to kill herself and then convincing the kingdoms of her world to kill the gods.<br /> <br /> Salem and many of her modern minions are model lessons of the importance of Mounty Oum\u2019s credo of \u201cKeep Moving Forward\u201d.<br /> <br /> Salem kept trying to return to the past before Ozma died, and so she became stuck. Rather than making what she could out of life constructively, she kept tearing the world apart in her efforts to turn back the clock.<br /> <br /> Ruby accepted that her mother was dead. Blake accepted that the White Fang had strayed from its righteous path. Yang accepted that her arm was gone and that she had been given the best prosthetic available. Weiss accepted that she could not be both the heiress to her father\u2019s company and a free huntress.<br /> <br /> Ruby could have lived in denial. Blake could have stayed with the White Fang or stayed out of its way. Yang could have given up. Weiss could have surrendered to her father to try and win back her inheritance.<br /> <br /> But they accepted what everyone else has to accept. You lose loved ones, limbs, precious things, and sometimes things and people and organizations change, and that change can be terrible.<br /> <br /> You can\u2019t turn back the clock; you can\u2019t fight Time any more than Salem could fight the gods.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe could waste our lives away; but if they were here they\u2019d say: Go forward, you must keep pressing on.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T23:18:10-08:00","id":1273844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1273650#post1273650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gravity Dust is surely involved (magnetism wouldn't explain how she could be dragging the Giant Nevermore down towards her inferior mass while she's flying upwards at it),</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, this is RWBY we're talking about. Dust, Aura, and Semblances sort of make physics their bitch. People do things their mass and velocity absolutely shouldn't allow without them losing limbs or turning into wet red smears ALL the time, and a lot of the technology is basically &quot;this is magic, because of dust.&quot;<br /> <br /> Something we haven't talked a lot about here... speculation about dust and it's nature. Someone correct me if I'm wrong, but it seems quite likely that dust is the literal dust of the first world, right? The world where magic was abundant and lived in everything, all the time? The dust of the first world remains in the second world (&quot;man, born from dust&quot; takes on a different meaning now) and can be harnessed to give them a semblance of the power they once enjoyed in the first world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but the sickles clearly show an attraction towards each other that doesn't seem like Gravity alone. </div> </div> </div>Could be. The show doesn't get into weapon porn as much as we'd like; the names of the girls weapons haven't even been uttered in three out of four cases. Given the plot device powers of dust, I'm actually uncomfortable going further than &quot;Maria's weapon glows with the color we associate with Gravity dust, and thus, given its observed characteristics on top of that, probably makes use of AT LEAST that kind of dust.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Either in person or in Qrow's story, </div> </div> </div>To be fair, at this point we have to regard EVERYTHING in Qrow's story as absolutely unreliable until confirmed by either our own eyes or a reliable third party. Because Qrow clearly got that from Oz, and Oz isn't reliable about <i>shit.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If humanity chooses the Light God's way, then the Light God wins and they get to live. They proved him right, and he wins the bet he made with his brother. </div> </div> </div>They get to live right up until the point where they do something that the Dark God decides justifies wiping them out again. The Dark God was &quot;happy&quot; to live by the terms of their first compact right up until the point where humanity did something that he viewed as sufficient justification for genocide. Perhaps the Gods have agreed to bind themselves in some way that whoever &quot;wins&quot; this final round can't ever go backsies, similar to the Yozi surrender oaths or the geases built into the Gods of Creation... but man, I wouldn't bet money on that.<br /> <br /> An explicit part of the whole Relic deal is that if humanity is judged and found &quot;worthy,&quot; then the Gods will return to Remnant <i>and live there</i>. The Light God says that flat out.<br /> <br /> That's fuckin' <i>terrifying</i>. The genocidal madman gets to return to the scene of his crime and set up shop? What happens if another version of Salem arises and has a go at him, a probability that likely rises to 1:1 on a long enough timeline? What happens if humanity changes such that the Dark God decides they no longer live in harmony with each other, something ELSE whose probability likely rises to 1:1 on a long enough timeline? And who the fuck judges that anyway? Do they both have to agree? If so, what's stopping the Dark God from always voting &quot;no&quot; on spurious grounds no matter what?<br /> <br /> Destroy a Relic. No; actually, ask Jinn if destroying a Relic will reduce the chances the Gods ever return to Remnant, and then go from there. (Although Jinn can't be regarded as wholly trustworthy, because there's a decent chance her knowledge derives directly from the Gods and serves their ends.) Humanities goal should be to keep the Dark God as far away from them as possible for as long as possible, and to certainly never, <i>ever</i> be judged by him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blake accepted that the White Fang had strayed from its righteous path... You can\u2019t turn back the clock; </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure Blake and the White Fang are the best example here. Blake uses explicitly redemptive and reclamatory language (&quot;we're going to take it back&quot;) and literally busts out the old White Fang banners. What is that if not looking at what the White Fang has become, deciding &quot;no; the past version was better&quot; and then deciding to reclaim it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T00:28:05-08:00","id":1273847,"title":"","content":"Anyone else looking forward to Saffron on Chibi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T01:53:37-08:00","id":1273852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1273847#post1273847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else looking forward to Saffron on Chibi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that'll be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T11:02:24-08:00","id":1273910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1273847#post1273847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else looking forward to Saffron on Chibi?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's this now? Did they drop a new episode, or announce Saphron would be in a future one? She'd be the first post-Beacon character used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T12:50:22-08:00","id":1273934,"title":"","content":"no, but I cant imagine her not being used. too much comedy potential there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T03:37:58-08:00","id":1274165,"title":"","content":"and now, a little discussion on forshadowing<br /> <br /> back in Season 3, when Ozpin asked Pyrra about what fairy tales she remembered, she named 3. &quot;the tale of the two brothers, the shallow sea, the girl in the tower..&quot;<br /> <br /> now, notice: <br /> <br /> the Two Brothers<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/rwby/images/f/fc/V6_03_00029.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/250?cb=20181117165619\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> the girl in the tower<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/rwby/images/3/3f/Salem_Human_V6_02_ProfilePic.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/500?cb=20181110220645\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> so, will the Shallow Sea be something important? Or won't they go the 'all the legends are true&quot; route?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T21:30:28-08:00","id":1274493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1273749#post1273749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Learning her lesson certainly would have taken less effort than repeatedly trying to kill herself and then convincing the kingdoms of her world to kill the gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, though, those gods are monsters and absolutely deserved to be killed. The only really awful thing she did in the first iteration of earth was fail to have a thorough enough plan to kill them, allowing them to genocide humanity.<br /> <br /> But I'm with the posters above who opine that the God of Darkness would have murdered humanity eventually anyway and that Salem's assessment of them (that their casual indifference to human life in favor of their idiotic deals with each other meant they were monsters) was entirely correct. The way he talks about learning from this version gives me the impression that the gods have gone through this cycle - callously create sentient being, then casually genocide them when they rebel or don't turn out exactly the way the gods prefer - several times already. They need to be stopped.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can\u2019t turn back the clock; you can\u2019t fight Time any more than Salem could fight the gods.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe could waste our lives away; but if they were here they\u2019d say: Go forward, you must keep pressing on.\u201d </div> </div> </div>That's ridiculous - you can't have it both ways. Either fighting an unwinnable fight for a better future is moving forwards, or it isn't. <i>Salem</i> is the one who is moving forwards (trying to make a better world without the gods after recognizing that they're flawed, monstrous beings.) <i>Ozpin</i> is the one who is stuck in a loop, desperately trying to win them back and restore the earth to whatever dumb vision they had for it rather than pushing for a new path.<br /> <br /> Salem was <i>100%</i> correct to try and kill the gods. I would have done it in her place, and I hope the rest of the cast eventually recognizes that she was right (even if her motivations were, yes, somewhat driven by personal emotions), uses the relics to summon the gods, then kills them to prevent them from repeating their actions anywhere else.<br /> <br /> What has Salem actually <i>done</i>, villain-wise?<br /> <br /> We know for a fact, note, that she <i>is not</i> the force behind the Grimm (they were active in the second world even when she was a recluse who showed no interest in anything) - she's able to exert some limited control over them due to dipping in the God of Darkness' pool, but they serve the God of Darkness, not her, and all their crimes are his, not hers. Up until then everyone assumed she was the Grimm Big Bad, but this season has confirmed that that's the God of Darkness (even if he left them to their own devices, he's still the one who created and 'programmed' them.)<br /> <br /> She lied to people to get them to kill the gods. This was justifiable given the monstrosity and vicious callousness that the gods displayed; and her argument was <i>not wrong</i> (the only real lie was that she'd &quot;stolen&quot; immortality rather than being cursed with it. Her argument that the gods want people to suffer and die is 100% correct, and she witnessed this firsthand.)<br /> <br /> She tried to unite the world by force. That's the only really <i>terrible</i> thing she did in the backstory, but even then, it puts her on-par with, well, just about anyone else who founded a nation. None of the existing nations in Remnant just &quot;happened&quot;, after all. And even then, it was at least notionally for the greater good.<br /> <br /> She rejected the gods - note that Ozpin bafflingly treats <i>this</i> as her great sin, which I am 100% against and was the moment Ozpin flipped firmly and permanently into &quot;misguided villain&quot; category for me. Did he miss the part where the God of Darkness committed casual genocide, while the God of Light looked on? Does he just... not care, that these gods murdered everyone he knew and loved? Seriously, what the fuck, Ozpin. You're a monster hunter. They are monsters. <i>Do your thing</i>, don't just start bowing and scraping because the God of Darkness is slightly stronger than a typical Grimm.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, let's weigh what the gods did. They tormented Salem and Ozpin for no reason beyond their stupid, arbitrary rules. They cursed Salem to an <i>eternity of torment</i> just because she loved someone so much that she was willing to tell a white lie - an entirely innocent one, hurting nothing except the God of Darkness' pride - in a desperate effort to save him. Oh, and when his pride was mildly hurt a second time, the God of Darkness <i>murdered an entire planet of humans</i>, so there's that.<br /> <br /> Modern-day Salem is doing a lot of other awful stuff (she's clutching the villain ball pretty damn hard), but nothing she does is anywhere remotely close to the monstrous acts committed by the God of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Remember - it's easy for viewers to forget this, because we were misled into think Salem was some sort of Queen Grimm up until now - <i>most of the things that suck in Remnant are not her fault</i>. The God of Darkness created the Grimm. He's the reason they run around murdering people. He's the reason Remnant is a horrible place right now. All of it is his decisions. No, she's not responsible for what the God of Darkness did - there was nothing remotely proportionate. If he'd killed just her army, sure, but he murdered the <i>entire planet</i> and then had the unmitigated villainous <i>gall</i> to try and blame her and guilt-trip her. After murdering an entire planet of people. Just to make her feel <i>sad</i>. And the God of Light is, obviously, just as bad, since it's patiently obvious he cares more about his brother than anything else - no, creating new humans doesn't fix anything. Human lives are not a commodity.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I was both shocked and annoyed when his storytime ended and the thing that people were upset over was that he hadn't told them that Salem was immortal, rather than the fact that Ozpin is a horrifying infernalist worshiping and serving a pair of genocidal Yozi, with the explicit goal of summoning them back so they can eradicate humanity (<i>again</i>) if they're unworthy.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the more I type, the more sure I am - <i>fuck Ozpin</i>. Salem has the moral high ground over him. Yes, even present-day chewing-the-scenery cackling-anti-humanity Salem. <i>She's</i> the one who is moving forwards. She's the one who recognized that the old ways were broken and who is trying to build a new and better world. Ozpin is a fanatical madman blindly trying to re-summon the god-demons who eradicated human once already, purely out of blind fanatical refusal to recognize their true nature or to understand that the world needs to move past them (and, if necessary, work out a way to actually defend against them or kill them for good.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1273098#post1273098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is, the gods aren\u2019t hypocrites for wanting Salem to respect life more than she does, because even her own kind expect that from her, and the gods aren\u2019t asking her to respect life as much as they do. (And neither of them agree on how important life is, to begin with.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If the gods actually had the slightest conception of the value of life themselves, the God of Darkness would have long ago committed suicide out of guilt. They were pontificating in an effort to make Salem feel guilty - but it was all vapid, meaningless babble. The God of Darkness <i>murdered</i> Ozpin. Right in front of her. In retribution for a <i>petty slight to his pride</i>. People die because they want them to die. People stay dead because they decided the rules require that they stay dead. Lives, according to them, have whatever value the demon-tyrants who forged it say it does; by their logic, parents can murder their children with impunity and it's sinful to object, and so on.<br /> <br /> If the gods had the <i>slightest</i> understanding of the value humans place on life - even the smallest, tiniest glimmering of it - they would have instantly understood why Salem lied to them to try and get Ozpin revived, and would have forgiven it. Only a monster (or a being so profoundly convinced of its absolute moral superiority that it is essentially a monster) could understand the value of human life and still hold Salem responsible for a lie as minor as &quot;I came to you first&quot;, let alone consider it something worthy of <i>eternal punishment</i>.<br /> <br /> They have no moral grounds to speak and absolutely zero moral authority. All they have is power. The idea that either of them have any grounds to lecture Salem on anything is morally repugnant, and in her place I would have spat in their faces and called them out as the monsters they are. They wouldn't kill her for it, since that would go against their <i>precious stupid pride</i>, right?<br /> <br /> They are monsters, fullstop. I'd call them the only irredeemably evil characters in the series so far (even Ozpin, the third-most evil character after them, seems to be more driven by misguided fanaticism; and most of the other &quot;evil&quot; characters seem more insane than anything else. The brothers commit casual genocide, over petty slights, with full understanding of what it means and without a hint of compunction, and give every indication of having done this before.) And I'd consider any ending that doesn't have them at least called out, if not fought and killed, to be utter tripe.<br /> <br /> Also, aside, just a bit of added assholery I just noticed from the God of Light: When speaking to Ozpin, he blames his brother for killing everyone. But in the context of the scene where it happened, it's pretty obvious he agreed with that measure (at least, he raises no objections and makes no effort to stop it - we know the gods can cancel each other out, and I'd imagine &quot;kill every human in the world&quot; would be a pretty big disruption to his precious <i>fucking</i> balance if it actually meant anything beyond &quot;do what we say or we'll hurt you.&quot;) So Ozpin's quest is fundamentally based on a lie - he's probably convinced that one god is evil and one god is good, without realizing that both are genocidal monsters. It's pretty appropriate for him to have his entire life and quest based on a lie given how much he lies to others, granted, but it's just one last bit of petty horribleness that stuck out for me.<br /> <br /> And one final observation: At least now we know why Ozpin is so reluctant to tell people the full story and why so many people betray him when they find out. &quot;My goal is to summon a pair of super-demons who will judge humanity and then genocide us if they don't like what they see, or rule over us like immortal tyrants if they do&quot; is <i>probably</i> not something that brings out loyalty.<br /> <br /> Oh, and when he was leaving Salem because she wasn't a mindless demon-worshipping fanatic like he is, he tried to kidnap all their kids (which is almost certainly part of the reason she snapped.) Just putting that out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 10-01-2019, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T22:53:46-08:00","id":1274501,"title":"","content":"Weird point, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar517_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"517\" data-vbnamecard=\"517\">Aquillion</a> is Ozpin trying to win the gods back? I mean from what we've got he's the one responsible for the vaults where the relics were stored ie ensuring that no one could bring them together. After that well the condition to not get exterminated when the brothers come back is to be better than the world they killed all the humans on it and well trying to make the world a better place isn't a bad objective regardless. Now whether or not he'd bring the brothers back at the end is an unknown, though I imagine he's debated both options and at least once whether it would be worth it to see if he could bring them back and convince them that it isn't time for judgement day but Salem is proving far too effective an obstacle to verify whether or not it would be possible to make a world they might not slaughter.<br /> <br /> Also as for the why not tell his story to people? The main points are, she's his ex, they actually did try the conquer the world in a storm of blood scenario ages back before a difference in opinion led her to kill him, she's got perfect immortality, and he's asked the nigh all-knowing artifact how to destroy her and the answer was literally, &quot;You can't.&quot; Those aren't exactly elements to your backstory that inspire faith and confidence even if people don't tend to defect to side of the immortal super mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T23:42:05-08:00","id":1274505,"title":"","content":"My reading was that the difference in opinion was literally her saying &quot;the gods have abandoned us, so we need to make a new, better world&quot; and him saying &quot;no, we need to try and return things to the way they used to be&quot;, ie. his intention to summon the gods and her rejection of that was what made them split. I read his horrified reaction as being theocratic in nature (ie. he finally understood that she no longer cared about his gods and couldn't deal with it.)<br /> <br /> Both of them agree that they want a better world, they just disagree on what &quot;better&quot; looks like - Salem wants a world that was better than it was before, with the two of them becoming better leaders than the gods <i>(</i><i>not fucking hard</i><i>)</i>, while Ozpin wants to try and force the world back to what it was when the gods were still around by &quot;earning redemption&quot; from them. In Exalted terms, she's a Solar Exalt and he's a loyalist Infernal.<br /> <br /> (Also I do recognize that some parts of what I'm saying are <i>very obviously</i> not what the authors wanted us to take from it. I think they're incompetent and are aping certain real-world stories - biblical floods, etc. - without understanding the mindset of absolute, unquestioning religious belief that makes them work, which clearly doesn't apply to their shiny glowing mass-murderers. We're supposed to accept that their big glowy demon-kings had the right to exterminate humanity Because Disobedience and Because Sin, and therefore we're supposed to be cheering on Ozpin's desire to grovel before the demons that genocided humanity once already. They haven't been subtle about giving Salem big obvious &quot;THIS IS A VILLAIN&quot; signals. And they're probably going to have her trying to inexplicably wipe out humanity because EVIL, and this is different from the God of Darkness because, uh, he calls himself a god and is really powerful I guess? And also she and a few hundred people she gathered insulted him, even though he was in no real danger, and therefore his murdering an entire planet was her fault? But I don't think it holds together <i>at all</i>. I do seriously mean it when I say I think that the gods are worse than Salem and that Ozpin is a misguided villain willing to eventually risk all of humanity for the sake of his demon-lords - I think the Loyalist Infernal comparison is very apt.)<br /> <br /> This also sort of ties into what I mentioned last season (where Yang went absolutely ballistic about Ozpin giving Qrow the ability to turn into a bird, when the <i>really</i> horrible thing he'd done was keep Salem a secret.) The writers recognize that Ozpin's actions are morally reprehensible and they clearly have &quot;and then people get mad at Ozpin&quot; written in the script, but they're either unable or unwilling to confront the worst parts of Ozpin's deceptions, so people constantly get mad at him for the wrong thing.<br /> <br /> I mean... Salem being immortal isn't really a big deal? Who cares? She's not omnipotent. She can be isolated or sealed or launched into space until she stops thinking or even just convinced to stop.<br /> <br /> The fact that the relics are capable of summoning demon-gods who have exterminated humanity and may do so again when summoned, and that <i>Ozpin, not Salem, is the one who wants to use them this way</i>, is... kind of a much bigger problem. Ozpin's motivation is a much bigger problem, too - basically 'make things the way they were a billion years ago when the god-monsters were around and judging us'. (Yes, he wants to improve the world. But he wants to improve it <i>so he can summon the demon-gods so they can put the world back the way it was before</i>. Again, that was his entire argument with Salem.)<br /> <br /> But they also want this part where people distrust Ozpin to be temporary. So they can't point out the <i>core</i> problems with his actions (since those are basically irreconcilable and turn him into a misguided villain when recognized.)<br /> <br /> I mean I'm not saying &quot;Salem did nothing wrong&quot; - she does want to rule over the world as a god, and they've been handing her constant Villain Ball stuff. I compared her to a Solar Exalt to Ozpin's loyalist Infernal above, and I think that's pretty accurate. But her problems are more with her methods, and... writing-wise, it feels forced? Why does she suddenly decide she wants to rule the world? Where did that come from? She was happy to just live in her hut doing nothing; Ozpin was the one who pulled her out of it. <i>He's</i> the one who had the idea to conquer everything, really.<br /> <br /> It feels like it'd be easier to talk Salem down than it would be to convince Ozpin not to summon his god-monsters. Like, they're both villains, and initially Ozpin is more sympathic because he's mislead and confused by bad theology, while Salem is doing horrible stuff with clearer vision; but Ozpin's <i>motivations</i> are fundamentally worse, and unless he can be convinced that his &quot;gods&quot; are horrific mass-murdering demons (which seems unlikely given that they literally murdered the entire world and he just sort of shrugs), it makes more sense to go to Salem and try to talk to her.<br /> <br /> (In fact, hold on, why are people determined to kill Salem? How, exactly, is she the Big Bad? Taking over the world was <i>Ozpin's</i> goal, not hers, even if she got caught up in the idea. The Grimm aren't her creations; she only controls them incidentally and, as far as we can tell, in a limited fashion, so killing her won't do anything to them. We don't know why she's collecting the artifacts, but based on everything we know, &quot;ensure that Ozpin can never use them&quot; is a very reasonable guess, ie. it's entirely possible she's trying to save the world and Ozpin is trying to destroy it. It feels like some keystone fell out of the plot at some point - how exactly is Salem the villain? She's been attacking academies, and has definitely done some really bad stuff in the service of that, but it was all ultimately only to get at the artifacts, and honestly based on what we know keeping the artifacts away from Ozpin feels like a <i>very good idea</i> - out of all the people on earth, he's the one person who can absolutely never be trusted with them ever, since he seems to at least be notionally willing to entertain the idea of eventually summoning his Evil Genocide Demon-Gods.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 12-15-2018, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T01:50:07-08:00","id":1274518,"title":"","content":"Yeah, see I think you're reading things in that aren't fitting. One, the evil god tyrant thing. Everything we have indicates that they were only in charge to the extent that they existed and people knew they existed. We actually don't have any indication that the brothers excercised any authority over the world if they weren't involved until the dark brother decided to kill the world. Hell even the promise of the relics is that if humanity proves worthy the gods will live among them again. Which they say just means that humanity will be less than they were before they were wiped out, we don't really know what that means beyond maybe the not having access to magic thing. Which only Oz and Salem had seeing how they were remnants of the old world. Granted their kids did end up with it as well, but I'll give the brothers a pass on that as the whole resurrecting Ozma incident did demonstrate that the two are hardly omniscient so entirely likely that .<br /> <br /> Second, that we're supposed to see them wiping the world out as justified. Yeah, I got no clue where you're getting that from, I mean you try to compare it to the biblical flood and that really doesn't work. I mean I've checked with a few religious friends of mine and they agree the great flood isn't supposed to have been seen as a good thing. At best its viewed as having divine justification, but as one of them put it that's really just &quot;I'm God, this is my house and I feel you are all horrible enough to deserve this even if I don't feel happy with having to do it.&quot; So everything I've got says we're not supposed to look at the dark brother wiping out humanity and go, &quot;Yeah that makes sense, they did have it coming.&quot; Especially seeing as how we've all mentioned that there's no indication the attack in question would have worked on either of them if they had chosen to take it. <br /> <br /> Now another point you keep coming back to. Salem not wanting to get the relics together to summon the brothers. We don't know that. We have no answers on why she wants the relics, but we do know she wants them because she's been hunting maidens to steal their powers to steal the relics. Maybe she wants them because they're insanely powerful and she can use them to her own ends to deal with what she feels is a worthy problem, maybe she wants to try smashing them as an f* you to the gods that made them, maybe she's hoping she can somehow leverage a combination to get a relationship councellor to reconcile the problems she and Oz have been having since that break up millenia back, or maybe she wants to summon the gods to try and somehow usurp their power. Basically you can't say Salem's goals are more benevolent than Oz's goals because the only thing we know of her goals is that she made it very clear that her underlings will not like what she does to them if they let their own goals get in the way of Salem getting what she wants. So until we know otherwise you're just making baseless conjecture with the whole, &quot;Salem is the lesser evil because she's just trying to stop Oz from summoning the gods.&quot;<br /> <br /> When did Salem decide she wanted to rule the world? Probably sometime during the rebirth of the world, there's a bit of a gap between Ozma's first reincarnation and all. Or it could just be a side effect of the whole diving into the pool that birthed the Grimm screwing with her head since her initial point to Ozma was just, &quot;Well they are more divided and fighting more than they used to, but I mean we are literally in a godless world. Still I guess if they had direction we could fix it. I mean we're both immortal, both have power beyond anyone else in this world, why not take up the old role of god and guide the people into whatever we want and make the kind of world the old ones couldn't make.&quot; As for the rejection, well no Ozma and Salem didn't break up because she didn't want to summon the old gods again. The first bit of conflict we got was Ozma wanting the world united, but feeling conflicted and guilty about the whole wage war and slaughtering those who want follow them to unite the world. Which Salem argued was completely justified since how else are they going to spread their ideals? The actual break up happened after one of their kids displayed magic and Salem argued Ozma's goal of making the world a better place so they don't get wiped out when judgement day happens gets Salem responding that they shouldn't waste time redeeming humanity and just replace them with a better species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T02:08:19-08:00","id":1274522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1274505#post1274505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reading was that the difference in opinion was literally her saying &quot;the gods have abandoned us, so we need to make a new, better world&quot; and him saying &quot;no, we need to try and return things to the way they used to be&quot;, ie. his intention to summon the gods and her rejection of that was what made them split. I read his horrified reaction as being theocratic in nature (ie. he finally understood that she no longer cared about his gods and couldn't deal with it.)<br /> <br /> Both of them agree that they want a better world, they just disagree on what &quot;better&quot; looks like - Salem wants a world that was better than it was before, with the two of them becoming better leaders than the gods <i>(</i><i>not fucking hard</i><i>)</i>, while Ozpin wants to try and force the world back to what it was when the gods were still around by &quot;earning redemption&quot; from them. In Exalted terms, she's a Solar Exalt and he's a loyalist Infernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>What made Ozpin want to leave with the kids was Salem suggesting that they wipe out all of humanity and repopulate with their family now that they know the gift of magic can be passed down to their children.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ultimately though, I kinda agree that the brother's haven't been written particularly well - or at least, don't meet my particular expectations.<br /> <br /> However; I feel like I don't know enough to really commit to that feeling. From their exchange, I got the impression that the reason the God of Light refused to revive Ozpin was because that would infuriate his brother and likely cause another huge war between them. Remember that the story of the two brothers has persisted so someone passed it on which means Salem must have been aware of the tale prior to deciding to mess with those primal forces. She'd have known about the 'balance' from their tale and elected to ignore it and risk antagonising a God with a vested interest in destroying everything that exists.<br /> <br /> The fact that 'they aren't omnipotent' was a realisation suggests that she previously thought that they were, or at least might have been, so &quot;playing with matches&quot; is about as generous a description you can give her gambit to try and fool the God of Darkness. We can estimate her utter self-interest in this endeavour based on her future actions so I can understand the God of Light's desire to curb that behaviour.<br /> <br /> Remember though, that though they don't say it directly, the God of Light at least implies to Ozpin that there is a hereafter where they can exist after death and if he simply let Salem be killed without dealing with the very obvious seed of chaos she represented then there's the chance she could have raised some hell there too since the Gods seem capable of passing to and fro at will; so for the sake of the whole endeavour he forcibly separates her from the thing she wants (via immortality) to communicate it as a punishment.<br /> <br /> I don't think that was a good idea either, but I'm running with hindsight so I can tell that that doesn't work out well for him. So, until we know more (or the series ends without telling us thus giving us only this information to work with) I don't feel like I can properly discern what his deal is. Is it likely he has some greater plan/knowledge? I sure hope so. What motivates him to send Ozpin back? and why did this not occur until many generations later? What's with the Relics? Why does Ozpin have to bring them together to summon them back - he already knows whats going on in Remnant so it seems kinda silly. I assume he's made some new bargain with his brother but we just don't know enough.<br /> <br /> So yeah, *shrug*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T03:26:00-08:00","id":1274535,"title":"","content":"A thought I had at work tonight...we don't know what Salem's goal is. But in her narrations, she never talks of ruling or destroying humanity. She does talk a lot of defeating Ozpin. And over on his side, Ozpin seems to be more about destroying her than anything to do with his mission.<br /> <br /> What if we're looking at the Vorlons and Shadows all over again. Two great powers fighting it out not for or over the oter, weaker people around them...but really just pissed off at each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T10:07:43-08:00","id":1274582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1274518#post1274518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When did Salem decide she wanted to rule the world? Probably sometime during the rebirth of the world, there's a bit of a gap between Ozma's first reincarnation and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that doesn't fit with what we saw. When Ozpin found her she was a recluse living in a run-down little hut, with no indication that she cared about the outside world. She only started to move and tried to improve the world when <i>he</i> convinced her it was a good idea. And (while he didn't tell her so), his goal was to &quot;improve&quot; humanity so he could summon the gods back and have them judge it, which is a patiently insane thing to want to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, that we're supposed to see them wiping the world out as justified. Yeah, I got no clue where you're getting that from, I mean you try to compare it to the biblical flood and that really doesn't work. I mean I've checked with a few religious friends of mine and they agree the great flood isn't supposed to have been seen as a good thing. At best its viewed as having divine justification, but as one of them put it that's really just &quot;I'm God, this is my house and I feel you are all horrible enough to deserve this even if I don't feel happy with having to do it.&quot; So everything I've got says we're not supposed to look at the dark brother wiping out humanity and go, &quot;Yeah that makes sense, they did have it coming.&quot; Especially seeing as how we've all mentioned that there's no indication the attack in question would have worked on either of them if they had chosen to take it. </div> </div> </div>But my point is, if you strip away the divine justification, the God of Darkness is just an insane mass-murderer who needs to be stopped - he becomes the Big Bad of the setting. There's no easy way around this - you can't murder an entire planet and not be a horrible monster. &quot;Because I created you and this world, and because I'm more powerful than you, I get to decide when it is or isn't justified to murder you all&quot; (basically, &quot;I brought you into this world, so I can take you out!&quot;) <i>is</i> the Biblical-flood justification that I don't think works here. By that reasoning, parents can murder their children, if they are disappointed in them.<br /> <br /> The inhabitants of his world were sentient beings - as soon as the gods created them, they lost the moral right to just kill them on a whim. (And even if you accept that it was &quot;justified&quot; by that ineffectual attack, the images made it clear that the vast majority of humanity had nothing to do with it and were genocided anyway. Every indication is that it had more to do with the God of Darkness' precious bruised pride than with anything else. And maybe another way to torment Salem, which is insane.)<br /> <br /> Once you go down that route, yes, the Brothers are monstrous demon-kings who need to be stopped before they can do that again, and Ozpin starts to look like their Loyalist Infernal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1274522#post1274522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What made Ozpin want to leave with the kids was Salem suggesting that they wipe out all of humanity and repopulate with their family now that they know the gift of magic can be passed down to their children.</div> </div> </div> </div>That wasn't how I interpreted what she said - when she said &quot;replace them and be what they could never be&quot;, I assumed she was talking about the gods, ie. instead of trying to &quot;redeem&quot; humanity so the gods will return, Salem and Oz should just take the gods' places. After all, the context of her saying that was when Ozpin explained the relics and suggested summoning the gods, and her rejecting that plan - it doesn't make sense for her to suddenly leap from that topic to random genocide (when moments ago she'd been focused on ruling humanity.) Based on what we've seen, she's not an utterly immoral monster like the God of Darkness is.<br /> <br /> (It's possible she was &quot;tainted by his evil&quot; or corrupted by his insanity or something by dipping in his pool, but we didn't really see much evidence of that in her actions or unambiguously stated goals elsewhere.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that 'they aren't omnipotent' was a realisation suggests that she previously thought that they were, or at least might have been, so &quot;playing with matches&quot; is about as generous a description you can give her gambit to try and fool the God of Darkness. We can estimate her utter self-interest in this endeavour based on her future actions so I can understand the God of Light's desire to curb that behaviour. </div> </div> </div>Hold on, I just realized something. If (as the dialog implies) she genuinely thought they were omniscient before, that would mean that she <i>didn't intend</i> to deceive the God of Darkness (she would have thought it was impossible!) Her wording, while it implied she'd asked him first, was just an accident on her part, or her trying to be an excessive suck-up (reasonable, given the importance of what she's asking.) That makes his reaction even more unjustified than before!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember though, that though they don't say it directly, the God of Light at least implies to Ozpin that there is a hereafter where they can exist after death and if he simply let Salem be killed without dealing with the very obvious seed of chaos she represented then there's the chance she could have raised some hell there too since the Gods seem capable of passing to and fro at will; so for the sake of the whole endeavour he forcibly separates her from the thing she wants (via immortality) to communicate it as a punishment. </div> </div> </div>Ozpin was literally dead and gave no indication of having experienced this (and he died before the gods decided to genocide humanity and all that, so he would have been there.) But beyond that, I'm not particularly onboard with &quot;we created an afterlife that we never told anyone about, so we're justified in mass-murdering everyone.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think that was a good idea either, but I'm running with hindsight so I can tell that that doesn't work out well for him. So, until we know more (or the series ends without telling us thus giving us only this information to work with) I don't feel like I can properly discern what his deal is. Is it likely he has some greater plan/knowledge? I sure hope so. </div> </div> </div>I don't think he does. Ruby's request was for what he was hiding from them, which means that if he had any important plans or knowledge that he was concealing, it would have been included in the vision. He's just a scared guy trying to get back the world he lost by frantically trying to appease the demon-kings that destroyed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 12-15-2018, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T12:11:50-08:00","id":1274599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1274582#post1274582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that doesn't fit with what we saw. When Ozpin found her she was a recluse living in a run-down little hut, with no indication that she cared about the outside world. She only started to move and tried to improve the world when <i>he</i> convinced her it was a good idea. And (while he didn't tell her so), his goal was to &quot;improve&quot; humanity so he could summon the gods back and have them judge it, which is a patiently insane thing to want to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well no, he was told that humanity wouldn't be whole unless the gods were present in the world. Considering when he came back there was no magic, Grimm were running rampant, there was a new humanity variant in cages, and apparently humanity seemed more willing to kick the crap out of each-other than he recalled. Considering that was the task he was given by the light brother, who even told Ozma flat out that his brother had caused a great tragedy and they were leaving the world as a result, in exchange for being allowed to come back to life and be with his beloved its not unreasonable that Ozma would be inclined towards the deal. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1274582#post1274582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But my point is, if you strip away the divine justification, the God of Darkness is just an insane mass-murderer who needs to be stopped - he becomes the Big Bad of the setting. There's no easy way around this - you can't murder an entire planet and not be a horrible monster. &quot;Because I created you and this world, and because I'm more powerful than you, I get to decide when it is or isn't justified to murder you all&quot; (basically, &quot;I brought you into this world, so I can take you out!&quot;) <i>is</i> the Biblical-flood justification that I don't think works here. By that reasoning, parents can murder their children, if they are disappointed in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>No see here's the problem, first you keep arguing that they're evil and the narrative is saying we're supposed to see them as good and what they did as justified. We're not. He thinks he's justified, but obviously the rest of the world doesn't think so, heck the light brother doesn't think he's justified since we're explicitly shown it giving a look that just screams he knows what's going to happen and hates that it is. Remember as well the dark brother is explicitly mentioned as finding life inherently abhorrent, hence his whole continually destroying everything his brother makes and even making Grimm for purpose of automating the destruction of his brother's creations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1274582#post1274582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inhabitants of his world were sentient beings - as soon as the gods created them, they lost the moral right to just kill them on a whim. (And even if you accept that it was &quot;justified&quot; by that ineffectual attack, the images made it clear that the vast majority of humanity had nothing to do with it and were genocided anyway. Every indication is that it had more to do with the God of Darkness' precious bruised pride than with anything else. And maybe another way to torment Salem, which is insane.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I'd say it has more to do with seeing humanity as a failed project. As far as he was concerned they were created to be a symbol of compromise between himself and his brother and something they could both be proud of. Then one of humanity decided to con him, and then started dragging the rest of humanity into a pointless fight against them whereby they tried to destroy/harm him and his brother. Ineffective as it was at that point he saw them as being pointless once they stopped being a thing he and his brother could be proud of and considering he's only ever seen life as a thing to destroy, well WYSIWYG.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once you go down that route, yes, the Brothers are monstrous demon-kings who need to be stopped before they can do that again, and Ozpin starts to look like their Loyalist Infernal. </div> </div> </div> No, it looks like a being that inherently wants to destroy everything that lives will you know destroy things that live if given a prompt to do so and that the being that liked life wasn't willing to start a forever war that would just end up slaughtering said same beings again and again and again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That wasn't how I interpreted what she said - when she said &quot;replace them and be what they could never be&quot;, I assumed she was talking about the gods, ie. instead of trying to &quot;redeem&quot; humanity so the gods will return, Salem and Oz should just take the gods' places. After all, the context of her saying that was when Ozpin explained the relics and suggested summoning the gods, and her rejecting that plan - it doesn't make sense for her to suddenly leap from that topic to random genocide (when moments ago she'd been focused on ruling humanity.) Based on what we've seen, she's not an utterly immoral monster like the God of Darkness is </div> </div> </div>The exact words were, &quot;Don't you see? None of that matters anymore. Why bother trying to redeem these humans when we could replace them with what they could never be.&quot; The first bit is definitely referring to the task the elder brother gave Ozma, but everything after that is all humans. Also Ozma didn't suggest summoning the gods. He pointed out that he was sent back to make humanity better, so they'd survive the judgement. (The actual line says he told her about the day of judgement he'd been told to prepare for which may imply that Ozma isn't suggesting they bring them back so much as he just believes the brothers are coming back one day.) <br /> <br /> Her focus on ruling humanity, had really been more giving Ozma what she thought he wanted. He was the one having problems with the whole waging war and killing people to spread their message and she was the one pointing out that the message wasn't spreading without a fight and that they should just destroy anyone who wasn't going to accept their words. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (It's possible she was &quot;tainted by his evil&quot; or corrupted by his insanity or something by dipping in his pool, but we didn't really see much evidence of that in her actions or unambiguously stated goals elsewhere.) </div> </div> </div>Jinn's line there is that the pool took an immortal and made her an immortal entity with a desire for pure destruction, though I will agree we don't actually know specifically what that means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hold on, I just realized something. If (as the dialog implies) she genuinely thought they were omniscient before, that would mean that she <i>didn't intend</i> to deceive the God of Darkness (she would have thought it was impossible!) Her wording, while it implied she'd asked him first, was just an accident on her part, or her trying to be an excessive suck-up (reasonable, given the importance of what she's asking.) That makes his reaction even more unjustified than before! </div> </div> </div>Debatable. The lines say she told him that she knew only he could give her back what she lost and carefully avoided mentioning his elder brother, so it could have been an accident with her not mentioning the light in case it cheesed off the dark as easily as it was a deliberate lie of omission. Remember since dealing with an omniscient entity isn't exactly a normal part of the human experience it isn't unreasonable to believe that she may have inadvertently reverted to treating it like a mindset she is used to dealing with. Afterall technically an all knowing entity wouldn't need you to ask for your boon either, since it would know what you wanted well before you came to ask. <br /> <br /> Of course, we've never really been expected to see the younger brother as reasonable, so whether or not Salem accidentally pulled a con isn't changing that much there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ozpin was literally dead and gave no indication of having experienced this (and he died before the gods decided to genocide humanity and all that, so he would have been there.) But beyond that, I'm not particularly onboard with &quot;we created an afterlife that we never told anyone about, so we're justified in mass-murdering everyone.&quot; </div> </div> </div>There does appear to be one. Afterall Ozma asked where he was when the elder brother told him about the task and the elder told him they were between realms. Then when Ozma initially refused the job he requested to go back to the afterlife to be with Salem, to which the elder pointed out that he wouldn't find Salem there. We also don't know that there was never any belief of an afterlife before hand. Most importantly the elder brother doesn't treat the eradication of humanity as something justified, he calls it a tragedy at the hands of his brother.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think he does. Ruby's request was for what he was hiding from them, which means that if he had any important plans or knowledge that he was concealing, it would have been included in the vision. He's just a scared guy trying to get back the world he lost by frantically trying to appease the demon-kings that destroyed it. </div> </div> </div>Aqua, Elkovash was talking about the light brother's plan not Ozma's. That wouldn't have been covered in the request for information. Though I admit it would be amusing if one could use the knowledge relic to dredge up information on the gods and their plans. Also at this point Oz's goal is to stop Salem, since she seems rather bent on wrecking stuff. And regardless of whether or not humanity has the capability to not be found wanting when the gods return, he seems to have concluded that they sure as heck don't with Salem running around doing what she wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T18:20:00-08:00","id":1275216,"title":"","content":"Are we going to see Ruby snap or break down this volume? In the opening, at the end sheblooks worn down. And in show she is clearly reaching her limit with everything going on. Poor thing may not make it to vol 7 with her sanity intact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T21:01:17-08:00","id":1275441,"title":"","content":"I just caught up after a hiatus and I see we're back on the gods. A lot of you hate the gods. I don't. I'm not going to convince any of you though, nor you me, so I'll pass on that front. <br /> <br /> Grim Reaper was sick. The Kama/Hand Scythes were sick, Darth Mauling them was sick. The Apathy was sick. <br /> <br /> I'm still against Silver Eye Protagonist Power. It's to &quot;so spesshul&quot; for me. It's a flat &quot;I Win&quot; button, and even the <i>Legendary Grim Reaper</i> just settles a fight with it it as a OHKO rather than it having an interesting effect/drawback. There seems to be no reason she couldn't just open the fight with that ability since she knows how to do it on cue. It's lame. <br /> <br /> I wanna know more about Cockney Clock B****. Was her 60 second time a super mode? Invulnerability? It seemed like a cool power but we aren't really shown how it works or what it does. <br /> <br /> How did the Cockney Clock gang know where the bird was gonna land? <br /> <br /> What's Grim Reaper's Semblance? Is it related to the Scythe Magnet thing? probably not but still. <br /> <br /> Solid episodes. S6 has rekindled my love for RWBY. <br /> <br /> Oh and as a note on Salem: She quite clearly wanted to conquer the world beneath her Sorcerous heels and instill her magic-capable descendants as the <i><b>Master Race.</b></i> I don't know why people are defending that as &quot;leading the world to a better place&quot;. As a Sorcerous Overlord myself, Yeah, I see how Unbridled Eldritch might over Creation is a gateway drug to megalomania, but let's not ignore the Ubermensch implications of it all. She didn't want to subjugate the lands of Mortals until she knew her kids had access to Magic. She's a Mage Supremacist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T11:59:02-08:00","id":1275586,"title":"","content":"On Twitter and maybe Reddit, Tock\u2019s Semblance is explained as \u201c60 second invulnerability\u201d. Can\u2019t be hurt, but looks like her Aura breaks afterwards. Good ambush assassin Semblance.<br /> <br /> Maria\u2019s Semblance has an audible cue in the fight.<br /> <br /> In the next episode, she calls it Prereflexes. She reacts to things before they happen, like a Spider-Sense. It sounded like it was warning her about the strike to her eyes, but she was disarmed and unable to block or dodge the attack in time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 03-10-2019, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T02:45:35-08:00","id":1275754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1274518#post1274518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Maybe she wants them because they're insanely powerful and she can use them to her own ends to deal with what she feels is a worthy problem, maybe she wants to try smashing them as an f* you to the gods that made them, maybe she's hoping she can somehow leverage a combination to get a relationship councellor to reconcile the problems she and Oz have been having since that break up millenia back, or maybe she wants to summon the gods to try and somehow usurp their power.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's one very, very real possibility that isn't on your otherwise exhaustive list, nalak, and it's the one I personally consider the most probable.<br /> <br /> Maybe Salem wants to pull the trigger. Maybe she wants to watch the world burn, and for the Gods to destroy everything, including her.<br /> <br /> She does, after all, have an appetite for infinite destruction.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T04:36:27-08:00","id":1275762,"title":"","content":"My problem with that is that she has no reason to think they'd kill her when they annihilate the rest of the world. She'd just end up in an empty world again forever.<br /> <br /> My money is on wanting to summon them so she can kill them (an admirably heroic-scale goal, certainly moreso than Ozpin's &quot;Loyalist Infernal&quot; shtick, even if her methods leave something to be desired.)<br /> <br /> I do find my theory that she wants to collect them so Ozpin can't use them to be amusing, though, since that would mean that Ozpin is trying to destroy the world by summoning his demon-gods and she's trying to preserve it. But I doubt that's where the story is going. (Also obviously Ozpin wasn't about to <i>immediately</i> summon his demon-gods, since he's apparently had the power to do so for a while if he's controlled all the artifacts up until now. Though we don't know how they ended up sealed - it's possible that previous Maidens rebelled against him when they learned what he was trying to do and that that's the real reason why the seals require maidens to open, ie. people realized it was insane to trust a fanatic like Ozpin with control over artifacts that can unleash world-destroying demon-gods.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T05:46:51-08:00","id":1275771,"title":"","content":"Then the Maidens wouldn\u2019t seal the Relics in the strongholds of the Wizard\u2019s power and authority, and they would have delivered them to Salem.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re going to flip the script on hero and villain, follow through.<br /> <br /> Which also means that the Wizard\u2019s previous incarnation ruled the world as its emperor after the Great War, the Faunus are thoroughly enslaved for cheap labor, and his next incarnation never gave away any of his magical power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T14:19:27-08:00","id":1275896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1275762#post1275762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with that is that she has no reason to think they'd kill her when they annihilate the rest of the world. She'd just end up in an empty world again forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still her best shot at being destroyed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My money is on wanting to summon them so she can kill them </div> </div> </div>This is possible, but she'd better have a much better plan than she had last time to justify the appalling risk of this move.<br /> <br /> I stand by my assertion that given the information we currently have, the smart play is to query Jinn thoroughly about the potential possibilities and consequences of doing so, and then destroy a relic. That's the safest play.<br /> <br /> I have to admit... zooming out at the meta level, the genocide plot point either has a deeper point to it we're not seeing yet (that is, there's gonna be some point where the cast actually realizes the God of Darkness is deeply evil and the God of Light has only marginal power to restrain him through weird Faustian bargains that he actually can't enforce well, so they need to explore other options) or it was deeply ill-conceived.<br /> <br /> Because if the show wants to follow an arc of &quot;the Gods are summoned back and find humanity worthy and live among it again, and this isn't objectively a terrible thing,&quot; it is going about it the wrong way. Someone is gonna try and bring them back at some point. You do not build a Chekov's Gun that big and never do anything with it unless you're entirely incompetent. And if you don't want the whole &quot;weighed in the cosmic balance&quot; thing to be super fucked, like I said, they're not going about it well.<br /> <br /> From a strict plotting perspective, here's how I would have played it:<br /> <br /> * * *<br /> -The Gods come to be, and war forever in the time before time before coming to their entente cordial. There are two of them, the God of Creation and the God of Destruction, although each also contains within itself a small part of the nature of the other; within Destruction is the desire to watch the universe evolve and move forward, new growth springing from the ashes of the old, and within Creation is the need to ever-create new things and not just fill the world to the brim and then be done forever.<br /> <br /> (If you want to be REALLY outre, you could do it so there are always two Gods, Creation and Destruction, but which one is which at any given time isn't sure. Sometimes the older, more level-headed one is the God of Destruction, and sometimes the younger, less secure, more chaotic one is the God of Creation. But that's not necessary, that's just me thinking out loud.)<br /> <br /> -The First Age of the World, when man arises, the ultimate act of collaboration between the brothers, who grant them both powerful gifts. A Golden Age, not necessarily of peace, but of wonder, magic, and power. The God of Creation is worshiped and is beloved by many, who seek his gifts and favor and understanding. The God of Destruction is shunned, respected and honored but feared; people do not understand his gifts and his powers, and some view them as curses and afflictions.<br /> <br /> -Ozma finds Salem in her tower. They adventure together until his death.<br /> <br /> -Salem approaches the God of Creation. He sympathizes, but tells her that even if he wanted to bring back Ozma, he can't; the domain of death belongs to his brother. He could create something new, but not reach through death to bring back the old.<br /> <br /> -Salem approaches the God of Destruction. Using her cunning, she determines not to simply straight-up ask him for a boon; rather, she presents herself to him as his acolyte, the first ever. The God of Creation has priests and priestesses in their hundreds and their thousands, but she is the first to offer to serve <i>him</i>. He accepts her, and begins to train her in his secret wisdom that she might go forth and teach the world how to better understand him.<br /> <br /> -Salem doesn't give a <i>shit</i> about the God of Destruction or teaching people to understand him and his wisdom. Salem is here to <i>invent necromancy</i>, yo.<br /> <br /> -Which she does.<br /> <br /> -And uses.<br /> <br /> -But both Gods find out, like, the very second she does, because Salem is one of those people who is so clever she shoots her own ass off. She's got her stupid death gate open and is in the process of pulling Ozma out of it (probably blighting the land for miles around and causing untold chaos and destruction) when both Gods show up and shut her down.<br /> <br /> -Salem is cursed. Because the Gods are merciful, and also sort of dumb, for her insane transgressions against nature she's cursed with immortality, to wander the world until she learns her lesson.<br /> <br /> -Salem thinks &quot;Deicide. What a <i>good</i> idea. But people generally like and/or respect the Gods. I'll have to tell all sorts of crazy lies! Fortunately I'm real good at lying. I faked out one of the Gods for <i>years</i>, this will be easy.&quot;<br /> <br /> -The armies of man march against the God with all the wonders and power of the age at their backs. The Gods obliterate these armies as easily as they might swat flies. Salem escapes, because she's the kind of roach even the gods have trouble pinning down.<br /> <br /> -The Gods are very upset with man. They revoke their gifts and blessings and fuck off out of the world. One of them fucks up the moon in a fit of pique. The First Age ends; civilization collapses, both because it was dependent heavily on the gifts bestowed by the Gods, and because Salem so poisoned mankind against itself that it tears itself into pieces fighting over the scraps. The world is reduced, a remnant of what it once was.<br /> <br /> -The Second Age begins. Mankind begins to rebuild. They discover within themselves a semblance (eh? eh? See what I did there? Fuck you, I'm clever!) of the blessings they once controlled, and discover and begin to manipulate Dust.<br /> <br /> -The Creatures of Grimm arise from the remnants of the God of Destruction's domain. The God of Destruction doesn't give a shit.<br /> <br /> -The Faunus arise from the remnants of the God of Creation's domain. The God of Creation is elated; new life that he hadn't planned for has sprung forth! He turns his face to the world again.<br /> <br /> -Salem seizes the God of Destruction's former earthly domain and begins to set herself up as a living god, offering &quot;protection&quot; from the Grimm that she, herself, largely (although not absolutely) has learned to control.<br /> <br /> -The God of Creation, by this time, has forgiven mankind; his brother, however, has not; he's still really fucking pissed off that Salem betrayed him and that mankind then stabbed him in the face <i>in her favor</i>. And the two must act in concert. The God of Destruction has agreed to these terms; the God of Creation may dispatch a champion to Remnant to stand against Salem and to unite and rebuild mankind. Along with this champion, they will once again bestow blessings, in the form of the four Relics. Mankind may use the Relics whenever they wish to summon the Gods back to Remnant and stand before them; if judged worthy, the Gods will dwell in Remnant again and bestow their blessings and the world will be made whole again. If not, the Gods will abandon Remnant to its own devices forever. The nature of the Third Age of the world is thus up to mankind to decide.<br /> <br /> I would also throw in the plot point that neither Salem nor Oz has the power to pull the Relic trigger. They need four worthy people in order to do it, who stand as proxies for and representatives of man in general.<br /> <br /> -Ozma returns to Remnant. The forever war between him and Salem begins.<br /> * * *<br /> <br /> Now, there are obviously some problems with what I've outlined here, but the point is it preserves the God of Destruction as a figure NOT of insane, malevolent, ridiculous evil, and the God of Creation as not simply utterly ineffectual, who requires the consent of his batfuck insane brother for anything to get done, and it makes the summoning of the Gods to Remnant not an obviously nuts choice. It also introduces some ambiguity in that choice; maybe you want the Gods to give you all their good shit, because things were pretty sweet in the old days, but also maybe you think that mankind need to learn to live without gods. It places agency in the hands of man.<br /> <br /> Gods can be a little bit evil and ridiculous, because they're gods. Ridiculous conditions and bargains and quests and divine neglect goes with the territory.<br /> <br /> But man, they REALLY can't be as evil as the God of Destruction is. Not in this day and age. You can get a pass on genocide if your name is Yahweh and people are writing your holy book like five thousand years ago. You really... CAN'T in a piece of popular entertainment circa 2018.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T14:47:33-08:00","id":1275906,"title":"","content":"It was a surprise to me that Salem started talking about plans to go after Shade Academy instead of Atlas Academy, but on second thought it makes sense. The Kingdom of Atlas is too hard a target, and better left for last when all the world outside of its gates is falling apart. Beacon is already held, and Haven empty, so the only vault left to choose is Shade's. Plus, the Relic of Destruction can be used against Atlas, or perhaps even to reveal the location of Beacon's vault by destroying all of Beacon until only an indestructible Relic of Choice remains.<br /> <br /> All of the academies should have the same school year, and Haven's school year was just about to start before Leonardo died and left the school closed.<br /> <br /> Team CFVY left for Vacuo to continue their training at Shade Academy. Their YA book series is going to begin with them leaving on a mission to rescue some people from a strangely never-ending horde of Grimm, which may be something Salem is causing to destabilize Vacuo before going after the academy.<br /> <br /> Team SSSN is also going to be heading to Shade soon, and they could be there at the start of the school year with Team CVFY.<br /> <br /> So even if Salem and her minions have been active in Vacuo long before Team RWBY finally gets there, two of their powerful allies will already be there, holding things together and ready to bring them up to speed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T10:56:04-08:00","id":1276085,"title":"","content":"It seems really hard to translate Yang Xiao-Long into a Dragon-Blood while keeping both her aesthetics and her tactics.<br /> <br /> Fire Aspect (Athletics, Dodge, Melee, Presence, Socialize) who favors Brawl/Martial Arts and Resistance, with other Abilities being picked to taste. Integrity, Archery/Firearms, Ride/Drive, Craft...<br /> <br /> Arguably the closest thing that a Dragon-Blood can get to Yang's &quot;Super Mode&quot; Semblance is the Fire Signature for Resistance, Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit. The Charm requires a Fire Aura, so any time that Yang's anima banner goes bonfire and turns any Aura she has into the Fire element, she can go Super Saiyan.<br /> <br /> But the Charm's <i>duration </i>is Aura, and that leads to some complications.<br /> <br /> Yang fights with her fists. Specifically, while wearing artifact fist weapons called Ember Celica, with great potential for Evocations. So naturally we'd want to choose the Ability that works best not only with Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit, but also with that weapon.<br /> <br /> Falcon Style allows smashfists, but it remains to be seen how well it matches her character concept. If it does, as a non-elemental Martial Art, its Charms pose no threat to Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit's duration.<br /> <br /> If Fire Dragon Style allowed the use of smashfists like her Ember Celica, it would be a perfect solution. But it doesn't, so it isn't. She can at least use the Style and its Charms for unarmed parries and kick attacks and maybe to potentially break limits with Falcon Style.<br /> <br /> The Brawl Ability and Terrestrial Brawl Charms <i>will </i>work with Ember Celica and its Evocations, but this is the most complicated puzzle.<br /> <br /> 1) If she's using Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit, she needs to maintain her Fire Aura. As a striker who seldom grapples, she becomes limited to basically just Become the Hammer and Pounding Surf Style. She couldn't even use Blade-Deflecting Palm.<br /> <br /> 2) Even without using Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit, once Yang's anima reaches bonfire, any Aura she has immediately turns into the Fire element, and if she loses that Aura, she will be prevented from gaining any new Aura from non-Fire Charms. But basically none of the Brawl Charms are Fire elemental, so Yang is locked out of the Aura-boosted effects and Aura-dependent of every Brawl Charm except the Fire Signature. So outside of Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit, the Fire Aura is of limited usefulness to her, even after heavy investment into Athletics and Dodge.<br /> <br /> 3) Erupting Fury Barrage, the Fire Signature, only spends Fire <i>Aura </i>but <i>not</i> levels of <i>anima banner</i>. As a reminder, a bonfire anima will transform any Aura Yang already has into Fire, and will prevent her from generating any Aura but Fire. But Erupting Fury Barrage is also the only Brawl Charm which <i>could </i>let her generate a new Fire Aura, so if she mixes elements with the EFB attack, she won't recover her Fire Aura at the end of the turn. She probably can't maintain that Fire Aura long enough to build the Initiative for another EFB.<br /> <br /> 4) Ignoring the Wood Signature Charm, a Terrestrial's only way to avoid or escape bonfire anima through spending anima levels is a Currents Sweep to Sea, a grappling Charm which is useless if your opponent never leaves close range, or at least not when you need to spend an anima level. So once she's in bonfire, she's probably staying there and stuck with Fire Auras and not getting back to a Water Aura. (This is something Ember Celica can solve, with an Evocation that spends anima levels.)<br /> <br /> 5) As a striker, Yang might want to use Stone Fist Strike, but it would cost her a Fire Aura that could be sustaining Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit or enabling/empowering other Fire Charms. More often, it would cost her a Water Aura that could be empowering Blade-Deflecting Palm, Pounding Surf Style, and Hammering Wave Technique, and allowing Swift-Striking Tide and Fist-Spinning Maelstrom. Stone Fist Strike could grant her an Earth Aura that would allow her to access Rolling Boulder Blow or Firmament-Shattering Impact for a smashing attack with her smashfists... if she doesn't need to use a reflexive Charm of the wrong type before her next turn. The Earth elemental Charms don't seem promising for anyone but Earth Aspects, since they only need to juggle two different elements instead of three. (They always told me not to build a <i>Magic: The Gathering</i> deck with three different colors.)<br /> <br /> 6) Wood Brawl Charms really have nothing for Yang. She doesn't need more grappling Charms, and Oaken Thew Exertion isn't useful enough for punching things to justify juggling a <i>fourth</i> element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-22-2018, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T12:00:16-08:00","id":1276293,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the really weird thing about the genocide plot point for me is that it is <i>completely unnecessary</i>. They had the God of Darkness kill everyone, then the God of Light made new people to replace them, so they could have just... had the God of Darkness revoke magic and leave, with no genocide.<br /> <br /> I'd still feel the gods are a bit dickish to punish all of humanity like that, but not to the point of &quot;fuck them&quot; evil that they come across as now.<br /> <br /> (Also, if Salem wants to kill the brothers, the logical thing would be for her to ask Jinn how to do so. Since they created Jinn, that might not work, but the seem about on par with the Yozis in terms of &quot;make sure our abused creations don't betray us.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Amusing joke theory: The God of Darkness didn't actually kill anyone. Instead, he teleported Salem to a duplicate universe with no people. The actual &quot;test&quot; is whether Salem and Ozpin realize that the supposed genocide was a monstrous act and rebel against the God of Darkness. If they do, they pass and Ozpin gets restored to life permanently, since recognizing the fundamental evil of the God of Darkness' genocide means that they now appreciate the value of life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T13:09:19-08:00","id":1276302,"title":"","content":"Granted a thing I've been curious about is how much of what they saw in that episode was completely new to Ozma. I mean that seems to be part of Jinn's operation hence why it was a full on vision instead of just her listing the major points. I mean we know from last week that parts of the vision could allow more information to be gleaned, hence why the current idea is that the silver eye trait is that it came from the elder brother. I mean its a fair assumption that Salem probably never told Ozma about that time she gathered an army to wage war on the gods figuring she'd either overthrow them, make them suffer, or make them kill her and that got everyone else on the planet killed instead.Seeing how that might require taking some of the blame for the incident.*<br /> <br /> So part of Ozma bailing out a few episodes ago are probably was probably a result of being forced to see just what and how much he was hiding all at once as opposed to the compartmentalization he'd been doing on the issues. Another part of it might have been just how much he was made aware of in more exacting detail than what he'd presumed in the past.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Hell I'd have to check the scene, but it might actually be possible that Ozma wasn't aware that the tragedy the light brother said the dark brother caused was an extinction event as opposed to just mass destruction. Let alone that his girlfriend provoked it. You know seeing how it appears civilization had already done a decent amount of reforming by the time he came back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T18:28:57-08:00","id":1276342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276293#post1276293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the really weird thing about the genocide plot point for me is that it is <i>completely unnecessary</i>. They had the God of Darkness kill everyone, then the God of Light made new people to replace them, so they could have just... had the God of Darkness revoke magic and leave, with no genocide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Narratively, that would mean everyone would know the truth about what the world was like, where the Grimm came from, and who was to blame for the fallen state of the world.<br /> <br /> Wiping out all of First Humanity means that no one knew the truth except Salem and Ozma, and Ozma could only spread the truth so far when competing with Salem's lies and humanity's fabrications.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd still feel the gods are a bit dickish to punish all of humanity like that, but not to the point of &quot;fuck them&quot; evil that they come across as now. </div> </div> </div>How much of humanity tried to stop the attempt to murder the gods? Those who weren't actively involved were complicit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if Salem wants to kill the brothers, the logical thing would be for her to ask Jinn how to do so. Since they created Jinn, that might not work </div> </div> </div>If Jinn's answer to &quot;how do I destroy Salem?&quot; was a simple &quot;You can't&quot;, then I doubt Salem can get a better answer about destroying, depowering, or otherwise defeating the gods who granted her that kind of immortality in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Amusing joke theory: The God of Darkness didn't actually kill anyone. Instead, he teleported Salem to a duplicate universe with no people. The actual &quot;test&quot; is whether Salem and Ozpin realize that the supposed genocide was a monstrous act and rebel against the God of Darkness. If they do, they pass and Ozpin gets restored to life permanently, since recognizing the fundamental evil of the God of Darkness' genocide means that they now appreciate the value of life. </div> </div> </div>Only Salem's trial is about admitting that she was wrong to value other human lives less than her own, which has nothing to do with how much either of the gods value human life.<br /> <br /> The rest of humanity's trial is about &quot;don't demand blessings from your creators while fighting among yourselves&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T18:30:33-08:00","id":1276343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276302#post1276302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted a thing I've been curious about is how much of what they saw in that episode was completely new to Ozma. I mean that seems to be part of Jinn's operation hence why it was a full on vision instead of just her listing the major points. I mean we know from last week that parts of the vision could allow more information to be gleaned, hence why the current idea is that the silver eye trait is that it came from the elder brother. I mean its a fair assumption that Salem probably never told Ozma about that time she gathered an army to wage war on the gods figuring she'd either overthrow them, make them suffer, or make them kill her and that got everyone else on the planet killed instead.Seeing how that might require taking some of the blame for the incident.*<br /> <br /> So part of Ozma bailing out a few episodes ago are probably was probably a result of being forced to see just what and how much he was hiding all at once as opposed to the compartmentalization he'd been doing on the issues. Another part of it might have been just how much he was made aware of in more exacting detail than what he'd presumed in the past.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Hell I'd have to check the scene, but it might actually be possible that Ozma wasn't aware that the tragedy the light brother said the dark brother caused was an extinction event as opposed to just mass destruction. Let alone that his girlfriend provoked it. You know seeing how it appears civilization had already done a decent amount of reforming by the time he came back.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wizard has used at least four questions over the last several hundred years or more; at least one of those questions could have been &quot;What was Salem hiding from me?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T18:53:45-08:00","id":1276345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276342#post1276342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narratively, that would mean everyone would know the truth about what the world was like, where the Grimm came from, and who was to blame for the fallen state of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to if that's not what the writers want.<br /> <br /> There are enormous swathes of history of our own world we know jack shit about, despite the fact that during those periods great civilizations had arisen and were operating. We still don't know where the Kingdom of Punt was. We only know that the Punic Wars happened because of two VERY thin primary sources. There's a five hundred or so period of Greek History that's an almost literal black hole, and a century-long period of English history where our only primary source is the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle, which isn't what you'd call comprehensive.<br /> <br /> And that's in OUR world, where civilization is far, far less precarious because we don't have murder monsters waiting to level our cities.<br /> <br /> You set the First Age of Remnant in the very distant past; go huge, like five or ten THOUSAND years. Toss a couple devastating, world-cataclysm Dark Ages between now and then and boom, nobody remembers jack shit about that ancient era, except for legends and stories that seem ridiculous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How much of humanity tried to stop the attempt to murder the gods? Those who weren't actively involved were complicit. </div> </div> </div>Yeah... no. This is an insane application of collective guilt. By this logic everyone who isn't actively fighting all evil, everywhere, all the time is complicit.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T20:05:14-08:00","id":1276358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276345#post1276345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... no. This is an insane application of collective guilt. By this logic everyone who isn't actively fighting all evil, everywhere, all the time is complicit.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I stand back and watch a man get stabbed to death without doing anything to stop it, not even calling the police, what then?<br /> <br /> Had other humans attempted to even warn the gods about the attack, the God of Light could probably have gotten his brother to spare them for their loyalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T20:17:52-08:00","id":1276363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276358#post1276358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I stand back and watch a man get stabbed to death without doing anything to stop it, not even calling the police, what then?<br /> <br /> Had other humans attempted to even warn the gods about the attack, the God of Light could probably have gotten his brother to spare them for their loyalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it infeasible that the whole of humanity had an awareness of the raid on the gods. Hell, I find it infeasible a significant majority was aware of it. That crowd was way too small to constitute enough for a total species judgement.<br /> <br /> I think it's pretty clear that the gods have something fucked up in their perspective on how to deal with problems, because overkill is always involved in their responses to some degree or another. Honestly, the both of them are the sort of gods that oblige you to become the devil, and Remnant is probably better off without them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T01:16:28-08:00","id":1276399,"title":"","content":"First, yeah the argument that not trying to stop Salem and her group's attack on the brothers constitutes guilt doesn't work. Not the least of which because we have no clue how many kingdoms she approached, it says she went to kingdoms and made the offer, but not that she went to all of them. Heck that she's convinced she could raise a bigger army when she thinks only her original forces were wiped out lends credence to the idea that most were probably unaware of the attack. More to the point, the indication is most people presumed the brothers all knowing and all powerful meaning most people would question the point of trying to defend them. You know seeing how the target of said attack would be presumed to already know, and sure as heck isn't in any danger from the attack. Heck checked with some religious friends of mine and their opinion on the matter was you point out the flaw in the idea, you try to talk the person out of it, and then if all that fails you prayers include the line, &quot;I'm not with the idiot, I tried to talk them out of it failed, and I am not involved in the idiocy they are attempting to commit.&quot; Plus maybe trying to get a good amount of distance and hope divine wrath doesn't have too much collateral damage for the purpose of making a point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T07:09:01-08:00","id":1276444,"title":"","content":"The problem being that the God of Darkness is not a reasonable fellow, and only behaves reasonable to the extent that his older brother can convince him.<br /> <br /> His older brother didn't even try to convince him to spare some of humanity, and I think that speaks to how impossible he felt that was without getting into a fight that would destroy all of humanity (and Second Humanity) anyway. You can argue about how much or little wiggle room the God of Light had to pull that off, but he clearly felt it wasn't enough to work.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, is no one interested in the &quot;Dragon-Blooded Yang&quot; puzzle above?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T07:57:49-08:00","id":1276455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276085#post1276085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems really hard to translate Yang Xiao-Long into a Dragon-Blood while keeping both her aesthetics and her tactics.<br /> <br /> Fire Aspect (Athletics, Dodge, Melee, Presence, Socialize) who favors Brawl/Martial Arts and Resistance, with other Abilities being picked to taste. Integrity, Archery/Firearms, Ride/Drive, Craft...<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>You can probably build a good fire-aspect brawler without using many brawl charms - grab an excellency, the balanced charms, the fire signature, maybe charms that you use at specific moments. Then grab resistance, athletics, dodge and evocations. The Athletics &quot;Run places while lighting your enemies on fire&quot; charms seem like good fits for Yang. She does do some grappling - generally not for very long, but some.<br /> I'd be inclined to say a lot of her ranged attacks and recoil-boosted stuff are Evocations of Ember Celica.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T09:45:52-08:00","id":1276470,"title":"","content":"Or maybe fire dragon style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T10:16:24-08:00","id":1276480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276455#post1276455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can probably build a good fire-aspect brawler without using many brawl charms - grab an excellency, the balanced charms</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be Become the Hammer, Water Dragon's Coils, Inescapable Whirlpool Hold, and Pounding Surf Style.<br /> <br /> But Pounding Surf Style is useless in a duel, and loses most of its power when Yang's Water Aura becomes Fire. Hammering Wave Technique isn't Balanced-keyworded and needs a Water Aura to make onslaught penalties last long enough for Pounding Surf Style in a duel. Even when fighting with her team, Yang is going to want a Water Aura to make Pounding Surf Style worthwhile.<br /> <br /> <i>EDIT: Excuse me, Balanced Brawl Charms also include Become the Wave, which like Pounding Surf Style is useless in a duel, but with her team it gives her an option for avoiding the need for Bellows-Pumping Stride or Dancing Ember Stride, allowing her more movement while keeping a Water Aura.<br /> <br /> This sort of teamwork also enables Swift-Striking Tide, but that Charm would end Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the fire signature </div> </div> </div>Plus the Earth Signature, at some point. In fact, possibly the Earth Signature before the Fire one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> maybe charms that you use at specific moments </div> </div> </div>Stone Fist Strike, Rolling Boulder Blow, and Firmament-Shattering Strike all fit Yang's style, but all of them force her to juggle a third element. She can use the first one at any time, but it will break any Water or Fire Aura she's got going. So she can't use any of them when using Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit, and two of them become unavailable when her anima reaches bonfire.<br /> <br /> I don't think she has any reason to learn the Wood Brawl Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then grab resistance </div> </div> </div>Definitely necessary for Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit and Ox-Body Technique, and it helps that Impervious Skin of Stone is Balanced. However, Robert Vance confirmed that Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit's ban against using Stamina to determine Soak means that Impervious Skin of Stone becomes powerless for its duration.<br /> <br /> But if she instead has an Earth Aura from using Stone Fist Strike, then ISoS is powered up, and she can use Unfeeling Earth Meditation and Perfected Scales of the Dragon (if she chooses that as her second Resistance Signature at Essence 5).<br /> <br /> If she's in Water Aura instead, Eternal Tide Endurance becomes available.<br /> <br /> <br /> Don't forget Integrity, either. Most of the basics are Balanced, and so is Immolating Phoenix-Soul Fury. Though Unquenchable Battle-Passion is purely Fire.<br /> <br /> The ones which are solidly Earth are compatible with or empowered by an Earth Aura she generates from using Stone Fist Strike to, and that includes the possibility of using Wound-Denying Dragon Faith to supplement Unfeeling Earth Meditation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> athletics </div> </div> </div>She can use Effortlessly Rising Flame, Soaring Leap Technique, Perfect Climbing Attitude, and Incense Smoke Ladder regardless of her current Aura. Three of those Charms can help her gain a Fire Aura regardless of her anima level, and one could help her enter an Earth Aura for use with her Earth-punching Charms.<br /> <br /> She can't use Bellows-Pumping Stride or Dancing Ember Stride (-/+Falling Star Maneuver) without breaking any Water or Earth Aura she has, though both are accessible while using Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit. Using Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit definitely helps one execute Falling Star Maneuver, but that's not possible until Essence 5.<br /> <br /> Starting a fire with Bellows-Pumping Stride (-/+ Seething Dragon Footprint) requires spending a Fire Aura, which would end Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit.<br /> <br /> Inescapable Blazing Advance likewise requires you to spend a Fire Aura, which probably cancels Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit instantly, before it can help with the rush roll.<br /> <br /> If she uses Strength of Stone Technique before getting a Fire Aura, she can stack its effects with Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit for attacking or performing feats of strength. She cannot use Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit together with any other &quot;feats of strength&quot; Athletics Charms, though using any of the Earth ones could help her get an Earth Aura for her Earth-punching Charms.<br /> <br /> After Inescapable Blazing Advance, her next Signature Athletics Charm is probably Unshakable Mountain Spine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> dodge </div> </div> </div>If she uses Threshold-Warding Stance to supplement a Disengage action, it could grant her a Fire Aura. Otherwise, being Balanced, she can use it to enhance Evasion without losing an Earth or Water Aura.<br /> <br /> Using Ebbing Tide Recedes would break an Earth or Fire Aura. But if she has a Water Aura from her Brawl Charms, ETC is empowered, and she can spend the Aura to use Flow With Strife (if she chooses that as her non-Fire Signature Dodge Charm).<br /> <br /> If she has an Earth Aura, she could expend it to use Unmoving Center Enlightenment (if she chooses that as her non-Fire Signature Dodge Charm).<br /> <br /> She can use Flickering Candle Meditation, Heat-of-Battle Advance, Hopping Firecracker Evasion, Ember-Amid-Smoke Misdirection, Unassailable Body of Fire, Bonfire Shadow Evasion, Coiling Dragon Dance, and Elusive Dragon-God Dispersion together with Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit... which is good, since losing her Stamina for Soak calculation, and the inability to use any Resistance soak Charm but Fire Protection Prana means her Evasion becomes crucial.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and evocations.<br /> <br /> I'd be inclined to say a lot of her ranged attacks and recoil-boosted stuff are Evocations of Ember Celica. </div> </div> </div>All of them, really.<br /> <br /> And again, there's Falcon Style, potentially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-24-2018, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T10:17:50-08:00","id":1276481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276470#post1276470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe fire dragon style.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already addressed that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276085#post1276085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yang fights with her fists. Specifically, while wearing artifact fist weapons called Ember Celica, with great potential for Evocations. So naturally we'd want to choose the Ability that works best not only with Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit, but also with that weapon.<br /> <br /> Falcon Style allows smashfists, but it remains to be seen how well it matches her character concept. If it does, as a non-elemental Martial Art, its Charms pose no threat to Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit's duration.<br /> <br /> If Fire Dragon Style allowed the use of smashfists like her Ember Celica, it would be a perfect solution. But it doesn't, so it isn't. She can at least use the Style and its Charms for unarmed parries and kick attacks and maybe to potentially break limits with Falcon Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T11:25:06-08:00","id":1276501,"title":"","content":"Ember Celicia are arguably bracers and not smashfists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T12:28:19-08:00","id":1276513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276501#post1276501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ember Celicia are arguably bracers and not smashfists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting proposal.<br /> <br /> They certainly do not cover Yang's fists at all. The protruding end is more about extending the gun barrel far enough that shots hit what she punches, rather than enveloping her fists in the blast, but the protruding part does not, itself, hit the target, because it falls just short of her knuckles.<br /> <br /> She can strike someone with it on a backhand strike, and she can use them to parry like bracers, but that alone doesn't necessarily make it a smashfist. Especially if, mechanically, the backhand is still a barehanded strike.<br /> <br /> If silken armor can be given special dispensation to work with martial arts Form Charms, it seems that bracers could be given special dispensation to work with martial arts parries.<br /> <br /> So, in effect, what we're looking at is a combat artifact that is not technically a weapon in the usual mechanical sense. It enhances attacks through its Evocations, without giving Yang's punches the traits of an artifact weapon.<br /> <br /> Therefore, it should be totally compatible with most martial arts that involve bare-handed attacks, such as Fire Dragon Style.<br /> <br /> Awesome. Thank you for contributing that idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T14:40:23-08:00","id":1276528,"title":"","content":"I can't remember, have we covered prosthetics yet so we can model Yang's new arm?<br /> <br /> <br /> can we use it's evokations to give it a vibration function?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T14:56:59-08:00","id":1276529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276528#post1276528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember, have we covered prosthetics yet so we can model Yang's new arm?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a sample prosthetic arm in <i>Arms of the Chosen</i>.<br /> <br /> Essentially, her new arm would simply serve as a replacement for her old arm AND the lost half of Ember Celica, allowing her to use her purchased EC Evocations with that arm, and any Evocations that would require the use of both halves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> can we use it's evokations to give it a vibration function? </div> </div> </div>Functions which assist in brushing one's teeth probably fall below the dramatic level of which players need to spend XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-24-2018, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T16:05:38-08:00","id":1276534,"title":"","content":"And if they enhance Celestial Bliss Technique?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T19:10:18-08:00","id":1276550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276534#post1276534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if they enhance Celestial Bliss Technique?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it would certainly allow for some Devastating Attacks.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=535\" data-tempid=\"temp_535_1545707201500_679\" /><br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=536\" data-tempid=\"temp_536_1545707034130_204\" /><br /> <br /> Devastating Attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T05:31:21-08:00","id":1276609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276550#post1276550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it would certainly allow for some Devastating Attacks.<br /> <br /> [ATTACH=CONFIG]temp_535_1545707201500_679[/ATTACH]<br /> <br /> [ATTACH=CONFIG]temp_536_1545707034130_204[/ATTACH]<br /> <br /> Devastating Attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Images not showing, but I'm not sure I want them to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T06:58:31-08:00","id":1276625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276609#post1276609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Images not showing, but I'm not sure I want them to.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s a cute comic of Penny giving a clothed Ruby a back massage enhanced by her vibration function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T13:26:04-08:00","id":1276683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276529#post1276529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Functions which assist in brushing one's teeth probably fall below the dramatic level of which players need to spend XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, how about one that makes the hand spin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T20:01:10-08:00","id":1276731,"title":"","content":"Episode 8 was ok. Not really that much to go on, some explanation of the the Silver Eyes and stuff. I didn't feel like any of that was a big groundbreaker or bombshell moment, we know Cinder is part Grimm and the backstory of the eyes isn't that meaningful tbh. <br /> <br /> I wonder why, if Salem put out a hit on the Grim Reaper for her eyes, that Ruby is on the &quot;Do Not Kill&quot; list. <br /> <br /> pretty standard mid season switch plotlines episode. meh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T15:27:07-08:00","id":1277406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276342#post1276342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narratively, that would mean everyone would know the truth about what the world was like, where the Grimm came from, and who was to blame for the fallen state of the world.<br /> <br /> Wiping out all of First Humanity means that no one knew the truth except Salem and Ozma, and Ozma could only spread the truth so far when competing with Salem's lies and humanity's fabrications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. People in the old world don't seem to know very much, and Salem herself was only raising her army for a comparatively short while from (what looked like) just a few major cities and population centers. It's not a particularly big army, from what we saw. Even then, just &quot;kill the entire army, including Salem&quot;, while callous, would have resolved it without the casual genocide of countless uninvolved innocents.<br /> <br /> (It would have required that the brothers go back on their word to make her suffer forever, which would doubtless offend their <i>precious</i> demon-god pride. But that's the point - they essentially murdered an entire planet in a fit of pique because their pride as demon-lords was offended. That's monstrously awful - worse than anything anyone else in the series has done by several orders of magnitude, to the point where it instantly makes them the overarching villains of the entire setting, with Ozpin as the more proximate villain due to his loyalty to them.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How much of humanity tried to stop the attempt to murder the gods? Those who weren't actively involved were complicit. </div> </div> </div>It's an entire planet! With several massive continents. Salem's army looks like it has, like, a few thousand people in it. Even if it didn't, there are countless innocent farmers, children, old folk... people all over the world who would have had nothing to do with that army and no way to stop it.<br /> <br /> And why would it even be humanity's job to protect the demon-kings? The Demon of Darkness and the Demon of Light have constantly presented themselves as aloof, omnipotent beings. How is saying &quot;fighting them is dumb, I'm just going to keep farming&quot; remotely a crime deserving of immediate death?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Jinn's answer to &quot;how do I destroy Salem?&quot; was a simple &quot;You can't&quot;, then I doubt Salem can get a better answer about destroying, depowering, or otherwise defeating the gods who granted her that kind of immortality in the first place. </div> </div> </div>They only asked how to kill her. Sealing the demon-kings or mind-wiping them or whatever offers a lot more options.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, the brothers are clearly spiteful, petty tyrants. I absolutely would not put it past them to have put more power and effort into making Salem suffer agony and pain (after all, she <i>offended</i> them by calling them out) than they bother to put into protecting themselves. They clearly think they're above all sentient beings, free to make and then torture or genocide them as they please based on whatever crimes or offenses they choose to concoct; lots of mythology has beings like that be careless about their own defenses.<br /> <br /> (This is the Exalted forum, after all. And if any entities in recent fiction deserved to be turned inside-out and imprisoned in their own bodies, it's the Brothers.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only Salem's trial is about admitting that she was wrong to value other human lives less than her own, which has nothing to do with how much either of the gods value human life. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but if the demon-kings themselves don't value human life (and they obviously, unambiguously place no value on it whatsoever), it's absurd and hypocritical of them to turn around and blame Salem.<br /> <br /> Salem's crime is wanting her dead lover back (something we clearly see the gods are capable of doing in multiple ways and at, as far as we can see, no cost to anyone else.) That's... not a very big crime, as far as &quot;crimes against life&quot; go.<br /> <br /> The Demon of Darkness <i>murdered an entire planet</i> and the Demon of Light dismissed this act of genocide as just the logical conclusion to a 'failed experiment.' That means they have no understanding of the value of life themselves, which means that their lecture to Salem was just vapid, spiteful babbling - she hadn't committed any actual crime as they understood it, she had just offended them personally, so they said whatever random things they thought would hurt her most, and made up whatever they thought would make them sound Wise and Meaningful in order to salve their own hurt feelings.<br /> <br /> But they can't actually have any serious feelings about the value of life when they're complicit in casual genocide. Obviously it's absurd to take any self-righteous posturing about the &quot;value of life&quot; seriously from demons who moments later genocide an entire planet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rest of humanity's trial is about &quot;don't demand blessings from your creators while fighting among yourselves&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Salem was the only one demanding blessings. (And, technically, it wasn't even a blessing so much as &quot;please repair the damage that the disease you created did to my loved one.&quot;) The others wanted to kill the demon-kings because Salem's story convinced them that the demons had no respect for human life and were therefore responsible for all the suffering and death humanity had to endure, which was <i>entirely correct</i>. The demon-kings proved it when they responded to this by, again, genociding an entire planet!<br /> <br /> Let's say that, in the instant when the Demon of Darkness tries to genocide the world, Salem suddenly becomes more powerful than them. (Let's say their creator, The Father, disapproves of what they're doing and empowers Salem to pass judgment on them.) She blocks the genocide-spell, then depowers them both and tells them that they must now live as mortals in the world they created, suffering the torments they inflicted on their creations until they've learned the value of human life.<br /> <br /> Is this outcome more or less just than the one we saw? I think it is <i>extremely obvious</i> that that would be a better outcome from any rational ethical framework - Salem's offenses are marginal at best; the crimes of the Brothers are obscene. She's the one who should be forcing them to learn the value of life, not the other way around. The only reason anyone would side with them is because they're more powerful - which is the logic of bullies and tyrants (quite appropriate, since, as I outlined above, they have no understanding of anything they tried to lecture Salem on - it was all exclusively about bullying her for having the audacity to trick them and therefore for hurting their vicious demon-god pride.)<br /> <br /> If Salem had <i>succeeded</i> in tricking them, or succeeded in binding and sealing them, she'd be rightfully seen as a heroic figure. If Ozpin had killed them - which was his <i>original job</i>, as a monster-slayer - he would be, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 12-29-2018, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T16:44:26-08:00","id":1277414,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Pyrrha has been invoked what, twice since her death? Well, twice it struck true. Anyway.<br /> <br /> So semblances can be stolen, albeit it's specific enough it looks like a big secret. Makes sense, considering we have already seen souls being toyed around. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T16:50:06-08:00","id":1277415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1277406#post1277406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Demon of Darkness <i>murdered an entire planet</i> and the Demon of Light dismissed this act of genocide as just the logical conclusion to a 'failed experiment.' That means they have no understanding of the value of life themselves, which means that their lecture to Salem was just vapid, spiteful babbling - she hadn't committed any actual crime as they understood it, she had just offended them personally</div> </div> </div> </div>Do note that you are judging them by the same criteria you would judge a human.<br /> <br /> They clearly do not. Whatever standards they hold between themselves is not the same that they do for humans.<br /> <br /> Which makes sense. They are not humans. They created the humans, apparently rather easily too. They literally operate on a different scale. It would be bizarre if they didn't judge by different values.<br /> Their standards for humans is more like ours are for the dogs we bred over the milennia.<br /> <br /> <br /> Primordials, anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T17:26:08-08:00","id":1277417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1277415#post1277415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do note that you are judging them by the same criteria you would judge a human.<br /> <br /> They clearly do not. Whatever standards they hold between themselves is not the same that they do for humans.<br /> <br /> Which makes sense. They are not humans. They created the humans, apparently rather easily too. They literally operate on a different scale. It would be bizarre if they didn't judge by different values.<br /> Their standards for humans is more like ours are for the dogs we bred over the milennia.<br /> <br /> <br /> Primordials, anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>This was the entire crux of my previous argument, that the Gods simply cannot be held to human standards and them destroying humanity in total as revenge for humanity trying to overthrow the gods is different that the human act of genocide. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar517_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"517\" data-vbnamecard=\"517\">Aquillion</a> is very anti-god however, seeing them as petty tyrants. <br /> <br /> Honestly we're just going around in circles vis-a-vis the gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T17:27:20-08:00","id":1277418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1277415#post1277415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do note that you are judging them by the same criteria you would judge a human.<br /> <br /> They clearly do not. Whatever standards they hold between themselves is not the same that they do for humans.<br /> <br /> Which makes sense. They are not humans. They created the humans, apparently rather easily too. They literally operate on a different scale. It would be bizarre if they didn't judge by different values.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, a king would tell you he should be judged by a different standard than a commoner, too. I think that since they have power, they can use that power to one-sidedly judge others and reject anyone else's judgment of them; but that's purely about them having power - bigger fists, holding a knife, holding the gun, whatever. Obviously from a narrative standpoint we're not supposed to <i>accede</i> to that logic - again, it's the logic of bullies and tyrants.<br /> <br /> In a larger moral sense, all sentient beings should be held to the same standard - more or less, with recognition that their state or status might grant extenuating circumstances. But that sort of extenuating circumstance would be more of a reason to grant mercy to the powerless, who are often forced into situations with no good answer or who are forced to weigh things that are precious to them against their moral code, than it is to grant mercy to the powerful, who have more options.<br /> <br /> In other words, if we're going to hold people to individual standards based on their circumstances and nature, I would be more inclined to grant mercy to Salem, who was in a horrible situation, and to judge the Brothers far more harshly - they had more than enough time, power, and freedom to acquaint themselves with the human mindset and the value of human life if they cared to do so, while Salem was forced to watch her beloved die directly in front of her and was then confronted by callous demons who could help but would not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their standards for humans is more like ours are for the dogs we bred over the milennia. </div> </div> </div>That's the sort of logic humans use when they exterminate each other, too. Even if we were to grant that it was ever valid logic (and I view it as both groundless and morally repulsive), the Brothers have shown absolutely no evidence that they're actually higher beings in any sense beyond having the power to to destroy and create life.<br /> <br /> That isn't some sort of vast cosmic mystery that necessarily implies (<i>jazz hands</i>) DEEP COSMIC CONSCIOUSNESS. We can create and destroy life, too. Their ability to populate a planet isn't far beyond what we can do with current reproductive technology; their ability to depopulate a planet is comparable to having a bunch of nukes. Part of the reason I'm trying to carefully avoid calling them &quot;gods&quot; is because the word is a thought-terminating cliche that leads people to ascribe this vague handwavy higher-consciousness and freedom from moral constraints to an entity without any <i>rationale</i> beyond &quot;well, they use that label, and they glow yellow, so clearly they're so super-smart and super-civilized that morality doesn't apply to them.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't think it works that way. Sentience and sapience are a hard line. Once someone has those traits, they have certain rights and certain responsibilities, which are absolutely equal and completely reciprocal whether we're talking about the highest, most transcendent cosmic god or the lowest crippled beggar - if the highest of holies murders a beggar, it is still murder, and they should be called to account to it. The fact that they aren't is purely because of the differential in <i>power</i>, not <i>value</i> - again, the logic of tyrants and bullies.<br /> <br /> My view on this is, in part, because our stories inevitably exist in the context of the real world; you can't show the Demon of Darkness genociding a world without considering the context of genocide in our own world. Because of that context, a story that implies that a god has more worth than a beggar is a detestable story. I'm not interested in any story that would imply that there exist superior sentient beings who have some sort of moral right to freely genocide and murder lesser sentient beings, and seeing stories like that makes me concerned about the mindset of anyone who would write (or even consider) something so horrible.<br /> <br /> (As I said above, while I'll argue this until I'm blue in the face, I have begrudgingly conceded that there's a high priority that RWBY is that sort of detestable story. Still, I'll keep watching in the vague hope-against-hope that the endgame is Salem and team RWBY banding together to bring the Brothers to justice.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Primordials, anyone? </div> </div> </div>Obviously everything I've said about the Brothers applies equally to the Primordials; that's part of the reason I get so irritated when the books (or posters here) seem to be engaging in apologetics for their mindset. Obviously they consider themselves to be above the morality of lesser beings, but their current situation shows that, well... if you're going to lean on the logic of bullies and tyrants to put yourself above anyone you consider incapable of harming you, you're likely to <i>live by the sword, die by the sword</i>, so to speak.<br /> <br /> (The state of the Primordials also shows how pathetic that sort of &quot;VAST AND SUPERIOR&quot; argument looks when it's stripped of the power that normally accompanies it. I don't think &quot;the Yozis are superior beings, so we should let them out and allow them to kill everyone else in the world at their whims if they choose to do so&quot; is meant to be seen as a sane or moral course of action. My own opinion is that it's so two-dimensionally stupid and moustache-twirlingly evil that the books wasted far more time on it than it was worth already. But, again, it does seem to have its defenders, given how many people still side with Ozpin.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 12-29-2018, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T17:42:26-08:00","id":1277421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1277417#post1277417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was the entire crux of my previous argument, that the Gods simply cannot be held to human standards and them destroying humanity in total as revenge for humanity trying to overthrow the gods is different that the human act of genocide. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar517_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"517\" data-vbnamecard=\"517\">Aquillion</a> is very anti-god however, seeing them as petty tyrants.<br /> <br /> Honestly we're just going around in circles vis-a-vis the gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree they are petty tyrants. By our standards. Condemning them for not holding up to that is foolish. Instead, condemn them for the dangerous monsters that they are <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T18:11:54-08:00","id":1277423,"title":"","content":"The God of Light expressed his condolences for Salem and actually lowered himself to the act of explaining his reasons and motivations to a woman who had absolutely no ability to force him to do anything. He really was ready to spill his guts to anyone who came to visit him, and he\u2019s the guy who created Jinn specifically to give humanity knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T19:09:59-08:00","id":1277429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1277418#post1277418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, a king would tell you he should be judged by a different standard than a commoner, too. I think that since they have power, they can use that power to one-sidedly judge others and reject anyone else's judgment of them; but that's purely about them having power - bigger fists, holding a knife, holding the gun, whatever. Obviously from a narrative standpoint we're not supposed to <i>accede</i> to that logic - again, it's the logic of bullies and tyrants.</div> </div> </div> </div>A king is still fundamentally human. Any differences he or she has to other humans are accounted in externalities and in human variance.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1277418#post1277418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a larger moral sense, all sentient beings should be held to the same standard - more or less, with recognition that their state or status might grant extenuating circumstances. But that sort of extenuating circumstance would be more of a reason to grant mercy to the powerless, who are often forced into situations with no good answer or who are forced to weigh things that are precious to them against their moral code, than it is to grant mercy to the powerful, who have more options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. This is a perspective worth holding, and the only way to remain moral if that moral code is to be isonomic. Yet, this <i>is</i> a complication that will arise eventually. Whatever other life forms that qualify as &quot;sentient&quot; (which is in itself a lurid question) will most likely be different enough that our current understanding of it breaks, especially if they are not derivative of our own. It's really hard to answer what is sentient without some tautologies, chief amongst them that any species that propagated for any significant time will value itself above others. Bridging acknowledgement and morality can be really hard.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1277418#post1277418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, if we're going to hold people to individual standards based on their circumstances and nature, I would be more inclined to grant mercy to Salem, who was in a horrible situation, and to judge the Brothers far more harshly - they had more than enough time, power, and freedom to acquaint themselves with the human mindset and the value of human life if they cared to do so, while Salem was forced to watch her beloved die directly in front of her and was then confronted by callous demons who could help but would not.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's empathizing more than moral judgment, isn't it? We all empathize. Yet she is very much human, and thus to be judged by human standards (and whatever else fits the bill, i'm sticking to just human for simplicity. In this sense, say, every species in the Mass Effect galactic council and some more fit what I'm labeling human here).<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1277418#post1277418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the sort of logic humans use when they exterminate each other, too. Even if we were to grant that it was ever valid logic (and I view it as both groundless and morally repulsive), the Brothers have shown absolutely no evidence that they're actually higher beings in any sense beyond having the power to to destroy and create life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, of course. Dehumanizing is the most basic tool to make people feel no remorse about destroying people. Why even bring this up? It's not applicable to the current discussion: every single case of de-humanizing humans is fundamentally different from treating with a truly non-human creature in the first place. This is not relativism. This is an axiom of the setting. The two brothers are not human, just like humans are not goats, just like sea sponges are not human. Whatever they are, they are labeled as gods for their transcendence of anything human.<br /> As such, they are literally beyond our capacity to understand comprehensively (and they will never be portrayed perfectly as such because humans are writing the script). <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1277418#post1277418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That isn't some sort of vast cosmic mystery that necessarily implies (<i>jazz hands</i>) DEEP COSMIC CONSCIOUSNESS. We can create and destroy life, too. Their ability to populate a planet isn't far beyond what we can do with current reproductive technology; their ability to depopulate a planet is comparable to having a bunch of nukes. Part of the reason I'm trying to carefully avoid calling them &quot;gods&quot; is because the word is a thought-terminating cliche that leads people to ascribe this vague handwavy higher-consciousness and freedom from moral constraints to an entity without any <i>rationale</i> beyond &quot;well, they use that label, and they glow yellow, so clearly they're so super-smart and super-civilized that morality doesn't apply to them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But it is, isn't it? They <i>are</i> portrayed as something beyond humanity.<br /> On the scale...While we alter the planet far more than most(probably all) earthen life forms ever did, we are nowhere near as powerful, nowhere near as immediately destructive as those two things were. They, literally, <i>casually and selectively</i> wiped out all of humanity. They could probably shatter the planet into an asteroid belt in a few days if the moon collapse is anything to go by.<br /> <br /> Compare to your &quot;all nuke total destruction&quot; scenario. We have what, 15 thousand nukes in the world? A rough estimate is 600 gigatons of yield. You can round up by saying its 15k tsar bombas, a total of 750 gigatons. 3,7 x 10^21 joules of energy released. That's roughly 250 days of the solar output that hits earth at the farthest from the sun (closer is just a wee bit more potent). Whatever result this brings is probably not going to be more than an exctinction event (remember extinction events tend to last a few millenia). A nuclear winter at least. A few millenia of radioactive waste at most.<br /> Which means that you can wipe out humanity(along with a bunch other creatures)... armed with the total combined efforts of millions of people backed by the work of billions before them, and the actual delivery probably demanding weeks upon weeks of precise strikes, and even then it might not wipe humanity out. We <i>know</i> as little as 10k humans managed to restart after an apocalyptic event.<br /> <br /> The gods <i>thanos snapped humanity off</i>.<br /> <i><b>Through individual might alone</b></i>.<br /> <br /> It's an entirely different scale, it simply doesn't compare. (even if one day it will. I conjecture it will, but the temporal separation is important. We are somewhat disconnected from our paleolitic cousins through how we can transform the world, and these humans that conquer stars will be disconnected from us for the same reason)<br /> <br /> Maybe it helps you shift a bit your perspective if you note that we currently are alone in our &quot;sentience&quot;? We have not created anything remotely sentient as these two gods did in creating humans so it's hard to compare.<br /> <br /> <b>More importantly, it's not &quot;freedom from moral constraints&quot;. My statement does not grant a &quot;right&quot;, nor a &quot;privilege&quot; via their condition. It is simply a statement that they do not function in a relatable way.</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1277418#post1277418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it works that way. Sentience and sapience are a hard line. Once someone has those traits, they have certain rights and certain responsibilities, which are absolutely equal and completely reciprocal whether we're talking about the highest, most transcendent cosmic god or the lowest crippled beggar - if the highest of holies murders a beggar, it is still murder, and they should be called to account to it. The fact that they aren't is purely because of the differential in <i>power</i>, not <i>value</i> - again, the logic of tyrants and bullies.<br /> <br /> My view on this is, in part, because our stories inevitably exist in the context of the real world; you can't show the Demon of Darkness genociding a world without considering the context of genocide in our own world. Because of that context, a story that implies that a god has more worth than a beggar is a detestable story. I'm not interested in any story that would imply that there exist superior sentient beings who have some sort of moral right to freely genocide and murder lesser sentient beings, and seeing stories like that makes me concerned about the mindset of anyone who would write (or even consider) something so horrible.<br /> <br /> (As I said above, while I'll argue this until I'm blue in the face, I have begrudgingly conceded that there's a high priority that RWBY is that sort of detestable story. Still, I'll keep watching in the vague hope-against-hope that the endgame is Salem and team RWBY banding together to bring the Brothers to justice.)<br /> <br /> Obviously everything I've said about the Brothers applies equally to the Primordials; that's part of the reason I get so irritated when the books (or posters here) seem to be engaging in apologetics for their mindset. Obviously they consider themselves to be above the morality of lesser beings, but their current situation shows that, well... if you're going to lean on the logic of bullies and tyrants to put yourself above anyone you consider incapable of harming you, you're likely to <i>live by the sword, die by the sword</i>, so to speak.<br /> <br /> (The state of the Primordials also shows how pathetic that sort of &quot;VAST AND SUPERIOR&quot; argument looks when it's stripped of the power that normally accompanies it. I don't think &quot;the Yozis are superior beings, so we should let them out and allow them to kill everyone else in the world at their whims if they choose to do so&quot; is meant to be seen as a sane or moral course of action. My own opinion is that it's so two-dimensionally stupid and moustache-twirlingly evil that the books wasted far more time on it than it was worth already. But, again, it does seem to have its defenders, given how many people still side with Ozpin.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep going back to how they are evil because they harm our moral standards.<br /> I agree.<br /> I wholeheartedly agree with that. They are monsters. And they will be monsters in this sense for so long as they are without peer.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yet none of that touches on my point of disagreement: They function differently from humans. And they do so in a manner that can't ever be connected back to humanity. This doesn't mean you are wrong in thinking they are monsters for what they do. It means you are wrong in <i>expecting</i> them to follow those rules, and in thinking doing this means giving them any sort of &quot;moral value&quot; you keep condemning.<br /> It's the &quot;going up the sentience scale&quot; analog of the &quot;lateral&quot; and the &quot;downards&quot; scenario of fighting off a predator or a mugger. You fucking neutralize them, but the standards use to judge them aren't, and can't be, the same.<br /> <br /> <br /> So please stop answering to my arguments as if they were apologetic. They're not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-31T20:44:08-08:00","id":1277753,"title":"","content":"Holy shit, I didn't think there could be a worse episode than Kuroyuri, but Lost did it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T05:05:05-08:00","id":1278038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1277753#post1277753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit, I didn't think there could be a worse episode than Kuroyuri, but Lost did it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well shucks. I'm just gonna have to wait with my fellow proles to find out what happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T07:17:19-08:00","id":1278061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1278038#post1278038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well shucks. I'm just gonna have to wait with my fellow proles to find out what happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have watched both episodes and don\u2019t know what he means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T09:18:36-08:00","id":1278088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1278061#post1278061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have watched both episodes and don\u2019t know what he means.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got some time today, I'll explain once I've got de-sickening done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T10:56:57-08:00","id":1278104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1278088#post1278088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got some time today, I'll explain once I've got de-sickening done.</div> </div> </div> </div>In case it matters, I do not see each chapter as an episode, but as one part of a movie which Rooster Teeth produces and releases in chunks, before airing the whole movie in theatres later. <br /> <br /> Which influences how I feel about breather chapters, unfocused chapters, and chapters that end on cliffhangers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T13:42:53-08:00","id":1278139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1278104#post1278104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In case it matters, I do not see each chapter as an episode, but as one part of a movie which Rooster Teeth produces and releases in chunks, before airing the whole movie in theatres later.<br /> <br /> Which influences how I feel about breather chapters, unfocused chapters, and chapters that end on cliffhangers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lost is bad on it's own, but it also just brings to the forefront a lot of problems that RWBY has on the whole.<br /> <br /> I like RWBY, but occasionally it stretches my tolerance for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-02-2019, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T19:19:34-08:00","id":1278221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1278139#post1278139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lost is bad on it's own, but it also just brings to the forefront a lot of problems that RWBY has on the whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>...such as?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T00:27:31-08:00","id":1278262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1278221#post1278221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...such as?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been desickening, I'm getting to it.<br /> <br /> ...Also I was watching the last seasons of Series of Unfortunate Events, BUT ANYWAYS.<br /> <br /> LET'S TALK ABOUT LOST.<br /> <br /> Not the Abrams one, the RWBY one. *rewatches to get bearing*<br /> <br /> A lot of Volume 6 has been pre-occupied with subjects and themes I've personally been finding dull on the whole-No, I did not want to know or care about Salem's backstory, and honestly reincarnation took out a lot of my interest in Ozpin's backstory, and hey kids, did you know that the sort of conflict you're facing now looks an awful lot like the job you went out of your way to train for? The house was cool, as we finally started redefining the conflicts for Blake and Yang, finally started delivering Qrow's alcoholism as a conflict, got into Weiss's trepidation, and the Apathy as a thing on top of all of that was a cooler metaphor and conflict than the actual Volume theme, but by and large this Volume just hasn't been there for me. But then we got to Lost, and it just highlights so many of RWBY's problems with storytelling philosophy and method, in particular to some of the very bad ideas it has about setup and payoff. I do not want to dive into that subject without going back and talking about the other seasons of RWBY and I've got too much to watch for that-so we'll try and keep the more pertinent points concise while we go through just the episode.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Oscar Has No Gas-Stakes in a Barren Character</u></b><br /> First off, when last we left off, we were left to chase off after Oscar-which is already a bit of a rocky place to start a conflict from. Oscar Pine, from his inception, has not really had much characterization beyond his base trope. Oscar has never been a character the series has dug enough into for us to invest his-we never got a sense of what his life was like, what his ambitions were, what he thought of the world, etc-since his introduction, the series has been more about just getting up and going with him to the plot points without working to get us invested in him. It's not like this season hasn't given us a lot of room to do so-but then again, RWBY is not as good at balancing its' character loads as some of the shows it tries to ape. The most they've done if sell us on the idea that he problems with the psychic invasion of Ozpin and that his arc should involve his surrender, but either Oscar just gives up too quick or not enough is given to his protests to really make me care too much about him. So going into the episode trying to be worried about Oscar just isn't going to happen-he's been too much a boilerplate trope to much care about him, too much of a concept to see him as anything worth losing.<br /> <br /> Normally this would be where putting Ozpin at stake would be effective, and in fact has some cool potential despite the fact that Ozpin has been losing a lot of his dynamics the older and more immortal he gets, because we at least get that he is important to the story and that his loss means something...except for two problems, namely a) having sidelined Ozpin for most of the Volume has put him out of sight, out of mind, and so without the character there to cause some tension and fear for his sake just isn't going to happen, and b) the show <i>really</i> wants you to understand that it's concerned about Oscar, seeing as <i>the Big, Bad Ozpin is such a big bad man</i>, which, sorry, what am I supposed to be holding Ozpin accountable to here? At worst, he's going to summon the gods again, and while I'm definitely for finding an answer without those assholes, really I just don't feel the stakes in stopping Salem near as much as the show would like me to. She has to be stopped <i>now</i>. That's <i>it</i>. Fighting her again and again is really no different from just fighting the Grimm over and over, and honestly that feels more thematically resonant with where RWBY wants to be anyways.<br /> <br /> As is, I'm just not particularly convinced Ozpin would summon the gods, and so beyond that, he's...what exactly? So without me feeling Oz is actually accountable for the MAJOR PLOT TWISTS OF THE SEASONS, It's harder for me invest in feeling bad for Oscar when I'm busy feeling like everyone else is being stupidly overbearing on Oz.<br /> <br /> So even before the episode begins, I'm not particularly invested in what's going to happen. The show knew this, and so had a clever plan!<br /> <br /> <b><u>As You Know, I Must Explain Things You Already Know-The Worst Waste of Telling Over Showing</u></b><br /> Hey guys, do you remember that one episode in Volume 3 where we got all we needed on Emerald's and Mercury's background? Have you been enjoying the way that Rooster Teeth has been telling you how they've been feeling and reacting now that their leader, Cinder, is no longer there to provide context on the sort of shit they've been getting up to? Have you felt rewarded for being a careful follower of the story they were telling through body language and meaningful production choices?<br /> <br /> Well, Rooster Teeth wants you to know that you were too stupid to pick up on any of that, because they decided to just spell it out for you and the rest of the dumb audience. That's what the beginning of this episode feels like to me.<br /> <br /> Like, I'm just sitting here and watching the dialogue between Emerald and Mercury slamming my head into the desk, constantly repeating &quot;YES, I KNOW, YOU SHOWED ME ALREADY. I KNOW THIS ALREADY.&quot; The only new thing I learned was that Mercury had his Semblance stolen from him by his father, which...I could have learned any number of other ways, namely entertaining ones where the elucidation of his situation might have an impact on one of our protagonists? Otherwise, I'm sitting here feeling talked down to by the show like I couldn't be expected to know this is <i>exactly</i> how they've been feeling and thinking all along because, you know, <i>I was watching the show</i>.<br /> <br /> And then Tyrion walks and I manage to lose <i>even more interest</i>. Team WTCH in general has been a bore. I'm still maintain interest in Cinder, though much like learning about Ozpin's immortality makes me less interested in what his actual story is, Cinder's relationship to Salem and the rest of the losers here makes me care less and less about what she wants, why she wants it, and where the root of her arc is. Hazel had the potential to be interesting but got shot with the most boring explanations and expressions in Volume 5. Watt is...vaguely interesting? Not enough to muster words for.<br /> <br /> And then there's Tyrion. From the moment this spiny tailed pissant appeared on screen, I have just wanted him to shut up. I hate him talking, I hate him worshipping, I hate him fighting, I hate him freaking out. His characterization is blunt and over-tried at, and he goes from being the sort of fun over the top you might enjoy in other characters to the sort of over the top that makes you wonder why no one else has killed him out of annoyance. The worst part is that he could have possibly worked, with the traits they gave him, as the minion of someone down the line, like maybe an assassin for Watts the same way Mercury is for Cinder-that would have been more rewarding to watch, but the fucking idiot ball as one of the four dragons for Salem, the big bad? His postion makes his hamminess fall apart. for me. He pisses me off so much it's hard to articulate what drives me nuts about him, beacause I'm too busy being mad that he exists.<br /> <br /> So anyways, Tyrion lays out some plot stuff and also exhorts the kids to, instead of being concerned with what they are getting out of their arrangement with Salem, to instead find joy in what they are doing, as a not-subtle way of explaining he would enjoying killing them like we hadn't picked up on that before hand, and like, that might be neat if I thought that was going to possibly move some things on the board of RWBY's story? Except that it's clearly not, because RWBY puts it's tells up like a big flaming dick on the horizon blaring &quot;These Hoes Ain't Loyal&quot; (that, yes, you hear from the horizon) RWBY does some things well, but effective intrigue with it's foreshadowing has never been one of them.<br /> <br /> Gah, I'm done with this part. What next?<br /> <br /> Oh. Right. Team RNJ.<br /> <br /> *sigh*<br /> <br /> <b><u>Team RNJ and The Lack Thereof-The A In Other A-Team Means Ass</u></b><br /> Okay, that's a little unfair, so let's back up a second.<br /> <br /> Some of you might remember the Volume 1 reviews I was doing when I was basically the only one with the subscription to Rooster Teeth. If you do, you might remember me not being too fond of team JNPR. I warmed up to them eventually, though, and by the time I got around to Volume 3, I actually really <i>sort</i> <i>of</i> dug them. I mean, okay, I never got into Ren and Nora, but I got into Jaune and Pyrrha to some extent, and I was, at the time, cool with everything that shook down for them at the end of Volume 3, and Hey, Look At That! There is a reason why they were here, all along! They're here to be Ruby's team in the meantime! And then we'll get to see them step up and become actual A Team material! Surely we'll discover all sorts of<br /> <br /> Look, that didn't happen. In fact, time and tide has made the remainder of Team RNJ kind of clearly lacking for place and purpose in the story. They feel like a relic of the first three Volumes that no one had the good sense to look over and rethink how to use them.<br /> <br /> They just haven't contributed much to the story. The comic relief has been, well, lacking-they never got laughs out of me that much to begin with but have literally not gotten an emotional reaction out of me for years. Character arcs and development? I do not have the hours tonight to explain how badly fucked up the story of Ren and Nora were in Volume 4, just suffice it to say that instead of an emotional journey that could have really fleshed out and made those two dynamic culminating in a catharsis of facing down their demons, we got told about their demons the laziest way possible before ending it and, oh, I guess Ren and Nora can be a couple now, like anything's going to come of that for the story. As for Jaune-Well Jaune is about to get his own griping session, but for now, know that &quot;they killed my girlfriend and I have feelings about&quot; loses out more and more over time. Plot action? No cunning plans, no badass rescues that didn't feel like they were there just to get it out of the way, no integral sacrifices or improvisations, nothing. Combat action? Eh, maybe, but I'm the guy who would have ended the Red Trailer on that first gunshot, so I'm not going to stress much out over that.<br /> <br /> RNJ just hasn't had anything to do and hasn't even tried to go out of their way to do more, and I just sit here with the problem of thinking that most of the roles they have been filling could have been filled by other people (Particularly Qrow, since the evolution of his relationship with Ruby from &quot;cool uncle&quot; to &quot;flawed adult&quot; has been the main thrust of her interpersonal relationships in the show since Volume 4 anyways), and unfortunately, the open reminder that they could always just stay in Argus (which, unrelated, is actually a lovely city design and I am cribbing it) and their doubts about being involved with the fight against Salem really hammers down how much of a non-contribution they've been making. At a point where I should be like &quot;No, don't give up, I'm rooting for you guys!&quot; I really want them to sideline themselves, and that's a far way to fall going from unexpectedly shouting with glee at a victory for a blonde-haired shit I hated a lot up to the point when he took a stand against a bear.<br /> <br /> Speaking of.<br /> <br /> <b><u>She Should Be Standing Here-Jaune and Pyrrha and How Things Have Gone</u></b><br /> I need to briefly explain the series of events before I get into this, so episode recap from where we last left off:<br /> <br /> So Team RNJ and Jaune's sister Saffron (yay lesbian representation, btw) are strolling through the city, looking around for Oscar and generally feeling depressed. Saffron, at one point, makes the above suggestion that they could just stay in Argus, do some good here and just quit the mission, and Jaune lays out that it's not that easy. Saffron leaves, and Jaune goes to sit down and feel bad, and after spying a cafe, Nora and Red decide to go get drinks and let Jaune have some time to himself. Jaune, feeling antsy as much as he feels depressed, gets up, and walks into the park across the street.<br /> <br /> And there he finds it. The thing that broke me. You could not have been more hamfisted or schmaltzy if you had had the heavens open and the angels sing out and the trumpets sound and from the celestial chorus descendeth the Holiest of Holy Girlfriends. There's a temple with John Goodman sitting on a throne that would have been less mind-numbingly jarring and ill-thought out to walk into than this. A sense of loss and respect and clarity and wonder were all lost by the god damn audacity of this park.<br /> <br /> Because in the middle of that park, gentle reader, was a <i>fucking huge memorial statue to Pyrrha Nikos</i>. Because <i>of fucking course he does</i>.<br /> <br /> Jesus Fucking Christ.<br /> <br /> Okay, gotta do more before I strip this apart, I can do this.<br /> <br /> SO.<br /> <br /> The music plays, and he approaches the statue of Her Exalted Girlfriendness For This Loser(Who Is You), and he is about to have a reaction, then goes to leave when GASP! A woman who could possibly be anyone and certainly not Pyrrha's mother talks to him. They spend some time telling you things you already knew and that Jaune already knew and doesn't really change anything, and then Ren and Nora come back and and there's more telling each other things they already knew and that we already knew, and one actually really heartwarming note from Nora and Ren establishing that Jaune has got to stop thinking of himself the way he does and they love him that really should have been expanded on and delivered on instead, but anyways, the stuff is said, and now it's time to go back to the house.<br /> <br /> Okay, caught up? Caught up. Good. Let's get the minor stuff out of the way.<br /> <br /> One, once again, 90% of the dialogue doesn't actually change anything, for the character or the viewers. As mentioned, the most effective thing was Nora and Red telling Jaune that they loved him and as such valued him and really gave a real sense that he needs to start understanding how to belong and draw inspiration from the others around him and to similarly inspire and strengthen the people around him instead of being hung up on his dead girlfriend. That aside, everything is shit that has been established and easily inferred from conversation mid-volume 3 onwards. This conversation did nothing for confronting their actual sense of weakness and non-contribution to the affairs of things. By and large, it's like Jaune got reminded to do his laundry. We got no sense of the dynamics that led to Pyrrha being who she was and how we or the characters could learn the same lessons she did and become more like her, nothing genuinely aspirational or inspirational for anyone.<br /> <br /> Two, okay, on a nitpick level, am I the only one who remembers how part of the problem that sparked the downfall of Beacon was Pyrrha overkilling a student and having that only be marginally be okay because it turned out the student was actually a really shady robot program on Atlas's part and therefore is probably actually something of a persona non grata? Like, admittedly, I was always curious why a student dying in this pretty hardcore tournament was a thing that Cinder would make a deal out of, but since it was, it's still worth noting that Pyrrha <i>overkilled a fellow student</i>. That's not a thing people are just okay with. You wanna tell me there's a memorial, sure, but not a huge fucking statue, you don't want to start celebrating your town pride over the woman who sparked all this shit happening.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the scene could have just worked with Jaune meeting up with Pyrrha's mother and talking, and in fact that, would have been a lot more quiet and intimate and heartfelt, particularly if you picked up on the unease of people around Mrs. Nikos and the relief she would have gotten just from finally being allowed to be openly proud of her daughter with someone who knew her and what happened.<br /> <br /> As is, the scene is stupidly overwrought and overblown and it takes me right out of it. It's just so. It's so on the nose. It's so <i>convenient</i>. It's just hamfisted and schmaltzy and even obvious that it just kills everything in it.<br /> <br /> By itself, it's just <i>bad</i>. It is <i>fucking</i> lazy storytelling. But there's a line that forces you to think outside of it, and it is a problem that has hung over RWBY since Volume 3, and will hang over it from here on.<br /> <br /> &quot;She should be standing here.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean. Yeah. She should be.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing-Jaune just doesn't have that much dramatic potential. No one in RNJ particularly had it to begin with. Consider, by contrast, Team RWBY-everyone in that story has complicated, dramatic relationships with people who hold power over major cogs in the world's wheelhouse that create a natural narrative arc for claiming power and responsibility in service to the ultimate conflict with Salem-Weiss has the Schnee Dust Company, Blake the White Fang, Yang the Branwen Tribe who even Salem didn't want to lightly fuck with, and Ruby her relationship to Taiyang and Qrow and closer relationship to Ozpin, plus she also gets to skate through with her being the Silver Eyed Special.<br /> <br /> Now consider RNJ. Ren had that potential, but his story is <i>almost</i> effective as a sort of failed state of that-someone who, had things gone differently, been in a position much like anyone on Team RWBY. Nora <i>might</i> still have it, but realistically her role is set and matched here, and I don't expect any real change or introductions of interesting dynamics with her. And then you have Jaune, who for all that he feels like a big deal is pretty openly a nobody in the story. THat is how they decided to play him, it was the text of the climax of Volume 5.<br /> <br /> On top of that, all of his fury and sorrow just sort of feels like a thing. He's Mad Because His Girlfriend Is Dead, and Because Some People Work Behind the Scenes, They Deserve His Ire. I know it has more logic than that, but it doesn't have any emotional or dramatic weight than that. Every conflict he has is not actually a conflict for him, it's just him being mad about his perfect girlfriend dying. It all rings hollow and cheap coming from him. A lot of his conflict just feels like that.<br /> <br /> Because, really, honestly, the better story would have been if he died fighting Cinder instead of Pyrrha.<br /> <br /> No, think about it, really think about it. Think about what that would have done to the story. Jaune's arc was always that he felt like a loser who had to stand up to expectations and realistically couldn't. He wanted to be a hero even though he couldn't actually rattle up a proper heroic effort. He had a good mind for approaching things, because his weakness made him look for advantages-but Jaune has always needed to prove to himself that he could Put Up The Fight, not just provide the clever idea. His most natural conclusion is to defy the fates that seem laid out in front of him and a loved one, and put up his best effort, and maybe even still have it be pathetic-but still be just enough to have made a difference. Imagine how gratifying it would have been for the kid who could never do anything got to go out doing <i>just enough</i>.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Pyrrha was always the girl who was going to die. Part of that is because she <i>was</i> the perfect girlfriend for Jaune (don't glare at me like that, that is one hundred percent of the logic of her characterization). She was always a setup for a punchline involving Jaune and Ruby getting together (Speaking of, oh yeah, that's inevitable kids) and basically just serving as tinder for Jaune's arc. But imagine if Jaune had flipped the script on her?<br /> <br /> First off, the blatancy of her story is instantly subverted. Everything that had been sloppily just laid out like it's the most natural thing in the world would have been pulled out from under us, and we'd have gotten a genuine surprise instead. Second, It would have taken her context and out of being nothing more than Jaune's perfect girlfriend, there's now this story world after character concept that's full and rich and ripe. She has a whole range of dynamic relationships to explore while <i>that</i> hole is being filled, and all of it is intriguing because none of us were waiting for it. Her relationship with Ruby, Ren, and Nora would not only be drastically different from Jaune's, but from the sort of stuff we're used to in storytelling. She would have to go and become someone else entirely new, both in her own eyes, the eyes of her peers, and the eyes of the audience.<br /> <br /> And you know, the place that starts her off as is just way more interesting too. After all, she's still a champion and legendary figure to a lot of people, who should, by all rights, still have a lot of clout as it goes-except that's now all tainted by the murder of another student and the starter of the Fall of Beacon. Her reputation is compromised, and that's a thing that would haunt the group from then on and demand a fight with a lot of complicated questions to answer in order to fix. That's a situation filled with an inherent push-and-pull, inherent tension, that has room to create a lot of narrative scenarios that would be rewarding to follow-up on. And that's before you get on her personal involvement with a lot of the major reveals since Volume 3, mixed in with the fact that she can wrap up the same sort of angst that Jaune has in the same thing, except that it hurts even more, because his brilliant heroism just highlights how much <i>she</i> failed<i>, particularly </i>since she has more all the more power to make the difference.<br /> <br /> I can't watch this episode without being forcibly reminded of how RWBY took the laziest option for that entire story thread, which is a problem that RWBY frequently has-that so many things are done just because it seems like that's how you do, much like the attitude of this entire Volume. And more importantly, it reinforces that, yeah, a sizable portion of our protagonists shouldn't be standing here, because they have contributed nothing.<br /> <br /> You'd think it would end there, but NOPE.<br /> <br /> <b><u>OH FOR FUCK'S SAKE-What Narrative Tension?</u></b><br /> Okay, so we resolved a major thread of doubt that's been going on for some of our heroes. Nevermind no one cared about it, because the problem was not only obvious but really in line with what they were doing, nevermind that it happened with characters who could disappear from the story at this point and not change anything-we got a Character Moment, and from There We Can Change Things. So back to the main problem. RNJ may have found new heart, but Oscar is still out there in the city, possibly lost, definitely still emotionally conflicted, still feeling diseased from the man who will take over his soul some day, still alienated from the rest of the group as the carrier of this Ozpin, so now it's surely up to RNJ to find him and make amends, so they can all come together and<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>HE IS LITERALLY JUST WAITING FOR THEM AT HOME, MAKING THEM ALL DINNER.</i></u></b><br /> <br /> Did. Did the plot just give up? Did the writer's just give up? What even the fuck.<br /> <br /> I trust I don't need to tell you how ending the narrative tension of the last episode's ending by just having that all work out in the end is just plain bad, but I'm going to-THIS WAS A BIG DEAL. Oscar was clearly upset, and he was clearly going to need to have some connections made-and instead, it's just solved. Like, WHat?!<br /> <br /> This isn't like the episodes of Black and White, back in Volume 1, where in Weiss changed her mind after a day of walking around, I should note (because I can see some of you thinking that and even possibly remembering how I wrote positively about it back in the day). Going with a quick comparison, the big difference is that we <i>got to see</i> Weiss thinking about it, and even got to see it cleverly portrayed, by both the subtle shifts of her dialogue and her body language. You could see her going at like a mature adolescent, someone who was literally growing up while working out her feelings and thoughts on the subject throughout a long, hard day, taking into account what everyone else was saying and doing in response to Blake. That might be over-reading a scene, but at a bare minimum, there are scenes of her possible growth to over read. Here, he's just-gone and then back and over everything.<br /> <br /> And you know, it's not like elements of this couldn't have been kept. HE COULD have been out shopping for dinner stuff as away to clear his mind and sort stuff out-he could have been found by Team RNJ contemplating the clothes, the active part of his brain telling him to sort step up, and make the changes to himself but the darker parts telling him to drop everything and just go back home, and they could have had a brief but mature apology-and-discussion of empathy and understanding, and Jaune could finalize that arc of his and help Oscar also actualize a character point of his own, well and truly fully stepping up into being both a contribution to this team and the Opener of the Way for Ozpin.<br /> <br /> But instead, he's just back home, fully actualized, having grown up entirely off screen and just WHAT THE FUCK IS THIS WRITING.<br /> <br /> And then they come up with the kernel of an idea for how to get to Atlas and Qrow has some crow shoved down his throat and that part's actually pretty satisfying.<br /> <br /> <b><u>I Can't Even This Episode-In Conclusion</u></b><br /> As I've mentioned, some of this is just tip of the iceberg for me. I like RWBY a lot in spite of itself more than because of it. RWBY is a <i>very</i> flawed series-but where it has fun and heart, it shines really strongly. But by contrast, some episodes are just so flat and hollow and paint-by-the-numbers that not only does it break with the logic of the show itself, but it completely makes you forget that the show <i>does have heart</i>. Previously, that episode was Kuroyuri, and that one is still really bad. And asides from that, RWBY managed to avoid breaking it's narrow tendons keeping it together.<br /> <br /> But Lost is just astonishingly lazy. It's the sort of episode that just evokes an onslaught of &quot;because of course&quot; after &quot;because of course&quot; It spends time telling you things you already know while not really thinking about things it should have thought of, and all of it so flatly predictable and unfleshed out you'd be better served reading TV Tropes-and to make matters worse, it just highlights <i>how much</i> RWBY gets by on that sort of logic. RWBY doesn't have isolated flaws, little nicks and scratches that can be ignored, but instead has some deep structural issues as a result of the way it fails to consider the consequences of what it's doing.<br /> <br /> Back at the end of Volume 1, I mentioned that I had fallen in love with the heart of the show, but that the best way I could think of to sell RWBY was a show for newbies into anime as a means of quickly learning the &quot;language&quot; of the movement. I thought, after the way Volumes 2 and 3 had developed, I was going to eventually turn out wrong-but the most depressing thing, after these three Volumes from there?<br /> <br /> Is that I'm forced to consider just how right I was to begin with. And that's not where I wanted RWBY to end up.<br /> <br /> Ah well, we'll see where it goes from here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-27-2019, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T12:54:31-08:00","id":1278670,"title":"","content":"It's telling that it took me almost a year after volume 5 of RWBY stopped airing for me to actually finish watching it. One night I had nothing to do, I decided to catch up on the show, largely because I'd heard good things about the new volume.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, it really looks much better when you view it all at once.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it's no surprise that volume 5 lost me. By comparison, as a whole, volume 6 is much better structured. It has stuff like, y'know, dramatic arcs in individual episodes, and a sense of forward momentum on several fronts. Where volume 5 felt like it had decided that it was going to be about team RWBY coming together again and that was <i>all</i> that was going to happen, volume 6 sprinkles with gradual progression and new hooks all over the place. <a href=\"https://youtu.be/nxa3gEAuBxM\" target=\"_blank\">This meme gets it about right.</a><br /> <br /> This RWBY works for me. I'm not going to get as excited about it as I was at the starts (and the end of volume 3), but if it keeps this up, it's certainly worth a few nights a year to keep up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T13:28:11-08:00","id":1278681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1278670#post1278670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's telling that it took me almost a year after volume 5 of RWBY stopped airing for me to actually finish watching it. One night I had nothing to do, I decided to catch up on the show, largely because I'd heard good things about the new volume.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like when I dropped <i>RWBY </i>after getting stuck on Jaune's arc, and only started watching again in time to get caught up for Volume 3.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll admit, it really looks much better when you view it all at once. </div> </div> </div>They're essentially movies, and I wonder what it would be like if Rooster Teeth would release them as such, instead of treating them like a TV show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T13:47:37-08:00","id":1278687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1278681#post1278681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like when I dropped <i>RWBY </i>after getting stuck on Jaune's arc, and only started watching again in time to get caught up for Volume 3.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They're essentially movies, and I wonder what it would be like if Rooster Teeth would release them as such, instead of treating them like a TV show.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question! I think it might potentially help the show content-wise, since it would necessitate a tighter direction and less filler time which unfortunately has been an issue since day one, but they'd lose much of the &quot;exposure time&quot; of having an airing show for the fans to swarm around.<br /> <br /> That said, I also think this volume is among the strongest in terms of adapting to the episodic format so far, as said above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T14:30:06-08:00","id":1278704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1278687#post1278687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good question! I think it might potentially help the show content-wise, since it would necessitate a tighter direction and less filler time which unfortunately has been an issue since day one, but they'd lose much of the &quot;exposure time&quot; of having an airing show for the fans to swarm around.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my take, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I also think this volume is among the strongest in terms of adapting to the episodic format so far, as said above. </div> </div> </div>It does, with forgivable exceptions like The Grimm Reaper, which will be perfectly fine as one part of a movie, but which would have seemed a bit unfocused as an episode.<br /> <br /> But that's why &quot;episodes&quot; are actually called &quot;chapters&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T16:05:44-08:00","id":1278720,"title":"","content":"I tend to watch through episode by episode and then all of it at once at the end of the series, because one of the interesting(and sometimes problematic) aspects of RWBY is that it tries to be both &quot;weekly series&quot; and &quot;extended movie.&quot;<br /> <br /> Tell you what, the theater viewings of RWBY are always fun.<br /> <br /> And to be fair, a) definitely better pacing in this season, and b) when we get around to character development outside of the conflict of the season and what Lost did, the character development has been pretty darn cool.<br /> <br /> It's just that I don't buy into the main conflict arc of the volume. There's better ways to induce the kind of despair they're going for in the characters than what they did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-04-2019, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T18:41:14-08:00","id":1278741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1278262#post1278262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing-Jaune just doesn't have that much dramatic potential. No one in RNJ particularly had it to begin with. Consider, by contrast, Team RWBY-everyone in that story has complicated, dramatic relationships with people who hold power over major cogs in the world's wheelhouse that create a natural narrative arc for claiming power and responsibility in service to the ultimate conflict with Salem-Weiss has the Schnee Dust Company, Blake the White Fang, Yang the Branwen Tribe who even Salem didn't want to lightly fuck with, and Ruby her relationship to Taiyang and Qrow and closer relationship to Ozpin, plus she also gets to skate through with her being the Silver Eyed Special.</div> </div> </div> </div>tl;dr: Jaune's real semblance is manpain.<br /> <br /> Also, this is an aside, but anyone who likes RWBY and X-Com should perhaps consider playing <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/470310/Troubleshooter/\" target=\"_blank\">Troubleshooter</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T19:27:28-08:00","id":1278745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1278741#post1278741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tl;dr: Jaune's real semblance is manpain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could have gone with a better paragraph, but yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T05:52:25-08:00","id":1278806,"title":"","content":"Also, another thing that your post reminded me I hate is how... generic the villains are? They feel like broad caricatures that never really got filled in. Their plot arcs are boring generic anime plot arcs with nothing interesting or unique to them, all of it telegraphed years in advance.<br /> <br /> Honestly, Roman was a better villain than these people. I mean, yes, his motivation was <i>also</i> just &quot;is Chaotic Evil&quot;, but at least he had a bit more style than them.<br /> <br /> I think part of the reason I focus on how utterly reprehensible their demon-gods is is because it's the place where the story went from &quot;following the rails with minimal self-awareness&quot; to &quot;so little awareness of the actual implications and meaning of what's happening onscreen that it jumped the rails and smashed into the proverbial wall.&quot;<br /> <br /> I <i>seriously</i> do think there was no more thought put into the God of Light than &quot;he shines yellow, calls himself a god, and talks in a deep soothing voice, therefore he is axiomatically right and people need to win his approval again.&quot; And the thinking behind the God of Darkness was &quot;what if evil dark monster god, but, <i>twist</i>, not evil because The Balance.&quot; And they also wanted to give Salem an angsty backstory so they also had their stupid gods do stupid terrible stuff to her and her entire world with virtually no provocation, and nobody involved in the project was actually bothering to put enough thought into it to consider how it looked as a whole.<br /> <br /> Sort of like how the entire cast freaking out about Salem not being killable to death feels like it's there because there was an &quot;everyone freaks out and is mad at Ozpin and sad here&quot; spot written in the overarching plan, but nobody really thought it through in any detail.<br /> <br /> Like... even putting aside the fact that there's other solutions, they weren't even actually talking about killing Salem until this season. Her name was only <i>mentioned</i> to the heroes for the first time last season. They barely know who she is and don't even know what her plan is - for that matter, why do they want to kill her? All they ever got out of Ozpin, that I can recall, is &quot;she wants the relics because mumblemumble. And we have to stop her because mumblemumble.&quot; Even the vision barely touched on it.<br /> <br /> At one point in this episode, what's-her-name asked why they couldn't just go do other stuff, and <i>that's a very good question</i>. Whatever vague evil plot Salem is trying to do, she's been trying to do it for a long time without success. Right now, she doesn't even seem that much closer to it than she ever did before - I guess she still has the Fall Maiden? And one of the relics is outside the vault? But the fall of Beacon doesn't actually seem to have helped her. If they hunted down Cinder and killed her (and maybe Emerald, too, who is the only plausible person on Team Salem who could inherit the Fall Maiden power) Salem would be almost back at square zero. They'd have to hide one relic again, but so what, Ozpin managed it once already, starting from less than this.<br /> <br /> This is probably a plotting issue - they're saving the big reveal of Salem's evil plot for later, and, <i>yes</i>, of course it will be genocide because the writers have no subtly and no self-awareness. But the heroes don't seem to have caught on to that. And at the same time, the writers also want to shift focus towards Salem so the overarching plot can move forwards, but... these two things don't work together?<br /> <br /> (Also, this would be more acceptable if it was just the kids who were freaking out - they're kids, ok, fine, they can be dumb. Qrow is an experienced hunter and doesn't have any such excuse, yet he's hit the hardest because the plot demands it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T16:53:43-08:00","id":1278895,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So it turns out the base commander of Argus is a better villain than most.<br /> <br /> Also, oh yeah, Adam's here.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-06-2019, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T21:35:09-08:00","id":1278912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com