tNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Well. Post broken aura he got stabbed in heart and lung, then he hit his head on a rock at near terminal velocity, to then fall terminally again on water.<br /> It is well said, the only way he can appear again is with resurrection levels of bullshit. Something I'd expect Salem or the gods to do, and that's about it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I get writer's finding ways to keep doors open, but then there's being pretty damn thorough as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T11:09:15-08:00","id":1282157,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">RWBY has a tendency to forget it's own world building so I'm glad that rolling out the giant mech had these consequences. I thought Adam was used relatively well by the standards of a character who wore out his welcome for me last season.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T06:26:19-08:00","id":1282279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1282157#post1282157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">RWBY has a tendency to forget it's own world building so I'm glad that rolling out the giant mech had these consequences. I thought Adam was used relatively well by the standards of a character who wore out his welcome for me last season.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, another thing that's been handled poorly until this season is racism against the faunus, its never really been visible in a way that implies the systematic way its been described in the lore. Both Cordovin's casual racism and Adam's brand imply way more than what we've seen before: Roman's slurs(which were neither taken seriously be the freaking White Fang nor a reason for him to avoid doing business with them), Cardin being the dudebro douchebag he is, and a &quot;No Faunus&quot; sign in a low income area. But Cordovin has legitimate(if poorly assigned) access to military equipment(and thus systematic authority to act on her prejudices) and Adam's brand hints at a slave labor project involving the SDC (which is basically a cyberpunk megacorp at this point, i'm thinking probably one of the Japanacorps from Shadowrun).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T08:43:04-08:00","id":1282290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1282279#post1282279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, another thing that's been handled poorly until this season is racism against the faunus, its never really been visible in a way that implies the systematic way its been described in the lore. Both Cordovin's casual racism and Adam's brand imply way more than what we've seen before: Roman's slurs(which were neither taken seriously be the freaking White Fang nor a reason for him to avoid doing business with them), Cardin being the dudebro douchebag he is, and a &quot;No Faunus&quot; sign in a low income area. But Cordovin has legitimate(if poorly assigned) access to military equipment(and thus systematic authority to act on her prejudices) and Adam's brand hints at a slave labor project involving the SDC (which is basically a cyberpunk megacorp at this point, i'm thinking probably one of the Japanacorps from Shadowrun).</div> </div> </div> </div>What are the actual mistakes and what were limitations of the narrative there, though?<br /> <br /> It's not like the characters were shown much outside &quot;complete wilderness&quot;, &quot;a school that clearly is built mostly by people that think otherwise&quot; (which makes sense considering its cultural roots and the fact anyone there is a terrifyingly strong fighter and highly likely to be willing to act on the offence), &quot;a haven that the people fighting against discrimination got for themselves and reign absolute&quot; (menagerie) and, briefly, mistral and argos.<br /> These are evidence that such racism is not ubiquitous, and that it follows diverse cultural lines. Which is close to how it works in the real world, you know? Peoples' ideas shift differently based on the different circumstances in which they live.<br /> <br /> So I agree it's not very visible. But it didn't feel, to me, nonsensical. They almost never went to places where it'd make sense for such discrimination to be pervasive, much less the norm, but not in a way that denotes &quot;the decried discrimination is not as common as they complained it is&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> If anything, what really broke sense for me is why it persisted the way it did before a threat like the grimm. Common enemies are excellent ways to persuade different people to band together. Precariousness is a magnifier for both violence and selflessness. Few things are more precarious than literal boogeymen indistinctly eating both standard human and faunus human. Whatever happened to overcome <b>that</b> huge (both magnitude and duration) stimulus to band together requires explanations that were not given (our sampling of hunters correlates well with this, for example). The alternative would be making such prejudice a recent development, and that's not how it was portrayed, thus demanding further explanation as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 01-23-2019, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T09:48:45-08:00","id":1282300,"title":"","content":"The problem before is that developer commentary said that Faunus racism the level we saw from Torchwick is the norm in Remnant, Team RWBY and JNR are outliers. And outside threats like the Grimm don't necessarily provide a catalyst for unity. Since its an environmental, not a political or ideological threat, space and resources are limited, that can lead to tribalism and xenophobia and Faunus traits(or lack thereof) provide a handy outgroup identifier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T10:14:07-08:00","id":1282305,"title":"","content":"Yes, it absolutely makes sense that if a story takes place in locations where a setting element doesn't exist strongly, it won't be very visible.<br /> But then you have to ask yourself: Why is it a setting element, if you're setting the story away from it?<br /> Either a setting element is important, in which case the writer should take steps to ensure it has enough visibility, or it isn't important or shown much, in which case it won't be a strong source of drama to use.<br /> <br /> I personally found the Faunus discrimination was reasonably strongly portrayed, by the standards of this show at least, but I do understand that some might feel that a story including a faunus as a protagonist should devote more focus to what that means.<br /> <br /> As for everyone banding together against the grim: Humans are great at unifying against outside threats as long as the in-group doesn't run out of resources (room, food, jobs etc). As soon as there isn't enough to go around, we are all to happy to splinter into ever smaller in-groups and exclude ever more people into new out-groups. And then all it takes is one Adam and a war starts.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T10:29:39-08:00","id":1282307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1282300#post1282300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem before is that developer commentary said that Faunus racism the level we saw from Torchwick is the norm in Remnant, Team RWBY and JNR are outliers. And outside threats like the Grimm don't necessarily provide a catalyst for unity. Since its an environmental, not a political or ideological threat, space and resources are limited, that can lead to tribalism and xenophobia and Faunus traits(or lack thereof) provide a handy outgroup identifier.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I dislike death of the author, I gotta point out that there's where that perspective matters-if we don't watch the developer commentary, how are we to know that Torchwick's level of racism is the norm of Remnant?<br /> <br /> Like, it's clear that racism exists and that there are pockets of really terrible systemic actions against the Faunus, buuuuut we never get what the average day is like on that subject from the show-the realities of racism in the world of Remnant is lacking a lot of textual space.<br /> <br /> Now mind you, they don't have to go out of their way to show us that &quot;OH DAMN, people are racist&quot;, per se, much like they don't have to show us the abuse Blake suffered before at the hands of Adam for us to believe it-but the show has been hesitant to really include the world element of that conflict in the text they've had so far outside of stating the flat morals of it. We've had exaggerated examples, which is actually fine, but the mundane, banal version of that evil has been missing. Society has, by and large, been ignored in favor of the mission or for the character drama, and not so much on the character vs society aspect of the story, even going so far as to have a lot of it's world building handled by the World of Remnant sections rather than finding ways to integrate that information into the show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-23-2019, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T03:39:59-08:00","id":1282403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1282305#post1282305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it absolutely makes sense that if a story takes place in locations where a setting element doesn't exist strongly, it won't be very visible.<br /> But then you have to ask yourself: Why is it a setting element, if you're setting the story away from it?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I'm asking what is writing flaw and what is not.<br /> The writer commenting that it is more ubiquitous than we saw shows they are not showing it correctly.<br /> If they intended for them to be more exposed to it, then they failed, and that is pretty much the pacing problem the show has if you think about it XD<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T11:03:12-08:00","id":1282462,"title":"","content":"I <i>really</i> disliked the way the Faunus arc was handled last season. We've gotten very little focus on the racism Faunus face or the reasons why the White Fang exists, and a huge amount of focus on the Faunus who go &quot;too far.&quot; The show makes vague handwavy statements about how to make the world better, but aggressively hates on any concrete examples beyond just &quot;be nice and hope racism just sort of fades away.&quot;<br /> <br /> The end result is that the current White Fang seems to have sprung from nowhere for no reason and is doing evil for the sake of doing evil (IIRC this was unambiguously stated for Adam - he wants an excuse to hurt people.) There's also an implication that anti-Faunus racism is something for the Faunus to handle (by being nice to everyone else and dealing with the White Fang themselves and so on), rather than something that the rest of the world holds responsibility for.<br /> <br /> I mean, showing only minimal amounts of anti-Faunus racism is one thing - if it just wasn't the focus of the show, I could understand that. But showing minimal amounts of it and <i>also</i> having an intense arc-long focus on how awful the White Fang is (and especially Adam personally, as its main representative in the show given that Sienna survived less than one episode) feels like it's minimizing the real-world issues involved in favor of a dumb reflexive-centrist &quot;we should do something, but nothing <i>too</i> extreme!&quot; that never leads anywhere.<br /> <br /> Also, aside from very early on when Blake was first being introduced, the show has repeatedly ignored the fact that the Faunus arc concerns Weiss, too. Her family is responsible for a lot of what the Faunus are suffering through. There's a lot more room for character development and discussion over what her responsibility is - but instead it only focuses on the Faunus who are going too far, not on the non-Faunus main character who has (or at least had), notionally, both the power and responsibility to do something about this.<br /> <br /> For that matter, hold on, did Adam know who Weiss was? Why was he ignoring her? You'd think the fact that Blake was literally close friends to the (former) heir to the Schnee Dust Company would be something that would set Adam off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 01-24-2019, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T11:27:34-08:00","id":1282466,"title":"","content":"Speaking of not showing things correctly, I heard Rooster Teeth has finally codified the visual effects for Aura Break versus Low Aura.<br /> <br /> Aura Break is when you get one full body shimmer followed by a rising particle effect, like an energy shield just broke into pieces and drifted off.<br /> <br /> Shimmers around a point of impact or multiple full-body shimmers with no particle effect only show &quot;low Aura&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe what we saw in Volume 4 with Qrow versus Tyrian didn't involve either of them actually breaking each other's Aura, but simply getting down to &quot;tournament disqualification&quot; levels, and maybe if either of them actually suffered Total Aura Break, they wouldn't have been able to leap around like supermen anymore?<br /> <br /> Given how they both actually suffered injury, perhaps Low Aura / &quot;tournament disqualification levels&quot; means that you no longer have enough Aura to protect yourself from harm, and thus why Tyrian's stinger worked and Ruby was able to cut off his tail?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T20:51:44-08:00","id":1282572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, aside from very early on when Blake was first being introduced, the show has repeatedly ignored the fact that the Faunus arc concerns Weiss, too. Her family is responsible for a lot of what the Faunus are suffering through. There's a lot more room for character development and discussion over what her responsibility is - but instead it only focuses on the Faunus who are going too far, not on the non-Faunus main character who has (or at least had), notionally, both the power and responsibility to do something about this. </div> </div> </div>When did Weiss notionally have any power over company policy? Her dad set policy not her. She could only do something once he kicked a bucket and she inherited the company.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For that matter, hold on, did Adam know who Weiss was? Why was he ignoring her? You'd think the fact that Blake was literally close friends to the (former) heir to the Schnee Dust Company would be something that would set Adam off. </div> </div> </div>His cuck senses were tingling and let him know which member of the team she was being shipped with so he focused on Yang as the main 'stealer' of Blake?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 01-25-2019, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T21:30:38-08:00","id":1282580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1282572#post1282572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When did Weiss notionally have any power over company policy? Her dad set policy not her. She could only do something once he kicked a bucket and she inherited the company.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost of the wealth and privilege she inherited - plus the big famous title that meant so much to her - were all built, at least in part, on oppressing the Faunus. When she first met Blake her reaction was &quot;eew, a disgusting Faunus terrorist who blows up my family's stuff for no reason!&quot; And as I recall, the resolution to that - while it's been a while - was a weaksauce &quot;racism is bad, mmkay&quot; with a dash of &quot;both sides have a point.&quot;<br /> <br /> But that doesn't, you know, make that history go away. As long as she identifies with the company, its wealth, and its reputation (and she certainly doesn't seem to have repudiated it), she also has to carry responsibility for the stuff it did. I mean she <i>could</i> intentionally walk away, or focus on plans to redeem it, but so far it's been mostly ignored. Nobody cares. <i>Adam</i> not caring is just the most bizarre example of it.<br /> <br /> And she does have power. Especially when she was the heir, she had the ability to send messages about what the company's priorities would be once she was in power, which would affect how people viewed it today and might influence policy to an extent (she could also have been ousted for this, but it would have been an important stand on her part.) And even once she's ousted she continues to have power - there are other people who see that what the company's doing is wrong; by establishing herself as the &quot;candidate&quot; for reconciliation with and reparations to the Faunus, she could send the message that the company's policy is not locked in. This would lead to pressure on her father to restore her as the heir in order to resolve the conflict.<br /> <br /> And if he refused (as he very well might), she would be in a position to do more <i>damage</i> to the company, further destroying its reputation, crippling its future growth, and forcing it to either change or make way for companies that will. The sight of the (former) Schnee Dust Company heiress openly acknowledging its crimes and denouncing it for them would lend a huge amount of credence to the idea that its crimes are serious things that have to actually be discussed and dealt with within Atlus society, rather than just being insignificant gripes that only outsiders or madmen like Adam care about. She has a platform to denounce past crimes against the faunus and advocate for change that is <i>vastly</i> beyond anything Blake could ever dream of.<br /> <br /> Of course, all of this would require actual risk and sacrifice on her part. But that's why it would make a better story. We might still see it - we haven't really gotten an Atlus-focused story with the entire cast yet, and that's presumably coming up soon. But there hasn't even been any real build up towards it - it feels like the show has totally forgotten how the Weiss / Atlus story is interconnected with the Blake / Faunus one.<br /> <br /> And the underlying thing that really annoys me about this is that it effectively sends the message that faunus rights is just Blake's story - that it's her responsibility to free herself and her people, when <i>Weiss</i>, in fact, is the one who grew up with the backing and support and privilege of a vast fortune that was extracted at their expense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> His cuck senses were tingling and let him know which member of the team she was being shipped with so he focused on Yang as the main 'stealer' of Blake? </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but his driving motivation (other than possessiveness of Blake) is supposed to be revenge against the people who hurt the Faunus, and, in his eyes, Schnee Dust Company is near the top of the list. It's weird that he's completely ignored the fact that Blake was / is palling around with its (former) heiress.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T22:19:00-08:00","id":1282586,"title":"","content":"Weiss doesn't need to have any power to be a target for Adam. Simply the knowledge that he could hurt her father through hurting her should have been enough for a revenge driven villain like Adam to be at least tempted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T00:35:38-08:00","id":1282595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1282586#post1282586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weiss doesn't need to have any power to be a target for Adam. Simply the knowledge that he could hurt her father through hurting her should have been enough for a revenge driven villain like Adam to be at least tempted.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, and I feel like if Adam had encountered Weiss first at Beacon then he probably would have gone after her instead of Blake since that would have been in the scope of his agendas and ,Cinder having a fire knife to his neck aside, he seemed pretty happy that if he wasn't where he wanted to be exactly he was at least on track for it. Blake was a target of some import to him for personal reasons when she showed up ergo he did what he did. Once they got back to Menagerie then the problem became that Blake started being a threat to his authority and direct goals followed by actually getting him ousted from his desired position of power.<br /> <br /> So at this point Blake has compounded personal grudges from Adam and well at this last junction he's pretty firmly in the camp of getting revenge on the person he feels ruined his life. In that regard Weiss would be a target on the grounds that she is someone Blake cares about first and foremost any other relationships are secondary. <br /> <br /> Though on a different note, show of hands people hoping scorpion boy bites it before the end of the season? Just he's not interesting to me. He doesn't have any nuances so far and his goals and reasons seem to be that he views Salem as a divinity, at least with what he calls her, and I guess he likes killing people. He doesn't add anything of interest, he has pretty much no interaction with he rest of Salem's underlings aside from a fondness for for intimidating and scaring Emerald and Mercury. Which isn't that interesting either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T01:21:22-08:00","id":1282598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1282580#post1282580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, but his driving motivation (other than possessiveness of Blake) is supposed to be revenge against the people who hurt the Faunus, and, in his eyes, Schnee Dust Company is near the top of the list. It's weird that he's completely ignored the fact that Blake was / is palling around with its (former) heiress.</div> </div> </div> </div>were you not paying attention. He didn't give two shits about the Faunus. It was all about him and him alone. He even said it himself. What the Schnees and their company did wasn't as bad as his property* rejecting him and declaring someone else more worthy. that was the point of the whole arc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *that's how narcissists always look at people<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T04:03:48-08:00","id":1282615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1282580#post1282580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And she does have power. Especially when she was the heir, she had the ability to send messages about what the company's priorities would be once she was in power, which would affect how people viewed it today and might influence policy to an extent (she could also have been ousted for this, but it would have been an important stand on her part.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Two steps out of line and she WAS ousted. Oppressive families are fun like that.<br /> <br /> And no, you can't expect someone who grew up on &quot;my family randomly died and almost all of it is to blame on faunus terrorists&quot; to be very conscious about it. Yes, even with the company's reputation. That's tribalism for you, it's a very human thing that you will find everywhere.<br /> Lo and behold, she did exactly what you'd expect from a reasonable, well-meaning person under those circumstances: After being shown there's more to it she dialed down and diversified her concerns.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T09:11:02-08:00","id":1282658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1282580#post1282580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And she does have power. Especially when she was the heir, she had the ability to send messages about what the company's priorities would be once she was in power</div> </div> </div> </div>And then she would instantly have the title of &quot;heir&quot; taken away from her. Just like when she defied her father in canon.<br /> <br /> Then Whitley becomes the heir, and what Weiss believes become meaningless. Congratulations on accomplishing nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T12:42:43-08:00","id":1282898,"title":"","content":"ok, pretty standard fare for an ending. a few thoughts:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Nice to see more of Summer. All the fan artists do her as looking exactly like Ruby, even down to the hair. Good to see they're not that similar. And pretty too. Tai was lucky.<br /> <br /> btw, how many Solars do you think it would take to beat that Leviathan? And at what Essence could one do it alone?<br /> <br /> I've been into Exalted too long. I guessed what Atlas was going to be not long after Qrow said his line.<br /> <br /> The Wicked Witch now has flying monkeys<br /> <img src=\"https://i.kym-cdn.com/entries/icons/original/000/017/204/CaptainAmerica1_zps8c295f96.JPG\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> And Salem, who till now was Orcus on His Throne, is entering the fray herself. This should be good.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 01-26-2019, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T13:56:42-08:00","id":1282906,"title":"","content":"It was an 'aight ending to an 'aight volume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T13:59:24-08:00","id":1282908,"title":"","content":"Anyone else like Neo's new outfit?<br /> <br /> I wonder with them getting new duds if this means others will too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/a