:"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T03:43:49-08:00","id":1284913,"title":"","content":"Vic Mignogna was just fired after sexual assaul allegations.<br /> <br /> And already the same incels who attacked the show for Bumble are alrady whining about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T05:57:45-08:00","id":1284928,"title":"","content":"Since his overall creepiness wasn't enough before, something new certainly came up.<br /> Well, it matters little. I'm more worried about them finding a good replacement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T12:29:06-08:00","id":1285033,"title":"","content":"It's more that enough people stuck their neck out to talk about the creepiness beyond the whisper network that it finally couldn't be ignored than any changes to the pattern, but yeah, long overdue.<br /> (That said, I had no idea previously, so I still got to experience fresh disappointment.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T12:54:35-08:00","id":1285039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285033#post1285033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more that enough people stuck their neck out to talk about the creepiness beyond the whisper network that it finally couldn't be ignored than any changes to the pattern, but yeah, long overdue.<br /> (That said, I had no idea previously, so I still got to experience fresh disappointment.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Has anything new happened or someone new come publicly forward?<br /> <br /> There have been complaints against Vic before, and his enemies made sure to bring them up when Rooster Teeth announced they were taking him on as Qrow's voice.<br /> <br /> I've been wondering if people started stirring up the same old rumors again because people who made a YouTube career out of mocking RWBY for the previous two or three Volumes can't find enough actual flaws in Volume 6 to attack. I know that at least one journalist took to attacking the recent DBZ Brolly movie where Vic was Broly's voice-actor.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rooster Teeth may not actually have any new reason to cut ties with Vic, so much as they might have decided that the controversy just won't stop coming back and they can't afford to deal with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do know I'm getting sick of people getting tried and convicted in the court of public opinion instead of courts of law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T13:16:13-08:00","id":1285049,"title":"","content":"...I can't even.<br /> Yes, there were recent testimonials on Twitter, there are a lot of pictures built up over the years, and fellow VAs are finally coming forward. It had nothing to do with RWBY at the outset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T16:34:14-08:00","id":1285076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285039#post1285039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do know I'm getting sick of people getting tried and convicted in the court of public opinion instead of courts of law.</div> </div> </div> </div>The level of sexual harassment that can get you fired from work is far, far below the level that can get you in trouble with the law. What &quot;courts of law&quot; do you think would have been invoked here? Do you believe every single time he inappropriately hugged or kissed someone at a con, they should have called the police?<br /> <br /> As a voice actor, his work at cons was directly representing the company; he doesn't have to be perfect or polite at all times, but there's a bare minimum standard. If he was sexually harassing people while attending cons for the company - even relatively 'minor' incidents, if, collectively, they added up to clear pattern - then that's obviously grounds to fire him, <i>even if he wasn't doing enough to get the law involved</i>.<br /> <br /> I would hope that Rooster Teeth HR looked into the allegations before deciding they were credible enough (and sustained enough) that he needed to get the boot, but it's silly to demand a &quot;court of law&quot; for something like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T03:09:08-08:00","id":1285179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285076#post1285076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you believe every single time he inappropriately hugged or kissed someone at a con, they should have called the police?<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Or at the very least security should have been called.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T03:38:22-08:00","id":1285187,"title":"","content":"Con security isn't very helpful. There have been cases reported of female fans beig assaulted at cons (by other attendees, not a VA) and threatened with arrest by security if they reported it. Their job is primarily defen the Cons reputation, not protect the guests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T03:39:43-08:00","id":1285189,"title":"","content":"And now for something completely different:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://schnee-dust-co.tumblr.com/post/182592530979/gang-i-think-the-theory-about-silver-eyed\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://64.media.tumblr.com/5a42a80c6a917fa7e044ae712d687ea5/47a2bd34b60d60eb-b6/s16x16u_c1/e9a8dab79ace6dba3f67f00f393f1d8373cf8b07.pnj\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://schnee-dust-co.tumblr.com/post/182592530979/gang-i-think-the-theory-about-silver-eyed\" target=\"_blank\"> let's just live~ </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://schnee-dust-co.tumblr.com/post/182592530979/gang-i-think-the-theory-about-silver-eyed\" target=\"_blank\"> http://schnee-dust-co.tumblr.com/post/182592530979/gang-i-think-the-theory-about-silver-eyed </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Gang, I think the theory about silver eyed warriors being descendants of Salem and Ozpin is VERY PLAUSIBLE. If not for all of the magic stuff, then because Ruby&rsquo;s journey is slowly leading her to... </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T04:53:25-08:00","id":1285206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285187#post1285187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Con security isn't very helpful. There have been cases reported of female fans beig assaulted at cons (by other attendees, not a VA) and threatened with arrest by security if they reported it. Their job is primarily defen the Cons reputation, not protect the guests.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's rather uncharitable. Some cons quickly sink into elaborate scams, those I agree with you, but they tend to die off on their own regardless. Others not so much.<br /> <br /> The impression I have from the cons I've been to (both as guest, as security, as attendee and as organizer) is that it's an overwhelming work, especially when it touches on something that delicate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T07:29:57-08:00","id":1285241,"title":"","content":"Liam Neeson's now under attack for something he said 40 years ago, taken out of context.<br /> <br /> And did Michael Jackson pop back up again? Some documentary movie or an episode on TV?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yeah, &quot;Leaving Neverland&quot; by Sundance.<br /> <br /> Are these really the worst figures in Hollywood? Or distractions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-06-2019, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T19:57:52-08:00","id":1285462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285039#post1285039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anything new happened or someone new come publicly forward?</div> </div> </div> </div>A bunch of new people have, but lets be honest here: Vic's behavior has been well-known for a long-ass time. He should never have been hired to begin with, and cons really should have stopped inviting him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There have been complaints against Vic before, and his enemies made sure to bring them up when Rooster Teeth announced they were taking him on as Qrow's voice. </div> </div> </div>And they were right to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rooster Teeth may not actually have any new reason to cut ties with Vic, so much as they might have decided that the controversy just won't stop coming back and they can't afford to deal with it. </div> </div> </div>Or they might have decided that he's actually a dirtbag and they don't want to work with dirtbags.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do know I'm getting sick of people getting tried and convicted in the court of public opinion instead of courts of law. </div> </div> </div>Vic Mignona has not been convicted in any court. He is a free man.<br /> <br /> If you want to make the course that people have formed an erroneous opinion of him, or the accusations surrounding him are so ill-founded that they should not be taken seriously, do that. But arguing that it is somehow illegitimate for people to have an opinion at all on whether or not his conduct was shitty or malevolent, and whether this shitty conduct means they don't want to associate with him anymore, is rank bullshit. People might be wrong here, and you're free to make that case, but arguing that the standard should be &quot;if someone literally isn't in jail, they should be treated like they've done nothing wrong&quot; is massively dubious.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Liam Neeson's now under attack for something he said 40 years ago, taken out of context. </div> </div> </div>Liam Neeson is under attack for something he said this week, not forty years ago. He specifically admits arming himself and going out hoping that someone who was <i>specifically</i> black would attack him so that he could kill them.<br /> <br /> That's pretty fucking appalling. The fact that he recognizes that it was appalling is encouraging, but the manner in which he shared it, since you so helpfully bring up context, was remarkably shitty, as he was trying to spin &quot;I went out hoping I could do a hate crime&quot; into PR for his ridiculous new revenge movie. He deserves a large degree of flack for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are these really the worst figures in Hollywood? Or distractions? </div> </div> </div>False choice. &quot;Neither&quot; is an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":4742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","user":"Murcushio","date":". 02-06-2019, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T03:19:39-08:00","id":1285517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285462#post1285462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A bunch of new people have, but lets be honest here: Vic's behavior has been well-known for a long-ass time. He should never have been hired to begin with, and cons really should have stopped inviting him.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing... His behavior up to this point was awkward at worst. And even if you think what he's done so far is criminal (which it can be, I'm not going to discuss that), roosterteeth kept him for FOUR YEARS knowing that.<br /> <br /> So either something new came up (my guess) or they are being damn inconsistent about their own policies.<br /> <br /> My chief concern here, in this topic, is the show. It's a shame that happened, Vic's acting is one of the better ones, and I hope they find someone suitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T03:34:32-08:00","id":1285520,"title":"","content":"maybe his contract expired and they took the chance to renew it?<br /> <br /> that or something happened internally","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T03:53:42-08:00","id":1285524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285462#post1285462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liam Neeson is under attack for something he said this week, not forty years ago. He specifically admits arming himself and going out hoping that someone who was <i>specifically</i> black would attack him so that he could kill them.<br /> <br /> That's pretty fucking appalling. The fact that he recognizes that it was appalling is encouraging, but the manner in which he shared it, since you so helpfully bring up context, was remarkably shitty, as he was trying to spin &quot;I went out hoping I could do a hate crime&quot; into PR for his ridiculous new revenge movie. He deserves a large degree of flack for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's less about what he was willing to do 40 years ago and more what we was willing to say to come across as a hard man. If it were up to me he'd not be allowed within 100 yards of any movie or TV series that resembles Taken unless it's a musical adaptation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T06:06:17-08:00","id":1285540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285517#post1285517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So either something new came up (my guess) or they are being damn inconsistent about their own policies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty okay with inconsistent as long as the last step gets it right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My chief concern here, in this topic, is the show. It's a shame that happened, Vic's acting is one of the better ones, and I hope they find someone suitable. </div> </div> </div>Hopefully, yeah.<br /> <br /> To be honest... of the &quot;latter-day&quot; RWBY cast members, the only two I've found truly impressive were Mignogna and Jen Taylor. (Yeah, I know Jen Taylor was technically the first character to speak. I'm not sure I count &quot;mysterious narrator.&quot;) Season 6 is a great season, especially after 5, but I remember looking at Coleen Clinkenbeard and Luci Christian in the credits and going &quot;I see Rooster Teeth have just kind of defaulted to using the same twenty VA's everyone else does.&quot; Aaron Dismuke is... fine. Etc.<br /> <br /> But back when this project was just Monty Oum's weird mocap side idea that Burnie Burns told him he could make if he got his Red vs. Blue work done in a timely manner, their voice cast was literally just &quot;anyone we could find at the office, plus we'll get Jen Taylor because why not.&quot; And that produced some <i>astounding</i> results, and I think those results were astounding precisely because they got people with non-standard, unique voices. Kara Eberle and that slight rasp she puts into Weiss' voice doesn't sound quite like anyone else. Arryn Zech was deeply awkward at first but really grew into a deeply unique voice for Blake. It's extremely difficult to imagine ANYONE being as good a Penny as Taylor McNee was/is.<br /> <br /> Now, Rooster Teeth has already declared &quot;this won't affect the show creatively,&quot; and doubled down on that. So presumably Qrow won't, like, be shot in the throat the second they arrive in Atlas. At the very least if he's suddenly exploded or written off people will find it very dubious that that was planned in some way.<br /> <br /> Rooster Teeth has two options here. The first is to strive for fidelity and consistency; try to pull an season three of &quot;Avatar: the Last Airbender&quot; move where they had to replace Mako (the voice of Iroh and a VERY unique voice) and they ended up lucking into someone who was almost completely indistinguishable.<br /> <br /> The other option is to be bold. Forget about fidelity, try and find someone who manages to exude Qrow-ness regardless of whether or not they're an absolute dead ringer for Mignogna. Treat it like if a person in a live-action show had died or gone to prison, or you were doing a remake of something forty years later when everyone originally involved is dead or no longer suitable. Find someone who would have been a great fit for Qrow if Vic Mignogna had never, ever existed and forge ahead on that, trusting that the audience will come around on them.<br /> <br /> If done well, either of these will work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T06:27:20-08:00","id":1285542,"title":"","content":"Ditto on 99%, but gotta comment on this bit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285540#post1285540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty okay with inconsistent as long as the last step gets it right.</div> </div> </div> </div>It presents a long term risk, especially if ultimately nothing new happened. It raises a hazard flag for working with them. It's the kind of stuff that will take a few years and reinforcements to be noticeable, so rwby should be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T07:27:32-08:00","id":1285555,"title":"","content":"As far as I can find, THIS is the new thing that happened with Vic, and it smells fishy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=giDD1rr8hUU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=giDD1rr8hUU\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=giDD1rr8hUU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=giDD1rr8hUU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T07:53:22-08:00","id":1285563,"title":"","content":"I'd wait before insisting on that, Sunder. Even advocating for suspicion is dangerous with this kind of topic. More will show with time and we will learn if this is righteous outrage or character assassination. I've seen enough of both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T09:16:07-08:00","id":1285581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285540#post1285540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If done well, either of these will work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heard a great suggestion on tumblr: Qrow delivers his first line just like Vic, then coughs slightly, and changes to a new voice. No one in-universe ever comments.<br /> <br /> I'd find it hilarious. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T09:22:32-08:00","id":1285585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285563#post1285563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd wait before insisting on that, Sunder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Insisting on what?<br /> <br /> What sorts of things are we supposed to wait before doing?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even advocating for suspicion is dangerous with this kind of topic. </div> </div> </div>As opposed to advocating for the destruction of a man's career based on a story that someone was able to unravel so easily?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More will show with time and we will learn if this is righteous outrage or character assassination. I've seen enough of both. </div> </div> </div>Who's going to report on this if it turns out the Anime News Network was wrong, much less willfully wrong?<br /> <br /> Any of the other &quot;official&quot; outlets that are casting judgment upon him right now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T09:28:56-08:00","id":1285586,"title":"","content":"I'd rather see neither, but he's already been condemned by the public. Here, too. Might as well just ride that wave until the truth comes out.<br /> You <b>know</b> people will be scandalized regardless of what turns up. It's literally endangering jobs at this point because companies are too afraid to even risk being denounced, regardless of their foundations.<br /> If he is guilty, whatever. If he is not, then that's fuel to tell outrage mobs to shut the fuck up.<br /> <br /> This is not the place for either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:23:11-08:00","id":1285632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285187#post1285187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Con security isn't very helpful. There have been cases reported of female fans beig assaulted at cons (by other attendees, not a VA) and threatened with arrest by security if they reported it. Their job is primarily defen the Cons reputation, not protect the guests.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Police then. Your comment shows how much a problem sexual harassment is, and unless serious countermeasures are taken, it's not going to go away. Even if others would tell you it's trivial, call the authorities; the whole point is to show that it's not trivial.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T13:11:47-08:00","id":1285657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285563#post1285563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More will show with time and we will learn if this is righteous outrage or character assassination.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is character assassination, it involves a LOT of people in a coordinated effort over close to a decade. People have been coming forward about Vic going at them inappropriately for a very long time now. It's only just now gaining traction, finally.<br /> <br /> Do people make false accusations? Sure. That happens. Do a shit-ton of people form a conspiracy to do so, and persist with it over many years, for no personal gain at all? Technically possible, but quite dubious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd rather see neither, but he's already been condemned by the public. Here, too. Might as well just ride that wave until the truth comes out. </div> </div> </div>Well, at this point there are two possibilities:<br /> <br /> 1) The truth is already out.<br /> <br /> 2) There's an enormous, unprecedented conspiracy engaged against Vic Mignogna.<br /> <br /> If it's the first, there will be no more &quot;truth&quot; to come out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You <b>know</b> people will be scandalized regardless of what turns up. </div> </div> </div>Either of those things turning up will a scandal! Thus, people should indeed be scandalized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If he is guilty, whatever. </div> </div> </div>Well, no, less &quot;whatever&quot; and more &quot;how the fuck did this guy get away with this for so long?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T13:35:43-08:00","id":1285669,"title":"","content":"That's the thing. You're assuming what's TOLD holds as much weight as what's been SHOWN. It doesn't, it can't, and your claim to conspiracy might indeed find itself proven correct. It wouldn't be the first time someone's repute is destroyed by scandal only for it to be proven false.<br /> <br /> Thus, again, I withhold my judgment. What's known feels like it's not enough to justify the reaction, so either RT is going by whispers (and inconsistently so, but we've been through that already) or something new came up. I'm giving them credit that something happened, and that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 02-07-2019, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T19:35:34-08:00","id":1285770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5H3soKn-m0A\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5H3soKn-m0A\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5H3soKn-m0A\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5H3soKn-m0A </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Provable conspiracy. At least for this latest round of trouble. Facebook groups putting together photoshopped &quot;evidence&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding earlier rounds of trouble... Something that doesn't make sense about people complaining about Vic &quot;groping&quot; them is that he's KNOWN to be very physically affectionate, and there are LINES of people going up to him. If you've seen him hug everyone before you in the line, AND you've heard anything about him as a person, why not just ask him to NOT do that with you? Or even decline to pose with him for a picture at all?<br /> <br /> At least one of the people who complained said that they were only in line to get an autograph for a friend, so why ask for a photo EXCEPT to complain about it later? And one of the photos that ANN used was by someone who DID ask for the photo and the physical affection, while in the company of her parents. She's spoken out against ANN for using her photo like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T23:58:15-08:00","id":1285824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285669#post1285669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing. You're assuming what's TOLD holds as much weight as what's been SHOWN.</div> </div> </div> </div>What the hell does this even mean? By this standard if you don't have verifiable physical evidence of some sort, it doesn't matter how many firsthand reports you get, you're obliged to not believe them, because all you've been &quot;shown&quot; is someone NOT doing anything.<br /> <br /> This is a pretty decent standard for law enforcement, at least <i>sometimes</i>, but it's completely untenable and unreasonable to be applied in all cases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Provable conspiracy. At least for this latest round of trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>You got a link to anyone who isn't, themselves, a conspiracy-mongering shitstain, Sunder?<br /> <br /> I clicked the link. Saw that this is someone who un-ironically used the term &quot;NPC.&quot; Closed it again, because people who do that are trash people.<br /> <br /> Even if your description is meaningfully accurate, which I highly doubt, we still have, you know, close to a decades worth of people saying Vic groped and came at them, not to mention his homophobia and anti-semitic remarks.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you've seen him hug everyone before you in the line, AND you've heard anything about him as a person, why not just ask him to NOT do that with you? </div> </div> </div>...holy shit, dude.<br /> <br /> There is a huge difference between &quot;I expect Vic Mignogna to hug me, I've lined up expecting that&quot; and &quot;I expect him to put his hand on my ass or under my shirt,&quot; which is what quite a lot of his victims are saying happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At least one of the people who complained said that they were only in line to get an autograph for a friend, so why ask for a photo EXCEPT to complain about it later? </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> This is beneath you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T02:06:37-08:00","id":1285832,"title":"","content":"You need absolutely nothing to make your judgment on someone. If you value fact over rumor, though, you do need more, yes. The proper way to believe a rumor is to INVESTIGATE, not to CONDEMN.<br /> <br /> So it all gets back, again and again, to what I've already said: rumour alone does not feel enough reason to ostracize the guy.<br /> You know the rumors, you're not comfortable, you don't associate(here's where most of his event cancellations and rt's firing fit). You know the rumors, and you have to associate, you pay very very fucking close attention to what he's doing so that you can either confirm he's ok or prove he's bad.<br /> <br /> So worry your warbles not, I'm not doubting anyone. I'm saying we need more to go beyond rumours and that neither outcome will be a surprise.<br /> <br /> Oh, btw, it's not a &quot;decent&quot; standard for law enforcement. It's a damn <i>requisite</i>. Ethical justice considers condemning innocents a far worse crime than letting guilty go. It was probably a figure of speech, but I need to make this clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 02-08-2019, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T07:24:05-08:00","id":1285883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285824#post1285824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I clicked the link. Saw that this is someone who un-ironically used the term &quot;NPC.&quot; Closed it again, because people who do that are trash people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truly, your commitment to researching both sides of an argument is to be admired and emulated.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you think the Nazis never had a good point with that whole &quot;If you tell a lie often enough and loud enough, people will start to believe it&quot; because they were horrible people. Being a horrible person means that you are automatically wrong at everything, stumbling through life like an incompetent Saturday morning cartoon villain.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you're lucky enough to buy gold bullion, but other times you have to go digging through the dirt to get it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Adding this in as it occurs to me:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285824#post1285824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not to mention his homophobia and anti-semitic remarks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's the antisemitism come from? And there's video footage of him confronting people who seemed to be protesting LGBT.<br /> <br /> So he didn't want to sign some people's porn, or shipping-related fanart. That's probably a wise policy, especially if those people would take it online as &quot;support&quot; for their &quot;ships&quot;. I'm sure that Funimation and the Japanese owners of the property don't want anything close to official on unofficial material.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a huge difference between &quot;I expect Vic Mignogna to hug me, I've lined up expecting that&quot; and &quot;I expect him to put his hand on my ass or under my shirt,&quot; which is what quite a lot of his victims are saying happened. </div> </div> </div>And every single person he groped just happened to be the kind of person who would keep smiling wide for the camera, as opposed to looking shocked or uncomfortable, and not one of them was the kind of person to turn about and slap him, or at least break away from him? Every single one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-08-2019, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T08:56:53-08:00","id":1285915,"title":"","content":"I've lost a *lot* of respect for long-time posters, based on what they've posted in this thread. Jesus Christ, guys.<br /> <br /> As for my personal feelings on this: its about damn time. I remember the hubbub that boiled up when Qrows VA was first announced. I did some research, and i was disgusted that Vic would be hired. It remained in the back of my mind all through his stay on the show.<br /> <br /> Good riddance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T09:43:30-08:00","id":1285934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285883#post1285883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And every single person he groped just happened to be the kind of person who would keep smiling wide for the camera, as opposed to looking shocked or uncomfortable, and not one of them was the kind of person to turn about and slap him, or at least break away from him? Every single one.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is unsurprising. Most women - hell, most <i>people</i> will not directly confront their harassers while they are physically present and actively harassing them, for fear of retaliation. Slapping someone is aggravated assault, and a very bad idea to do to someone wealthy and famous, and even just calling someone out can escalate the situation and put the victim in more danger. Both directly, from the abuser, and in the case of a celebrity like Vic Mignogna, indirectly from rabid fans. It is much safer to do whatever you need to do to get out of the situation quickly and safely, and take further action once you are away from the harasser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T10:07:13-08:00","id":1285941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285934#post1285934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is unsurprising. Most women - hell, most <i>people</i> will not directly confront their harassers while they are physically present and actively harassing them, for fear of retaliation. Slapping someone is aggravated assault, and a very bad idea to do to someone wealthy and famous, and even just calling someone out can escalate the situation and put the victim in more danger. Both directly, from the abuser, and in the case of a celebrity like Vic Mignogna, indirectly from rabid fans. It is much safer to do whatever you need to do to get out of the situation quickly and safely, and take further action once you are away from the harasser.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's so much evidence, then why is anyone working to <i>manufacture</i> evidence? As in the previous video.<br /> <br /> But there's a video that shows a list of all the accusations against Vic, so that someone can look into them themselves, and points out some coincidences and inconsistencies and patterns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tqDPM4djy_k\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tqDPM4djy_k\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tqDPM4djy_k\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tqDPM4djy_k </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This guy claims to have gone through all of these things and says that, except for maybe two of them, they're all &quot;I heard this from a friend&quot; rather than &quot;this happened to me / right in front of me&quot;. With this list of compiled evidence, his claim should be easy to disprove if it's false.<br /> <br /> <br /> If Vic's been molesting underage girls, then someone should have called the police and gotten his ass arrested, but none of the people claiming to witness any of these things had smartphones?<br /> <br /> If someone can present actual evidence and a case against him that holds up in a court of law, I'll denounce him right along with everyone else. If his lawyer can't prove his innocence or at least establish reasonable doubt, I'll admit he's probably guilty.<br /> <br /> But all I see and hear about are rumors that someone else heard about, except when I see actually video and Twitter evidence that disproves some of the things people accuse him of doing, or reveal libel and fraud by his enemies.<br /> <br /> We're not talking about Harvey Weinstein, here. Vic doesn't have the kind of power to make or break someone's career, or else he could save his own. Harvey was accused of much worse for much longer (the &quot;casting couch&quot; was an open joke), and major news networks refused to run a story on what an investigation turned up on him because of the kind of power Weinstein had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-08-2019, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T10:59:46-08:00","id":1285963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285832#post1285832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need absolutely nothing to make your judgment on someone. If you value fact over rumor, though, you do need more, yes. The proper way to believe a rumor is to INVESTIGATE, not to CONDEMN.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, by this standard, if you don't have physical evidence, merely the reports of witnesses, you're obligated to disbelieve them. All of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know the rumors, and you have to associate, you pay very very fucking close attention to what he's doing so that you can either confirm he's ok or prove he's bad. </div> </div> </div>Again, though, by your standards, what you've learned from your personal observations doesn't count to anyone who can't, themselves, confirm it with their own eyes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, btw, it's not a &quot;decent&quot; standard for law enforcement. It's a damn <i>requisite</i>. Ethical justice considers condemning innocents a far worse crime than letting guilty go. It was probably a figure of speech, but I need to make this clear. </div> </div> </div>It is not in fact a requisite. Law enforcement will often arrest people or press charges based on nothing more than eyewitness testimony, which under your rubric they shouldn't be doing. And you know what? That's absolutely okay. If you get enough people to say &quot;that's him, that's the guy&quot; it is often not only justified to lower the hammer, you're derelict in your duty if you DON'T.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that eyewitness testimony should always be trusted. But it also can't be completely disregarded, either from a legal standpoint or an interpersonal one, in favor of &quot;you got physical evidence? If not you got NOTHING.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Perhaps you think the Nazis never had a good point with that whole &quot;If you tell a lie often enough and loud enough, people will start to believe it&quot; because they were horrible people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, when someone ADMITS they're horrible, I'll believe them, yes.<br /> <br /> If someone admits openly they're horrible, and then wants credibility on <i>other</i> things, I will generally NOT believe them. Why should I? They've admitted they're terrible! Terrible people usually don't get credibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where's the antisemitism come from? </div> </div> </div>Well, the time a fan told him he was Jewish and Mignogna said &quot;we can fix that&quot; leaps to mind.<br /> <br /> I don't care if he was joking. That's a shitty fuckin' thing to say, and is in fact anti-semitic.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So he didn't want to sign some people's porn, or shipping-related fanart. </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the key thing here. SOME people's. Show up with straight shipping fanart? Pen comes out. Show up with non-straight stuff? Get away from me.<br /> <br /> Mignogna, of course, is free to sign or not sign whatever the hell he wants. And I am free to judge him for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If someone can present actual evidence and a case against him that holds up in a court of law, ...We're not talking about Harvey Weinstein, here. </div> </div> </div>Well, this is hypocritical.<br /> <br /> Nobody has brought anything against Weinstein that has held up in a court of law, either, although that might change. But it's okay to lower the boom on Weinstein, but not okay for Vic?<br /> <br /> You can, of course, try (and it's been cute watching you try) to make the case that Weinstein's accusers are credible and Mignogna's are not. But that's not what you're doing; you're making the case that the standard for Mignogna should be &quot;holds up in a court of law&quot; whereas for Weinstein, it doesn't need to rise to that level.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T11:44:40-08:00","id":1285970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285963#post1285963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, by this standard, if you don't have physical evidence, merely the reports of witnesses, you're obligated to disbelieve them. All of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.You investigate.I said it before, more than once. Investigating is not discrediting.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285963#post1285963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, though, by your standards, what you've learned from your personal observations doesn't count to anyone who can't, themselves, confirm it with their own eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less. Remember to include tangible evidence. Documentation. You name it. Hearsay is not enough on its own to do anything but prompt suspicion. I have also said this before.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285963#post1285963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not in fact a requisite. Law enforcement will often arrest people or press charges based on nothing more than eyewitness testimony, which under your rubric they shouldn't be doing. And you know what? That's absolutely okay. If you get enough people to say &quot;that's him, that's the guy&quot; it is often not only justified to lower the hammer, you're derelict in your duty if you DON'T.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that eyewitness testimony should always be trusted. But it also can't be completely disregarded, either from a legal standpoint or an interpersonal one, in favor of &quot;you got physical evidence? If not you got NOTHING.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a very unsubtle difference between, for example, arresting someone because she's being accused of something dangerous enough there's a risk of her committing another crime or hampering the investigation.<br /> This is not a condemnation, it's a preventive measure to make sure the investigation will carry on. <br /> Same thing with pressing charges. Pressing charges based on hearsay is perfectly normal. From there you go to <i>prove</i> your hearsay.<br /> <br /> And when they actually arrest, as in executing a sentence, based solely on testimonies? Well, have you followed related news around the world? This IS injustice. Witnesses lie. Witnesses err. Human memory is <b>shit</b> for most subjects relevant to proving something happened. It's shit to the level people can be talked into remembering things that never happened. And it happens <i>a lot</i>. We have an obscene number of people falsely accused and arrested every day, and we have been discovering these mistakes for DECADES now.<br /> <br /> <br /> You keep replying to me saying &quot;rumors aren't enough&quot; as if I was saying &quot;rumors are to be ignored&quot;. Clear your perspective, you're literally replying to arguments I'm not making. Have you even noticed that I am GIVING CREDIT to roosterteeth in their decision, despite thinking it hasty?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T13:45:50-08:00","id":1286007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285970#post1285970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope.You investigate.I said it before, more than once. Investigating is not discrediting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but again, by your own standards, if the investigation ONLY turns up eyewitness testimony, one is obliged to ignore it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More or less. Remember to include tangible evidence. Documentation. You name it. </div> </div> </div>So if someone SAYS &quot;this guy acted like a dirtbag,&quot; that's not enough, but if they WRITE IT DOWN, we're golden.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hearsay is not enough on its own to do anything but prompt suspicion. I have also said this before. </div> </div> </div>Which again, is you saying &quot;if you don't have physical evidence, you've got jack shit.&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same thing with pressing charges. Pressing charges based on hearsay is perfectly normal. From there you go to <i>prove</i> your hearsay. </div> </div> </div>One of the ways in which &quot;hearsay&quot; is proven is by bringing in the people saying it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You keep replying to me saying &quot;rumors aren't enough&quot; as if I was saying &quot;rumors are to be ignored&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Because that seems to be what you're saying. Your stance seems to boil down to &quot;it doesn't matter how many people say something happened to them, if they can't produce physical evidence, all you've got is a rumor, and all a rumor means is you investigate, but if the investigation merely brings you back around to the people saying things happened to them, it remains only a rumor.&quot;<br /> <br /> If I've got that logic chain wrong I welcome the correction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Clear your perspective, you're literally replying to arguments I'm not making. </div> </div> </div>Your arguments seem incredibly inconsistent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you even noticed that I am GIVING CREDIT to roosterteeth in their decision, despite thinking it hasty? </div> </div> </div>Giving Rooster Teeth credit would seem to be inconsistent with your stance on the matter, because if they cut ties based on &quot;rumors&quot; that would seem to be something, by your standards, that should not be praised.<br /> <br /> Also, where, precisely, did you give them credit? This topic came up back on page 23, in post #336 from vampire hunter D. As near as I can tell, in every post after that your position on Rooster Teeth has either been noncomittal, or to voice concerns over their &quot;inconsistency.&quot; Neither seems like &quot;giving them credit&quot; to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T14:31:26-08:00","id":1286022,"title":"","content":"Ok, you're not even trying to read what I write charitably. I'm out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T14:55:15-08:00","id":1286028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285941#post1285941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's so much evidence, then why is anyone working to <i>manufacture</i> evidence? As in the previous video.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey man, I never said anything about there being \u201cso much evidence.\u201d You asked why, if he was groping fans, none of them turned around to slap him or at least yell at him. And I answered, most people don\u2019t confront their harrassers directly, especially not in the moment, and especially when the harasser is in a position of power. Vic may not be Harvey Wieinstein, but he still has unfathomably more power, physical, financial, and social, than your average teenage girl. So, if he\u2019s been groping teenage girls, it\u2019s unsurprising that none of them have slapped him for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T21:30:59-08:00","id":1286089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1285883#post1285883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Truly, your commitment to researching both sides of an argument is to be admired and emulated.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. That works both ways. If an argument is strong, and if it is backed by reputable, reliable evidence then it doesn't matter who makes it; but, conversely, that means that <i>you</i> shouldn't have to rely on someone else to make it, either. You should be able to just present the argument and the evidence yourself in order to convince us; you shouldn't have to link to a YouTube channel to make it for you.<br /> <br /> 2. It's obviously not possible to validate all evidence and all assertions ourselves; in that case, we have to rely on the reputations of the sources doing the reporting. A source with a strong reputation for fact-checking and accuracy can lend weight to even cautious or vague assertions, since they have a reputation that they're putting behind an accusation simply by reporting it (even just as an accusation!) Conversely, someone who is known to exaggerate, lie, manipulate their viewers, and so on is a terrible source to include in your chain of evidence - if you think <i>they</i> found good evidence, you'd be better off going straight to their source and presenting that here yourself. If the only place you've ever seen that &quot;evidence&quot; is in that video, and it's impossible to produce it or find it anywhere else - well, then you're asking us to trust their reputation, and they have none.<br /> <br /> 3. People are not inhuman logical machines. We're all subject to sentimentality and irrationality; when I <i>know</i> that someone is going to try to manipulate me, or when they seem like they have a history of using lies to manipulate their viewers, it's reasonable for me to refuse to give them the opportunity to do so. Nothing about this prevents me from getting &quot;both sides of the argument&quot;, because if they present an argument worth listening to, someone I <i>do</i> consider worth spending the time talking to (eg. you, however much you are straining that consideration at the moment) can present the argument and evidence themselves. I don't have to (and, given my limited time and energy, cannot) listen to every argument from every person; but as long as an argument is strong, and as long as I trust <i>some</i> worthwhile people, arguments worth hearing will reach my ears eventually.<br /> <br /> 4. Conversely, since I know that YouTube videos in particular are a much easier way to pull at people's heartstrings or fire up their misdirected anger than text, I tend to get particularly suspicious when someone refuses to present what <i>ought</i> to be a simple, concise argument themselves and instead tries to get me to watch a YouTube video from someone who is obviously trying to push a political agenda.<br /> <br /> 5. I don't have infinite time or energy. I'm happy to look at any <i>reputable</i> evidence you have as long as you can present it reasonably concisely. But you have to show at least some respect for my time by putting your best foot forward. Starting your argument by linking to a frothing moron on youtube tells me that you either have nothing, or you suck so badly at constructing arguments that we're wasting our time.<br /> <br /> 6. Exploiting the limited nature of time and energy is a tactic used to manipulate people - presenting shitty arguments over and over or at great length in order to overwhelm people; getting them to waste time talking to and listening to you so you can influence them even if your argument is weak, and so on. The only defense against that tactic is to demand that you <i>get to the point</i> (yes, I am aware of the irony given the length of this post) and to reject things like massive YouTube manifestos out of hand unless you can come up with a <i>very</i> compelling reason why this video in particular is so worthwhile and why you can't just present the argument yourself if it's actually strong enough to overcome the fact that the channel's owner appears to be a lying, manipulative sack of shit.<br /> <br /> If you have actual, reputable evidence, go ahead and present it. If you have coherent arguments, make them - I don't care where you got them (although if it looks like an argument I've heard over and over, I'm likely to tune it out, because of point 5.) I'm not going to waste my time watching shitty, blatantly-manipulative youtube channels, but if they actually have evidence and an argument then you should be able to present it on your own without relying on them, right?<br /> <br /> But if you can't - if you're reading this and realizing that the &quot;evidence&quot; from that video might, perhaps, not have a snowball's chance in hell of convincing me when summed together with in-line citations and given a neutral description - then I want you to at least <i>consider</i> the alternative. That is to say: You were suckered by the various things I outlined above - combined with, in your case, a <i>desire</i> for the things they were saying to be true - and that the people who keep sending you these videos aren't trying to arm you with FACTS and LOGIC, they're using your outrage over what you see as an injustice to recruit you into a larger political cause. People who are arguing in good faith - rather than just trying to use flashpoints like these to try and get their foot in the door to recruit you into their shitty ideological cults - will be eager to present their arguments as concisely and quickly as possible.<br /> <br /> There are some complicated subjects that benefit from or even require longer in-depth analysis, yes, but this doesn't seem like one of those. If you have evidence, you can provide it directly from the best available source. If the best available source is, uh, <i>that</i>, then you don't have anything at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-09-2019, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T02:44:05-08:00","id":1286130,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Can we just let the subject drop please? It's barely on topic for RWBY at this point let alone Exalted. <br /> If you still feel strongly you're welcome to take it to Off Topic. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T02:56:01-08:00","id":1286135,"title":"","content":"Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T10:00:22-08:00","id":1286212,"title":"","content":"So, I've got a LOT of predictions how Volume 7 is going to go down.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pre-Volume Trailer</b><br /> <br /> Just as Ilia basically stole Blake's trailer before Volume 5, and Adam got the only trailer before Volume 6, we might get a trailer focused only on revealing the backstory and motivations of Cinder or Dr. Arthur Watts. We've been left in the dark about Cinder's motivations for too long, and Watts is going to need some fleshing out before he can serve as a principle antagonist this Volume. We know that he's a disgraced Atlesian scientist and doctor, so his past is especially relevant to the next Volume, but Cinder Fall might also come from Atlas for all we know.<br /> <br /> We don't know anything about Tyrian's background, but he's been extremely obvious about his motivations. He wants to serve Salem because he sees her as a goddess. That's more than we know about Cinder, who wants to become powerful and feared because... of unknown reasons. Salem is a means to that end, for her, not the end in and of itself.<br /> <br /> With Watts, we don't even know what he is trying to get out of this relationship, or why he wants it. He only comes across as better-handled than Cinder because we haven't known him as long, and he's that same kind of snarky, charming villain we lost when Roman Torchwick died.<br /> <br /> Since we know Watts has plot-relevant connections to Atlas, we can easily learn more about his past and his desires as the plot progresses, so my money is on Cinder getting the character trailer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Volume Itself</b><br /> <br /> Our heroes can't land in Atlas City without getting arrested for illegal possession of Atlas equipment. Now that Atlas' military has spotted their approach, they can't attempt to flee, either. They're in jail, and Ironwood is not happy. After he takes the Relic of Knowledge away and locks it up, and sits down without heroes to get some answers, he's furious.<br /> <br /> He's also the one in total control, and the one who needs to keep up public appearances by not letting our heroes get away with what they did without punishment.<br /> <br /> As the adult nominally in charge, most of the blame falls on Qrow, whom Ironwood consigns to the drunk tank and mandates some time with an alcoholism therapist. If Qrow, on heels of his Volume 6 experiences, agrees that's fair and that he's got a problem he needs help with, Ironwood whips out his scroll in a panic, demanding the therapist appear immediately. Qrow may be cooling his heels a lot this Volume, because detoxing from alcohol is not only terrible for the patient, they also stink to high heavens such that no one wants to be around them. (If we're particularly lucky, Qrow attends the same AAA meeting as Weiss' mother.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Maria, as a little old blind lady and a virtual stranger to the group, is not held very if at all accountable for their actions, especially if her identity as the Grimm Reaper (and the pilot of the stolen plane) can be kept secret, so she might get off scot-free. Oscar, who can be passed off as Maria's grandson if necessary for any reason, could avoid punishment entirely due to being a minor under Qrow's supervision.<br /> <br /> <br /> Teams RWBY and JN_R are still in trouble, but Ironwood can actually make that work out for everyone's good (especially Weiss') by enrolling them all in Atlas Academy as part of a juvenile delinquent rehabilitation program. After all, he can vouch that all seven of them are great potential hunters that Remnant desperately needs, and play to Atlesian pride by suggesting that there's no better academy for teaching them how to behave themselves like proper, law-abiding adults.<br /> <br /> So, we might not get severe-weather outfits for our heroes as such, but we're could get them wearing Atlas Academy uniforms (which at least are designed somewhat for the cold). It will be an interesting opportunity to see how well their inherent colorfulness is expressed while wearing such colorless clothing.<br /> <br /> Since Weiss Schnee should be legally an adult at this point, and would be effectively a criminal against the state, Ironwood's authority over her life finally eclipses that of her parents, so that Jacques cannot simply take her away from Atlas Academy. This might be the straw that finally breaks the back of the two mens' friendship.<br /> <br /> Ironwood can convince our teenaged heroes that enrolling in Atlas Academy has other benefits. Now that they've secured the Lamp of Knowledge, where else would they go? They don't know how to take the fight to Salem, so they're stuck playing defensively like always. None of them are licensed hunters, so they won't be allowed to help take Beacon back from the Grimm, so why not do what Team CFVY did and try to finish their formal education? Licenses aside, their skills still need improvement before they can take on the likes of Hazel or Tyrian, and Atlas is now one of the only two hunting academies still operating.<br /> <br /> It might be a prison (or a prison away from prison, in the case of Weiss and her family's estate), but at least it's one that is dedicated to making them stronger warriors, and there are worse places to stay while they try to figure out what to do next. (And we, the audience, know that they aren't going to be staying for longer than two or three Volumes, maximum. Vacuo will be a major breath of fresh air, after this arc.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Oscar especially needs more training, and being forced to enroll at Atlas Academy would be the perfect impetuous for him to become the new P of Team JNPR. He'll be joining Atlas younger than Ruby joined Beacon, but Ozpin's muscle memories and his own field experience should help him qualify, especially with Ironwood's approval.<br /> <br /> Ironwood has particular reasons to keep Oscar close and under house-arrest. First of all, because he wants to keep Ozpin close when Ozpin won't force and maybe can't convince Oscar to stay in Atlas. Second of all, because he would like for Ozpin's successor to sympathize more with how Atlas and Ironwood operates, and Atlas Academy is the perfect place to impress upon the boy the superiority of Atlas' methods.<br /> <br /> <br /> Being in Atlas Academy, of course, brings our heroes into contact with a number of faces we want to see again. Starting with Flynt Coal and Neon Katt. Because if anyone can help our Beacon babies (and Blake in particular, as the only faunus) survive the pressure-cooker that is Atlas Academy, it's Team FNKI, who can show them all the best places on and around (and far from) the campus for letting off steam.<br /> <br /> Winter might transfer into the faculty to spend time with Weiss and help her refine her skills offscreen. In a similar way, Maria might have some tips for how Ruby can fight with her scythe and Gravity Rounds. If we meet the two remaining members of Team FNKI, K and I might have tricks or styles relating to other characters. Maybe Nora and Ren, so someone might finally teach Nora how to use Lightning Dust for herself.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ciel Soleil might return as the opposite of Team FNKI; a teacher's pet trying to make our rule-breaking heroes toe the line. Her screentime might be vanishingly brief; she wasn't even a friend of a friend, and we don't know if Penny was her partner or only suddenly placed on her team just for the Vytal Tournament, but we do know that Ciel and her team were not trusted enough to know about Penny's nature. We might not even meet the rest of Ciel's team. Really, there's only two obvious ways to expand Ciel's potential as an antagonist/obstacle: (1) if she has a new Penny as a partner, whether it is merely a lookalike or the same Penny but with her memories of Ruby missing for whatever reason, with Ciel eager to keep her charge away from a &quot;questionable&quot; influence like Ruby. (2) Ciel's become the Winter Maiden after the Fall of Beacon. Without either of these conditions, Ciel is a footnote at best, and not worthy of revealed weapons, fighting style, or combat Semblance.<br /> <br /> If Penny (or a replacement) isn't already active, then we need to see Doctor Polendina directly first, and this is where Yang and Maria come in. Yang's replacement arm was hinted to be made by Polendina, on the Argus Limited she was reading a magazine of prosthestic limbs like she was considering her future options, and her arm was damaged by Adam. Maria was going to Atlas expressly to get her eyes repaired. When they go to see the doctor, Ruby goes with them to learn more about how her sister's and grandmother's parts work, and meets Penny's father.<br /> <br /> Depending on how this meeting goes and what Ruby learns, she could finally face a moral dilemma (for that vaunted &quot;character growth&quot; people claim they want to see) if bringing Penny back demands knowledge only Jinn's final answer can provide. Ruby could be forced to choose between saving the world and saving her friend. Even more so if she needs to steal the Staff of Creation, which might have a cost like Equivalent Exchange or an opportunity cost like the Lamp.<br /> <br /> It seems unlikely that Ruby would have a subplot of temptation to steal and use the Jinn's last answer for personal gain FOLLOWED by a subplot of dealing with the new Penny being amnesiac or someone completely new, so if she goes through with it, I think she should either totally succeed or totally fail. I'm leaning on &quot;totally fail&quot;, as punishment for putting herself before everyone else in the world like Salem did, and so that Penny is spared the guilt of being brought back to life at the cost of everyone else's chances for victory.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of old magical relics and moral dilemmas, let us return to Ozpin. Atlas Academy is the opportunity that Ozpin has been waiting for since he reincarnated into Oscar. He thought that when he arrived at Haven, he could reconnect with Leonardo and start getting on top of the declining global situation, only for Leo to prove suspiciously shifty and then be revealed as the worst sort of traitor. Then Ozpin lost whatever influence he could have with Ruby's group when he lost their trust and they proved untrustworthy in return. But now he's in Atlas, and Ironwood is no traitor, nor someone who would alienate Ozpin even after learning the truth about Salem, because Ironwood would rather have as much information as possible, even if he takes every word Ozpin says with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> As long as everyone remains in Atlas, under Ironwood's control, Ozpin doesn't need to worry about Oscar choosing to go whichever inadvisably dangerous place Ruby goes; Oscar is finally someplace safe from Salem's assassins, where he can continue training to become the next Wizard. Ozpin probably would have preferred that training to happen in Vale and Beacon, but beggars can't be choosers. And even if Ironwood never trusts Ozpin is telling the whole truth ever again, at least the two of them trust each other enough to cooperate and plan together how they can keep Remnant from falling apart.<br /> <br /> <br /> Descending from that top-down view, we go to the ground level of Remnant's woes, Team FNKI can take Yang and Blake down into Mantle where free-spirits and faunus can find some fun. This is an opportunity to explore the class divide between Mantle and Atlas City (which I suspect will pay homage to A Tale of Two Cities, though I know nothing about the book besides &quot;it was the best of times, it was the worst of times&quot;).<br /> <br /> It's also here that our heroes can run into whatever their enemies are doing. Because if Cinder and Neo went anywhere to disappear and look for an opportunity, it would be Mantle first. Tyrian might also be working apart from Watts down in Mantle, seeking out the local White Fang. With Sienna Khan and Adam Taurus dead, the international organization is leaderless, leaving the Atlesian branch answering only to itself and wondering if they should make contact with Ghira Belladonna. Tyrian might instead convince them to serve Salem as Hazel attempted to do with Sienna Khan.<br /> <br /> <br /> Whatever Watts ends up doing, I'm hoping for a battle of SCIENCE! between him and Doctor Polendina. One wonders if Watts was at all involved in making Penny. If Penny returns, could Watts infect her with a control virus and make her fight Ruby?<br /> <br /> <br /> Weiss' mother, Willow Schnee, might finally rouse herself from her depressed, drunken stupor to go visit Weiss at the academy to berate her for bringing shame on her mother and the family name. I can't imagine what else Willow cares about, considering that she didn't care enough about her children to be part of their lives.<br /> <br /> This confrontation might also finally reveal more about the history of the Schnee family and provide an explanation about why their Semblance is hereditary. I suspect that the snowflake glyphs belonged to a royal or noble family that Nicholas Schnee married into when he became rich (old blood and nouveau riche marrying is an old story).<br /> <br /> I might get my wish about Willow attending the same AAA meetings as Qrow if she makes such a disruptive public scene that Ironwood has her arrested as well. If his alliance with Jacques is already broken because of custody over Weiss, then Ironwood has little left to lose by incarcerating the man's wife.<br /> <br /> (It would be hilarious if, by the end of the Atlas Arc, Willow divorces her husband and starts a relationship with Qrow, for maximum humiliation against Jacques and lots of amusing awkwardness among our heroes.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of Jacques, that's definitely one high-class avenue for civil war that Watts can exploit without getting his hands dirty like Tyrian. And if Jacques does get involved with Salem's schemes, then we could end up having a battle at the Schnee Manor that leaves the building utterly destroyed and Jacques arrested for treason, leaving Willow Schnee in control of her father's company.<br /> <br /> Free from Jacques at last, the Schnee family members all reconcile their differences. It is made clear that Whitley, whatever his faults, isn\u2019t to blame for Weiss getting herself disinherited with her own outbursts, and he doesn\u2019t like his father any more than the rest of the family. Weiss is confident that her mother and little brother will straighten the company out and redeem the family name without her, so she can focus on saving the world as a huntress with her team.<br /> <br /> But Weiss does take the family yacht, because our heroes need their own air-ship without stealing from the military again. Klein goes along with her to serve as her personal cabin-boy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Neo is going to manage to steal at least one Relic; possibly the Relic of Creation, so that our heroes won't get to enjoy whatever advantage it could give them. At least with the Lamp, they can't use it for fear of having no more answers for another 100 years or so.<br /> <br /> If Cinder manages to kill the Winter Maiden and steal her power, then Atlas Vault is left as unsecure as Mistral's, and our heroes have to transport the Lamp again, this time to Shade Academy in Vacuo. Because where else does a magical genie lamp belong but a desert kingdom? Where it might get stolen and used by Emerald (Aladdin / Cleopatra).<br /> <br /> <br /> Ruby might get kidnapped by Flying Berlingels and taken into the Solitas wilderness, where Salem is hiding; close enough to control the Grimm to capture and not kill a specific target, but far enough to avoid being seen, and close enough that our heroes can rescue Ruby without having to find Salem's base to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T12:32:40-08:00","id":1286266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1286212#post1286212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Cinder manages to kill the Winter Maiden and steal her power, then Atlas Vault is left as unsecure as Mistral's, and our heroes have to transport the Lamp again, this time to Shade Academy in Vacuo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't necessarily agree with everything else but I think we're only due for one season in Atlas.<br /> <br /> Based tenuously on the needs of narrative pacing and the formula established thus far, I'm tentatively predicting that we're going to follow the season 4/5 structure going forward. By which I mean:<br /> <br /> Season 4: Journey to Mistral<br /> Season 5: Mistral<br /> Season 6: Journey to Atlas<br /> Season 7: Atlas<br /> Season 8: Journey to Vacuo<br /> Season 9: Vacuo<br /> Season 10: Journey to Vale<br /> Season 11: Vale<br /> <br /> I'm basically 100% sure the series will end where it began: in Vale. Full circle. Oh, there may be some sort of final confrontation at Salem's evil lair, but the last arc is gonna be back in Vale.<br /> <br /> I have a lot more hope for season 7 than I did for 5. We got a more complete picture of Argus and its people in four, five episodes there than we got of Mistral in over a season there. I'm hoping Atlas is more than Mistral was, because Mistral was &quot;one house, a deserted academy, and ten minutes of Qrow wandering alleys.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T14:01:37-08:00","id":1286285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1286266#post1286266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't necessarily agree with everything else</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't bother me. But I'd love to hear what other people think will happen.<br /> <br /> Some posters over at SpaceBattles absolutely hate the idea that our teenage heroes might be forced to enroll at Atlas, but they don't offer any explanation for how Ironwood can get them out of trouble for stealing the airplane, or how they can avoid Ironwood making some effort to keep them under control when they cannot escape his control within his kingdom and still cooperate with him against their enemies. Just like when Weiss was back under her father's thumb, the patriarch holds all of the cards, and righteous anger isn't going to change that.<br /> <br /> Ironwood's a good guy, but he's a military man in a militarized kingdom (which probably exercises universal conscription, like other tiny frozen real-world countries who need all the soldiers they can get). Dude is going to run a tight ship, and likely has a poor opinion of Team RWBY and JNPR's discipline. He definitely watched the doubles match with Team FNKI, which FNKI dominated up until the final moments thanks to better teamwork and excellent psychological manipulation. As for JNPR, they lost a lot with Pyrrha's death, and Oscar could use their help to catch up.<br /> <br /> Chronologically, Team RNJR spent at least a month in Mistral City, including the time it took Qrow to recover before he introduced them to Leonardo. Even if they only spent a week in Atlas, I would expect plenty of that week to be spent in Atlas Academy uniforms, except when they have free-time to leave campus and see the city(ies) with Team FNKI. And while in Atlas City, where better than Atlas Academy to keep learning how to fight?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but I think we're only due for one season in Atlas. </div> </div> </div>The possibility of which is why I didn't mention anything about Team STRQ.<br /> <br /> Some fans are so eager for anything Team STRQ related now that Summer Rose has a model, but it just doesn't seem realistic. It seems highly unlikely that either Taiyang or Summer came from Solitas before attending Beacon, and we know the Branwen Twins didn't.<br /> <br /> We may not flashback to how Taiyang reacted to Raven's return until after our heroes leave Atlas. Why chase after that plotline when there's already so many to cover in Atlas?<br /> <br /> Now, if we have two Volumes in Atlas, then I fully expect something like this:<br /> Back at Patch Island, Taiyang goes looking for Raven at the barn (house?) where Yang went looking for her as a child. First he immediately asks how his daughters are doing, eventually he challenges her to grow up, and finally he invites her to come see him at his house when she\u2019s done sulking.<br /> <br /> After Taiyang feels he\u2019s done what he can to convince Raven to grow up, he has her teleport him to Yang or Qrow, and we get to see Taiyang fight. Probably against Hazel, where Taiyang can demonstrate the wisdom of \u201csometimes the best path is around the obstacle rather than through it\u201d.<br /> <br /> If Raven stays behind, as she likely will, we get to see her walking around Taiyang\u2019s house, looking through his things. Also, Yang\u2019s, Qrow\u2019s, Summer\u2019s, and Ruby\u2019s things, and possibly ends at Summer\u2019s cenotaph. Then she might teleport to Taiyang and rescue him from something. This may or may not lead to her death at Cinder\u2019s hands.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm basically 100% sure the series will end where it began: in Vale. Full circle. Oh, there may be some sort of final confrontation at Salem's evil lair, but the last arc is gonna be back in Vale. </div> </div> </div>Of course. The Academy that has already fallen. The Relic Crown of Choice that remains hidden and locked away somewhere on its grounds. The end-game, final-disc boss Wyvern monster waiting on the remains of Beacon Tower.<br /> <br /> A monster that might be a Boss-Rush type boss, with its spawning ability. A great way for Rooster Teeth to really go all out and have our heroes cut their way through a series of the story's best and most interesting Grimm.<br /> <br /> Beacon Academy is the most logical place for our heroes to finally go on the offensive. Right now, and probably until then, our heroes have been on the defensive, never knowing where to attack in order to strike a blow against their enemies. Beacon is the only place we know where they can attack to achieve an objective, whether to take Beacon back or just to retrieve the Relic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have a lot more hope for season 7 than I did for 5. We got a more complete picture of Argus and its people in four, five episodes there than we got of Mistral in over a season there. I'm hoping Atlas is more than Mistral was, because Mistral was &quot;one house, a deserted academy, and ten minutes of Qrow wandering alleys.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I won't say 5 was terrible, but it did disappoint. Volume 6 has also given me plenty of hope for Volume 7.<br /> <br /> Obviously, judging by that massive post above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T22:15:23-08:00","id":1286363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1286285#post1286285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Some posters over at SpaceBattles absolutely hate the idea that our teenage heroes might be forced to enroll at Atlas, but they don't offer any explanation for how Ironwood can get them out of trouble for stealing the airplane, or how they can avoid Ironwood making some effort to keep them under control when they cannot escape his control within his kingdom and still cooperate with him against their enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this is all contingent on what the writers want to happen, because there's a <i>lot</i> of leeway here.<br /> <br /> Your scenario is absolutely plausible and believable. However, if the writers don't want to go that way, it is also plausible and believable for Ironwood to cover everything up.<br /> <br /> Right now, literally the only people who know that Manta 5-1 was stolen are the people manning Argus Base, and the only person there who knows FOR SURE who it was is Cordovin. Remember, comms can't reach from Anima to Solitas anymore. It is entirely possible that Qrow has Jimmy Jims personal private priority line on speed-dial and is pulling out his scroll the second the camera was off him at the end of the season (if Atlas ATC can communicate with them to say welcome home, that means they're within local tower range of Atlas) and is having a quiet word with him. Ironwood has them cleared to his private landing pad, and has the ship sent back to Argus with regular troops who deliver a sealed confidential pouch to Cordovin: &quot;You did good letting them take the ship. As far as anyone else is concerned Manta 5-1 was dispatched to Atlas to return Weiss Schnee. Your records already reflect that; if they reflect ANYTHING else, or your men believe anything else happened, kindly correct that.&quot;<br /> <br /> I am not saying this <i>will</i> happen. I'm saying if it <i>did</i> happen, it would be plausible. Ironwood might place more value in keeping this all very quiet and very off-book and minimizing everyones exposure. He might not <i>want</i> to have a big public brouhaha. Especially since as things stand now, the Ozluminati conspiracy is in shambles and Team RWBY and Team JN_R represent teams of assets who are flexible, deniable, and already fully briefed, which means he doesn't have to risk widening the circle of those in the know.<br /> <br /> There are also a lot of middle-ground scenarios. What happens is going to be contingent on how much freedom they want the characters have and what conflicts and stories they want to tell. Maybe they don't give a shit about Academy stories anymore and have no interest in making Ironwood a giant pain in the ass for our heroes.<br /> <br /> Or maybe you're absolutely right and they do.<br /> <br /> Both are super plausible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dude is going to run a tight ship, and likely has a poor opinion of Team RWBY and JNPR's discipline. </div> </div> </div>???<br /> <br /> Ironwood's one interaction with Ruby Rose was overwhelmingly positive and featured him complimenting her take-no-prisoners full-speed-ahead approach to Huntressing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T23:53:02-08:00","id":1286371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1286363#post1286363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your scenario is absolutely plausible and believable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. It's nice to have someone with a different opinion say so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is entirely possible that Qrow has Jimmy Jims personal private priority line on speed-dial and is pulling out his scroll the second the camera was off him at the end of the season (if Atlas ATC can communicate with them to say welcome home, that means they're within local tower range of Atlas) and is having a quiet word with him. Ironwood has them cleared to his private landing pad </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Finally, someone offers a plausible and believable rebuttal to my scenario instead of expressing a purely emotional &quot;I don't like that, I don't want that to happen&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ironwood might place more value in keeping this all very quiet and very off-book and minimizing everyones exposure. He might not <i>want</i> to have a big public brouhaha. </div> </div> </div>I'm sure he'd love to avoid one, but I was operating on the premise that keeping things so quiet was impossible. That the only option he had was damage control.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Especially since as things stand now, the Ozluminati conspiracy is in shambles and Team RWBY and Team JN_R represent teams of assets who are flexible, deniable, and already fully briefed, which means he doesn't have to risk widening the circle of those in the know. </div> </div> </div>That's a good point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe they don't give a shit about Academy stories anymore </div> </div> </div>I could argue that they stopped giving a shit about those as soon as Blake's arc in the first Volume, where she runs away from school (on a weekend, but still) to avoid consequences and then decides to become a vigilante. The next major story arc is about Blake leading her team into becoming vigilantes with her, as they wait for classes to end to go investigate more crimes.<br /> <br /> For all that they were in school, very little of the story actually involved school. NARUTO had more emphasis on being in school, with students actually having training arcs to learn skills from their teachers, and he had graduated from his academy at the beginning of his story.<br /> <br /> But my point is, if our heroes could be in school and still run around saving the world in their free time, they could do it again. Except this time, they're more eager to leave school and aren't happy to return when they're done for the day, because it's no longer a home away from home, but a juvie prison.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and have no interest in making Ironwood a giant pain in the ass for our heroes. </div> </div> </div>This is one of those highly variable things that can go whichever way the writers want, depending on how many other obstacles they want to put before our heroes.<br /> <br /> Can Ozpin get Ironwood to see reason? Will Ozpin even bother to appear after Ironwood learns the truth about Salem? Do our heroes hide the truth about Salem in the hopes that Ozpin will finally reappear, or does Yang still distrust him so much that she'd rather risk Ironwood going off the rails than ever give Ozpin breathing space?<br /> <br /> Is it less that Ironwood is being unreasonable and more that there are serious threats within Atlas that he's trying to deal with, and he's happy to do whatever our heroes want as long as they can help him out?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ???<br /> <br /> Ironwood's one interaction with Ruby Rose was overwhelmingly positive and featured him complimenting her take-no-prisoners full-speed-ahead approach to Huntressing. </div> </div> </div>His interaction with Yang after she broke Mercury's leg on global television was much more strained. He was sympathetic to her stress-induced hallucination (as he understood it), but not her dramatic reaction.<br /> <br /> And appreciating Ruby's spirit and initiative is different from admiring her self-control. In any case, it's less about Ruby as a person and more about anything he might remember about Yang and Weiss' embarassing performance against Flynt and Neon, and Team JNPR's embarassing moments against Team BRNZ. All of which should be easily available footage for him to review to refresh his memories of what all of these teenagers are like before he passes a legal judgment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T21:14:46-08:00","id":1286970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1286371#post1286371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His interaction with Yang after she broke Mercury's leg on global television was much more strained. He was sympathetic to her stress-induced hallucination (as he understood it), but not her dramatic reaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a long time since I saw that scene, so I might have to go back to refresh my memory, but I thought his response was more &quot;yes, I can tell something is up, but it doesn't matter. The big picture is more important, and that means we have to deal with what people saw.&quot; (The big picture in this case being the risk of a catastrophic trust cascade failure leading to a massive Grimm invasion.)<br /> <br /> And in retrospect he <i>wasn't wrong</i>. Yang got a raw deal, but she was still acting like a spoiled child and failing to see what was really at stake (ie. a lot more than her personal reputation.) Ironwood was basically telling her that he could tell something was up and that if she took the fall now in order to limit the potentially-catastrophic damage resulting from what happened, he'd make it good in the long term. And while later events made the damage to her reputation mostly immaterial, he did pay her back - he's the reason she has an arm, remember. That gift shows that he knows who she is and, despite her immaturity at the time, he did respect what she did.<br /> <br /> I think he might still be concerned that she's a bit immature (and he was totally right, Yang <i>was</i> immature and reckless back then), but he'd probably be open to the idea that she's grown.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ...all that aside, though, while I think having them enroll in Atlas would be fun (I thought the &quot;Harry Potter&quot; school scenes were the best parts of the show), I don't think it's in the cards, since it would feel like slowing things down and lowering the stakes, and the writers seem to be aiming more for escalation. Besides, there's already a ton of stuff to address in Atlas without also adding extensive school subplots in the academy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have a lot more hope for season 7 than I did for 5. We got a more complete picture of Argus and its people in four, five episodes there than we got of Mistral in over a season there. I'm hoping Atlas is more than Mistral was, because Mistral was &quot;one house, a deserted academy, and ten minutes of Qrow wandering alleys.&quot; </div> </div> </div>The issue was that Season 5 split its focus across a bunch of plot threads. Between glimpses of Atlas, Raven's bandit camp, and the entire Menagerie plotline, we didn't actually get much time at Mistral.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T08:47:12-08:00","id":1287063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1286970#post1286970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a long time since I saw that scene, so I might have to go back to refresh my memory, but I thought his response was more &quot;yes, I can tell something is up, but it doesn't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't jive with him talking about stress-induced hallucinations or his own experience with how those can happen even after the battle is over, and he's rubbing his robot arm as he says this.<br /> <br /> Something really bad messed Ironwood up savagely in the past. Probably the thing that cost him half his body. The man is incredible for getting back in the saddle after being crippled so badly, but that doesn't mean he's ever completely recovered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yang got a raw deal, but she was still acting like a spoiled child and failing to see what was really at stake (ie. a lot more than her personal reputation.) </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Weiss was making similar mistakes after her father took her back to Atlas, what with summoning the boar at the party and then going off on her father when he held all of the cards.<br /> <br /> Neither one are to blame for their irrational states of mind. Yang had just been horribly set up and Weiss was in an abusive environment. Neither should their teenage lack of perspective be treated as a personal failing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...all that aside, though, while I think having them enroll in Atlas would be fun (I thought the &quot;Harry Potter&quot; school scenes were the best parts of the show), I don't think it's in the cards, since it would feel like slowing things down and lowering the stakes, and the writers seem to be aiming more for escalation. Besides, there's already a ton of stuff to address in Atlas without also adding extensive school subplots in the academy. </div> </div> </div>I never specified any extensive school subplots.<br /> <br /> I offered the possibility that Penny might be back, but she doesn't remember Ruby, and Ciel Soleil is preventing Ruby from interacting with Penny, as well as also being a general pain in the ass for the other heroes. Also that Flynt and Neon might be giving Yang and Blake tips on how to handle an interracial relationship in the Kingdom of Atlas.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I didn't see much happening on-screen in the school itself at all, save for maybe an exposition scene where a professor introduces some background and a plot point. Flynt and Neon would actually serve to get at least some of our heroes OUT of the school and into the city. Even the Penny subplot would lead away from the school and into the secret mad scientist labs of Dr. Polendina.<br /> <br /> For the most part, I saw enrolling our heroes in Atlas Academy as a way to create tension and pressure within the cast and audience. &quot;How can we/they save the world when they're being forced to go to school?&quot; But beyond that, and the two possible subplots I mentioned, Atlas Academy would just be a way to justify our heroes getting stronger off-screen.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, I just remembered another subplot. It is mandatory that Weiss sings on stage at another concert, with Flynt providing musical accompaniment (possibly with the rest of his team; maybe Neon is a drummer) as she sings another &quot;Fuck You, Dad&quot; song, and this time REALLY spills the tea on him in front of all of Atlas. Because what's he going to do? Double-disown her?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issue was that Season 5 split its focus across a bunch of plot threads. Between glimpses of Atlas, Raven's bandit camp, and the entire Menagerie plotline, we didn't actually get much time at Mistral. </div> </div> </div>And the time we did have at Mistral, it wouldn't have made sense to leave the house. Especially not for the super-secret discussions.<br /> <br /> Though, come to think of it, we did see a lot of Kuo Kuana. So in a sense, Volumes 4 and 5 were the Mistral AND Kuo Kuana volumes, and it makes sense that we didn't see as much of one of them as we wanted. (I mean, I wanted to see more of Kuo Kuana as well, but the parts I want to see are the parts of a kingdom we never get to see; the border defenses, the agricultural areas, and the industrial areas.)<br /> <br /> Just about the only thing we didn't get to see in Kuo Kuana that we have seen elsewhere is a school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T19:43:41-07:00","id":1295721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266310-rwby-volume-6?p=1276501#post1276501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ember Celicia are arguably bracers and not smashfists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boulders-as-Pebbles Attitude, and the general incompatibility of Lunar Strength Charms with firewand discharges, has got me thinking.<br /> <br /> What if Ember Celica is a pair of firewands, built into bracers, which are designed to work together with a punching action so much that Yang's muscle-power contributes to the power of the shots?<br /> <br /> Fire Aspect Charms prioritize Strength and Dexterity, Solar Brawlers favor Strength, and Strength-favoring Lunars would want to use their Strength Charms with projectile attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T21:26:33-07:00","id":1295737,"title":"","content":"I'd just make them artifact bracers that have a projectile attack as the first evocation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T04:03:06-07:00","id":1295751,"title":"","content":"That seems the easiest way to do it, yes. Dunno how to balance it, though there's probably not much to do. At worst it has to be a Simple evo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T07:23:10-07:00","id":1295807,"title":"","content":"That Evocation could require firedust instead of or in addition to pure motes of Essence.<br /> <br /> But you don't think that the short-range, punch-assisting explosion would be the first Evocation? You'd start with the ranged attack, and then build into the close-range attack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T18:42:01-07:00","id":1322544,"title":"","content":"vol 7 poster is out<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/newsfeed/001/510/418/ae5.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I notice they all got new outfits. Weiss's inparticular has a military look to it. Ruby has a really short skirt. And Blake looks like she cut her hair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T02:05:59-07:00","id":1322575,"title":"","content